Two companies continue to sign contracts to buy and sell more than 2,000 tons of organic rice from farming communities in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): Amru Rice and Golden Rice have signed contracts to purchase 2,200 tons of organic rice from 11 farming communities in Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, stated that the Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union was the first union established in Cambodia in April 2016 with a total of 25 community members with 5,403 farming families located in both districts. 07 of Preah Vihear Province. The vision of this Union is "Farmers in Preah Vihear Province will have a prosperous life with dignity and dignity."
By signing a contract to buy and sell organic rice from this community, Golden Rice will buy 1,200 tons of organic rice from 7 farming communities with 1,000 producers and Amru Rice will buy about organic rice. 1,000 tons from four farming communities with 500 producers, a contract to buy more than the quantity signed in June recently.
Oknha Song Saran, CEO of Amruray Cambodia, said that 2023 is the ninth year of the contract to order organic rice from the farming community in Preah Vihear province.
He pledged to make great efforts to promote and export Preah Vihear organic rice to the world market more widely and vigorously in order to make Preah Vihear rice more famous in the international arena. . However, he continued to urge all farmers to continue their loyalty to comply with the principles of the contract, especially organic standards.
Ouk Kimsan, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, said that the Royal Government in turn has been studying trade to find markets by exporting Cambodia's agricultural products to the world market and agriculture is still the backbone of economic development. Nationally, Preah Vihear is the target province of agriculture.
It should be noted that throughout Preah Vihear province, the work of cultivating rice in the rainy season of 2023 has implemented 100,059 hectares of plowed land and 100,301 hectares of land planted and planted on 99,817 hectares, equal to 100. 48%.
