Who is Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection?
(Phnom Penh): The new Council of Ministers, headed by HE Dr. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, was officially sworn in on the afternoon of August 22, 2023 under the highest presidency of the King.
On the morning of August 24, 2023, the new Council of Ministers of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly held its first plenary session under the high presidency of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Huot Hak is one of the new ministers in the new cabinet of the new government, who will be the Minister of Inspection. By 2023, Huot Hak will be 50 years old. He was born in Trapeang Kong village, Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, to a father named Huot Chhun, a mother named Yim Hong, a wife named Song Thida, and three sons and daughters.
On education, he received education and training both inside and outside the country. He graduated with a Bachelor of Laws from the Faculty of Law and Economics and a Diploma in Senior Diplomacy from the Royal School of Administration (ERA) in 2001.
In this new mandate, the Royal Government has set out to implement the first phase of the Pentagon's political programs and strategies, which continue to focus on deeper and broader reforms in order to contribute to the maintenance of achievements. The old ones that the previous generation of senior leaders have built, and the successors of this new generation are also committed to creating more new achievements.
As the new Minister, Mr. Huot Hak is determined to always remember the five working methods of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the great Khmer hero who led the country for more than 40 years: "Bath mirrors, scrubs, treatments and surgeries."
This instruction was made at the first plenary session of the new Cabinet of the 7th mandate this morning, August 24, 2023.
