Amid growing competition with the United States, China is seeking to expand its membership, with more than 40 countries queuing to join. But India, another major BRICS power, is wary of rushing to expand without wanting China to use the bloc against the United States. On the other hand, India itself is also seeking influence for itself.
The BRICS countries of Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa represent 40 percent of the world's population and a quarter of the world economy. The BRICS is a coalition of large and small economies, democracies and authoritarian states with a shared vision of finding an alternative to a Western-ruled world order that would better serve developing countries.
Leaders of the BRICS countries, including Brazil, India and China, attended the summit along with 50 other heads of state and government. Russian President Vladimir Putin, who faces international arrest warrants for war crimes in Ukraine, did not attend the summit in person, but spoke via video link.
