Kampot Kep Salt was decided by the Ministry of Commerce to register a geographical indication of goods together with two other Cambodian products: Kampot Kep Fish Sauce and Takeo Lobster on April 26, 2023 on World Intellectual Property Day.
After Kampot-Kep salt products were registered as a geographical indication in April, he noted that only about 10 groups of farmers were able to produce according to GI salt standards, as GI salt production required higher production techniques than conventional salt. At present, there are 5 groups of producers who have applied to become members of the Kampot-Kep Salt Brand Traders Association.
He said that next year, there may be more applicants for GI standard salt production, and the association will increase publicity, guidance and training for them to understand the charge book of salt production according to GI standards.
Please be informed that currently there are about 139 groups of salt producers in Kampot and Kep provinces. This year, more than 70,000 tonnes of salt was produced due to production constraints as rain began to fall in April, forcing farmers to miss harvests.
