(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Forestry Administration has continued to bring more than 100 mixed trees to plant in Stung Meanchey Primary School to contribute to making Phnom Penh a green city, especially for the environment of the entire primary school. Fresh to enhance the atmosphere for students to breathe the fresh air of the trees and to celebrate the 9th of July.
Koam Seiha, director of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration, said that the distribution of trees and seedlings for planting in the school yard at this time was also attended by teachers, students. The purpose of planting trees now is to celebrate the Tree Festival and to increase green cover in Phnom Penh as well as the school environment so that students can enjoy the fresh air.
He added that Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng provided these trees and always advised the Forestry Administration to plant trees together and to love and take care of the trees as we love and care for our children. Wood is very important for human life, animals and all kinds of biodiversity, especially it is a wind barrier, a flood barrier and brings rainwater to increase human livelihood.
On that occasion, Ms. Lao Then, Principal of Stung Meanchey Primary School, thanked the Governor of Phnom Penh through Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration for providing trees and planting them in the campus. Has provided many benefits to humans and animals, especially for students now and in the future to the next generation to know the luxury trees of Cambodia.
The director of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration added that more trees will be planted in other places because the trees can not only provide shade for students, human beings, animals, it can help reduce climate change on the planet and help eliminate toxins. In the campus as well as in Phnom Penh.
