(Phnom Penh): A total of 799 job opportunities from 10 major companies will be offered to young people, students and job seekers in the job forum and internship opportunities tomorrow, August 24, which is co-organized By the National Employment Agency (NEA) of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Labor and Vocational Training.
Students and those who are looking for a job or want to change jobs can bring a resume (CV) to apply and interview with representatives of those companies from 8:00 am to 5:00 pm in Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training compound next to IFL Institute.
Mr. Neou Sethy, Human Resources Officer of Cathay United Bank, said that the NEA Job Forum has played an important role in helping the company in the past to recruit staff because this program provides an opportunity for the company to meet directly. With you looking for a job or you want to change jobs.
He added that in the past, Cathay Bank has cooperated with the NEA several times. As a result, the bank has acquired many employees who have been working with the bank as well.
He believes that for tomorrow's forum, many students will come to apply for job interviews with the bank through NEA promotions.
190 Municipal-District Administration Implemented Sub-National Administrative Investment Fund
(Phnom Penh): From 2017 to the present, 190 municipal and district administrations throughout the country have implemented sub-national administrative investment funds. This is according to Dr. Keo Bengwat, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Finance, Sub-National Administration and the Chairman of the Secretariat of the Board of Management of the Sub-National Administrative Investment Fund (AECC).
Dr. confirmed this during the opening ceremony of the Inter-Ministerial-Institutional Consultative Workshop on the Update of Guidelines on the Annual Performance Assessment for Municipal-District Administration on August 23, 2023.
Dr. Keo Bengvath stated that the municipal administration must compete based on the annual performance evaluation policy for the municipal administration and the district administration must compete based on the annual performance evaluation policy for the district administration. As a result, 14 municipal administrations and 108 districts have won the annual performance appraisal, with a total allocation of 41,406 million riels in the state budget.
Dr. Keo Bengwat added that the Guidelines for the Annual Performance Assessment for Municipal / District Administration is an evaluation tool used by the Secretariat of the Sub-National Administrative Investment Management Board to evaluate the performance of Municipal / District Administration. Implemented from 2017 to 2023.
