(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, at the inauguration ceremony on August 23, 2023, announced the implementation of the reforms launched by former Foreign Minister Prak Sokhon.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, the reforms include:
1: Continue to strengthen the process to create new achievements of the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations, especially continue to pay attention to the training of human resources in the field of diplomacy to build strong, clean, intelligent and focused on national interests.
2: Promote the restructuring of institutions and continue to develop the necessary ministries and infrastructure, both hardware and software, such as promoting project proposals for additional construction as needed,
3: Expand the capacity of the institution by continuing to pay attention to increase the number of officers in stages and provide incentives to capable and talented individuals
4. Continue to urge the Ministry of Economy and Finance to re-implement the revision of the salaries of diplomats and staff serving in overseas missions every two years in order to be able to respond appropriately to the actual economic situation.
