National Assembly reviews request to elect a new member of the Constitutional Council to replace the late Mr. Sam Prohmna
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia, HE Dr. Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, on Wednesday morning, August 23, 2023, held a meeting to review the proposal to elect a new member of the Constitutional Council.
The National Assembly Standing Committee discussed and approved the proposal to elect a new member of the Constitutional Council to replace Mr. Sam Prohmna, a member of the Constitutional Council who passed away in the past.
The Standing Committee of the National Assembly has assigned the General Secretariat of the National Assembly to announce the selection of qualified dignitaries and report back to the Standing Committee of the National Assembly.
Please be informed that the Constitutional Council is one of the supreme bodies enshrined in the 1993 Constitution, to protect the observance of the Constitution, to interpret the Constitution and the laws passed by the National Assembly and the Senate to finalize and decide on election-related disputes. Deputies and senators.
In principle, the Constitutional Council cannot take matters into its own hands. Only the King, the President of the Senate, the President of the National Assembly, the Prime Minister, a quarter of the senators and one-tenth of the members of parliament or the courts can request to the Constitutional Council to review the constitutionality of the law.
