In fact, the university has appointed the position of managing officer on this occasion in accordance with the skills, degrees, experience and dedication of each officer. On this occasion, Mr. Houry, Dean of the Faculty of Business and Tourism Management, representing the 15 management officers, made five important commitments, including:
1. Must comply with the Law on the General Statute of Civil Servants of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Must strictly abide by the professional ethics of teachers 3. Must abide by the letter, norms and all the principles set by the National University of Battambang 4. Must abide by the internal rules of the university and follow the instructions of all leaders Hierarchy 5. Must continue to participate in the development of all university reforms in accordance with the strategic plan.
Mr. Sok Khorn urged all management officers to consider their duties as core tasks and perform them responsibly and effectively. All officials must be mindful of the common interest and the national interest. All daily activities must be carried out on a regular basis, reporting, requesting advice and participating in resolving inactive issues responsibly.
