(Indonesia): After His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet was elected by the National Assembly as the Prime Minister of Cambodia to lead the Royal Government in the 7th term, Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, announced his readiness to continue to provide strong support. Fully and closely working with Cambodia under the leadership of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet.
The Secretary-General of ASEAN expressed his confidence that under the skillful leadership of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, will continue to move towards a brighter future for the benefit of both the people and the people of ASEAN. .
The ASEAN Secretariat is ready to continue to provide full support and work closely with Cambodia and other ASEAN Member States towards achieving the ASEAN Community Vision 2025 and beyond 2025. He looks forward to welcoming His Excellency the Honorary Governor in Jakarta for the 43rd ASEAN Summit and related summits next month.
The following is the full text of ASEAN Secretary-General Dr. Kao Kim Hourn:
"I would like to extend my warmest congratulations and congratulations on the occasion of His Excellency's inauguration as the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on August 22, 2023. The election of the Prime Minister of Cambodia is a testament to the confidence that the Cambodian people have given to His Excellency's leadership in promoting Cambodia's ongoing peace, development and prosperity.
Since becoming a member of ASEAN in 1999, Cambodia has continued to make significant contributions to the ASEAN Community Agenda. Cambodia's commitment to ASEAN development and integration was most recently demonstrated by its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022, which has led the region to return to normalcy after the Kovid 19 pandemic began to decline.
Cambodia's ASEAN chairmanship is also recorded in international history. After 11 years, Timor-Leste's application for ASEAN membership has made significant progress following the adoption of the ASEAN Heads of State / Government Declaration on ASEAN Membership Application during the 40th Summit and 41 and the relevant summits in Phnom Penh, East Timor are authorized in principle as the 11th member of ASEAN.
As an observer granted by the ASEAN Heads of State / Government, Timor-Leste now has the privilege of being able to attend all ASEAN meetings, including the ASEAN Summit. This case has greatly contributed to Timor-Leste's progress in preparing to become a full member of ASEAN.
