(Phnom Penh): Before officially taking office, the Prime Minister and members of the Royal Government always take the oath of office in the presence of the King, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach and the Guardian Angel in the Royal Palace of Chaktomuk Mongkul.
The following are the oaths of the Prime Minister and members of the Royal Government who took the oath of office before His Majesty the King, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach and Tevata Reaksa Svetchot before taking office.
We, the Prime Minister and members of the Royal Government, take the oath of office in the presence of the King, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach and Tevata Reaksa Vet as follows:
In carrying out our duties and in carrying out the mission entrusted to us by the people of Cambodia, we are committed to respecting the Constitution, serving both the present and the future for the benefit of the people. People, nation and motherland of Cambodia. We swear not to exploit the national interest for our own or for our family or for our party or for our party.
We are determined to sacrifice our lives to protect both now and in the future: * Complete independence of the motherland of Cambodia * Full national sovereignty * Legal territorial integrity in the land and sea borders Cambodia existed during the period 1963 to 1969 * National unity and did not allow any division or separatism.
We are committed to maintaining neutrality and non-alignment for Cambodia, both now and in the future, and will not allow anyone who wants to interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia or to order Cambodia's national and international policy. We do not serve foreign interests and do not harm the interests of the people, the nation and the motherland of Cambodia.
We are committed to upholding, both now and in the future, a liberal, multi-party and multi-party democracy, as well as a strong respect for human rights, as enshrined in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.
We are determined to fight against all kinds of corruption, against social injustice, and to fight for national reconciliation, for national unity, for social peace and national peace, for the prosperity of the Cambodian people and for the glorious glory of the motherland of Cambodia. Worship and love of all of us.
The Central American Congress is a political body representing six countries in a region that has become a hotbed of conflict between Taipei and Beijing. The US House of Representatives on Monday approved a proposal initiated by Nicaragua to remove Taiwan from the status of permanent international observer and replace it with China.
In response to the decision, Taiwan's Foreign Ministry said in a statement on Tuesday that "dictator Daniel Ortega has volunteered to be a Chinese pawn to seize our rights in the Central American Congress." " Taiwan said the move also highlighted China's intention to undermine Central American democracy, as well as China's ambition to expand influence in the region.
In the Central American Congress, only Guatemala has formal diplomatic relations with Taiwan. The Taiwan withdrawal comes just days after Taiwan's deputy leader William Lai returned from a visit to Paraguay, during which included a brief visit to two cities. The United States is an act that has angered China.
