The meeting was chaired by Ms. Sorn Sokha, Director of the Department of Women's Affairs of Stung Treng Province and officials from various departments around the province.
Speaking on the occasion, Ms. Sorn Sokha expressed her appreciation to the Department of Women's Affairs of Stung Treng Province for its good cooperation with relevant institutions in helping to strengthen the capacity of women at the institution and at the local level to better understand the rights, opportunities and opportunities. Welcome to make decisions in both society and family society.
In the past, it has been observed that the number of women in decision-making in institutions and units in Stung Treng province has changed significantly at the provincial, municipal, district and local levels, in line with the Royal Government's policy to increase the number of women in Leadership in decision-making only makes society prosperous.
She urged authorities at all levels in Stung Treng to pay attention to and provide employment opportunities for women to participate in capacity building by supporting and encouraging them in order to promote gender equality within the institution and integrate at the grassroots level. Well.
Ms. Sorn Sokha also highlighted the achievements of the Department of Women's Affairs in the first half of the year in response to the promotion of gender equality to help women and girls in Stung Treng to have more opportunities, rights and benefits. And efficiency.
The department focuses on women's economic empowerment, health, social services and social protection, legal protection in public and political decision-making, and implementation in line with the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Women's Affairs. Provincial development plan as well.
