(Phnom Penh): During the recent fundraiser for the conservation of Khmer elephants, Ms. Khay Chenda, President of the Ayaurata Elephant Association, paid a courtesy call on Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Her Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and Her Royal Highness. Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen and other philanthropists donated money to save the district elephants in Ratanakkiri.
Ms. Khay Chenda said that this gala night raised money from philanthropists to continue the conservation of elephants.
Ms. Chenda said that from year to year, the association receives more support from philanthropists to help save the district elephant in Ratanakkiri province, which is endangered.
The money raised by the association is used for elephant conservation, breeding, tree planting to provide animal shelter, as well as other social work in indigenous areas. Each year, the Ayeyarwaddy Association spends about $ 100,000.
Currently, the Ayeyarwaddy Association has three adult elephants and one baby elephant. At the same time, the association has recently tried to breed more elephants. Through this breeding, Ms. Chenda hopes to get positive, if not yet successful, she will continue to breed until successful. The president of the association also called on all citizens to donate money to save the district elephants in Ratanakkiri.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Appoints Mr. Khuong Sreng as Representative to Inaugurate Samrong Blvd in Boeung Samrong Development Project in Prek Pnov District
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 21, 2023, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, presided over the inauguration ceremony. Officially, Samrong Blvd., which is 5,200 meters long and 30 meters wide, is in the Boeung Samrong Development Project, Samrong Kandal Village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
Samrong Boulevard has a total length of about 5.2 km, which is a concrete road and is up to 30 meters wide and 9 meters long on each side. This boulevard will be the new face as well as the main artery in the north of Phnom Penh, connecting from National Road 5 to the Third Ring Road through Borey Phum Samrong, which will facilitate most of the traffic in Prek Pnov bridge area.
Samrong Blvd. will facilitate the traffic of the people, especially the exit from National Road 5, including connecting to the Third Ring Road and the expressway to Sihanoukville as soon as possible. . Through this achievement, the developers of Borey Phum Samrong hope and believe with optimism that Samrong Blvd. will be an indispensable achievement in the goal of sustainable development north of Phnom Penh.
