Chemical reaction on fire at animal skin processing factory in Dangkor district, the authorities used water to close almost 100 cars
(Phnom Penh): A fire engulfed a factory processing animal skins, causing a fire to burn about 30% of the warehouse, which did not cause any injuries.
The above fire occurred at 10:30 pm on August 19, 2023, at the CIPEL factory, animal skin processing factory, Prey Sampor village, Sangkat Kraing Pong, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that during the operation, 24 fire trucks were deployed.
Including 17 fire trucks of Phnom Penh Capital Office using 68 trucks and 2 auxiliary vehicles from the 70th Brigade, 4 trucks using water, 1 truck of Cambodia Beer Company using 2 trucks of water. 2 cars in Nora city use 4 water trucks and 2 cars in Borey Peng Huoth Boeung Sno use 4 water trucks.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that in the case of the above fire, which is a type of galvanized steel structure (size 15 meters by 25 meters), the fire destroyed the warehouse about 30% and will not cause the fire to spread to nearby houses. Left side.
