Washington has approved its allies Denmark and the Netherlands to send F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine for use in defending against Russian aggression, a US official said on Thursday. Once the Ukrainian pilots are trained. In ASEAN, which country has the most migrant workers?
(Phnom Penh): The International Organization for Migration (IOM) recently released its 2022 World Migration Report, noting that there are four countries in ASEAN that send the largest number of migrant workers. The Philippines, Indonesia and Burma or Myanmar and Vietnam and other countries sent more than 1 million people.
The international organization estimates that there are more than 6.1 million Filipino migrant workers, followed by Indonesia with nearly 5 million and Myanmar or Burma with more than 3.7 million. There are more than 3.4 million Vietnamese migrant workers in Laos, compared to more than 1.3 million in Laos. Thailand, meanwhile, has more than 1.1 million migrant workers, while Malaysia and Singapore alone have the smallest number at less than 1 million.
In the world, the country with the largest number of migrant workers is India, with more than 18 million people traveling abroad in search of work, followed by Mexico, China and Russia. In Cambodia, more than 1.3 million people are working in Thailand, South Korea, Japan and other developed countries, and more than 1 billion deposits a year flow into the country to supplement their livelihoods. National economy.
The International Organization for Migration (IOM) emphasizes that all citizens have the right to choose the workplace of their choice, and the search for employment, mostly to developed countries, is a high-income opportunity. Vocational skills in the new workplace and it is a contribution to support local economic activities and social development.
Please note that the story of workers in Cambodia has become a political story in Cambodia, which the opposition or some critics have used as an excuse to attack and pollute society. However, from the above figures, we see that the problem of migrant workers is a global issue, not a separate issue of Cambodia, because the number of Cambodian migrant workers is very small compared to neighboring countries and compared with The international community is still very small.
