On the morning of Sunday, August 20, 2023, he participated in the consultation between the ASEAN Economic Ministers and the 19th EU Trade Commissioner in Samara, Indonesia. At the meeting, the ASEAN Secretary-General highlighted the strengthening of cooperation in areas of common priority, such as digital trade, green technology and supply chain resilience.
Earlier in the day, ASEAN Secretary-General Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the 12th ASEAN-Canada Economic Ministers' Consultation. He stressed the need to strengthen economic ties between ASEAN and Canada, including through negotiations for an ASEAN-Canada Free Trade Agreement.
On the afternoon of August 20, Mr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Ms. Mary Ng, Minister for the Promotion of International Trade and Economic Development of Canada. On that occasion, the two sides welcomed the economic cooperation between ASEAN and Canada and agreed to work closely together to strengthen ASEAN-Canada relations.
Later in the day, the ASEAN Secretary-General, representing the 10 ASEAN member states, signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the Expansion of Cooperation between ASEAN and the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO), another important milestone in Long-standing cooperation between ASEAN and WIPO.
Afterwards, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn participated in the third ASEAN Economic Ministers' Consultation with the United Kingdom. The meeting discussed the progress of the implementation of economic cooperation activities under the ASEAN-UK Work Plan and potential areas for future economic cooperation, including digital transformation and green change.
On the afternoon of August 20, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, participated in the 7th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Consultation with the Representative of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. The two sides welcomed the completion of the first protocol to amend the ASEAN-Hong Kong Free Trade Agreement and look forward to the signing of the protocol soon.
