Woman giving birth on the street was rescued by authorities and midwives at Rovieng District Health Center, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): A woman who had a miscarriage on the street was rescued in time by the district and commune authorities and the midwives of the health center. The incident happened at around 9:00 pm on August 19, 2023 in Rattanak commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, said this morning, August 20, 2023, that before the incident at about 8:00 pm, the woman's family was sent to the health center to give birth. After traveling about 1 km from the house, the woman began to have severe abdominal pain and gave birth.
After receiving information from the people that there was a case of a woman giving birth on the street, he also instructed a deputy district governor to check and bring an ambulance and a midwife to rescue and transport to the health center until now. Both mother and newborn son are in good health under the care of a midwife.
Mr. Hor Bun Hour said that the woman who gave birth on the street was 28-year-old Chhoeun Krech, who lives in Ker village, Rattanak commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province. How.
He said that the case of this woman had labor pains on the street was caused by negligence, not following the doctor's instructions, because when we went for a monthly pregnancy test before giving birth, the doctor told us the correct date. Clear delivery.
The district governor also called on families with members to give birth to follow the doctor's instructions, especially to send the woman to the hospital or health center before delivery. Yes, until severe abdominal pain must be delivered before the delivery, which can affect the health of mother and child or can affect the life can be said.
