(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 19, 2023, the General Commission of the National Police held a press conference to present more detailed operations to crack down on armed criminals who raided to free a drug lord in Siem Reap province, which carries a 52-year sentence related to large-scale drug trafficking, and orders further trafficking from prison.
General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, confirmed through a press conference that so far seven criminals have been arrested, including six Cambodian-Americans (holding US passports) and Chinese-American (holding an American passport). They are hired criminals to act.
On the day of the incident on August 17, 2023, there were four criminals who went directly to the dental clinic in Siem Reap when the prison guards sent them for dental treatment, which had been treated in prison but did not recover. In addition to the four criminals who acted directly, they also have two other aid groups to be ready to intervene in the event of a clash with law enforcement.
General Mak Chito described that immediately after the incident, following the strict orders of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, all the police forces worked together to identify the target they fled from Siem Reap. Come to Phnom Penh to hide temporarily.
In the middle of the night on August 18, 2023, the National Police General Force determined the location where the criminals were hiding and arrested seven people on the night of August 18. Separately, for the mastermind, the convict fled abroad.
At the same time, General Mak Chito stressed that the Cambodian authorities know the location of the country where the mastermind fled and are working closely with neighboring countries to arrest and bring him back. The strictest legal convictions cannot be waived. The border police are also cooperating to investigate further, he said.
Separately, to the question of whether this case can be given from the inside? General Mak Chito asserted that as a law enforcement officer, the task force would investigate the matter in order to put an end to all suspicions raised in the event that any level of involvement was found to be in accordance with the law. No.
Responding to the suggestion that this incident may have been due to a loophole in the prison guards? The Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police acknowledged that this could be said to be a loophole for the authorities, because in the past, Cambodia has never had a case of gunmen coming to free prisoners like this.
General Mak Chito added that prison guards when carrying the drug lord to the dental clinic also had the same weapon, but a long weapon in the car. But at that time, if the prison guards had a gun in their hand, there would have been a clash with the criminals, and more precisely, there would have been injuries or even deaths.
Earlier, General Mak Chito claimed that the National Police Force and prison guards would pay more attention when sending detainees to any destination to prevent and prevent such crimes. Never again.
