The summit between Biden and the leaders of the two major US allies in Asia, South Korean President Yoon Soo-yul and Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida - was held on vacation. US President Camp David's goal is to try to show solidarity between the three countries in the face of China's rise to power and the threat of North Korea's nuclear weapons.
In the joint statement of the summit, the United States, South Korea and Japan expressed their commitment to consult with each other during various crises and work together to respond to challenges, provocative actions and threats that affect interests. Overall.
