The 100 Nights team welcomes and appreciates the positive progress in Cambodia-EU relations during difficult times.
(Phnom Penh): The 100 Nights Working Group issued a statement welcoming and appreciating the positive progress in relations between Cambodia and the European Union (EU) during these difficult times, which have been marred by global complexity and impact. Sequence of 19 Kovid epidemics.
In its statement, the 100 Nights Working Group said that strengthening the partnership between the EU and Cambodia, especially in the context of becoming Cambodia's largest trading partner and an important ally and development partner. It is a testament to the long-term cooperation that has evolved since the post-Civil War era.
The recent exchange of remarks between Cambodian Foreign Minister Prak Sokhon and outgoing EU Ambassador to Cambodia Carmen MORENO highlights significant progress in bilateral relations. Minister Prak Sokhon praised the attention of Ambassador Carmen MORENO, who has played an important role in strengthening relations between Cambodia and the European Union, leading to the improvement of both units.
Initiatives that extend infrastructure rehabilitation, agricultural development, resource management, human resource development, and demining have contributed to Cambodia's socio-economic growth. The recognition of Cambodia's role as chair of ASEAN in 2022, coupled with the successful ASEAN-EU Summit, confirms the positive development of cooperation between the two sides.
The 100 Nights working group expects the incoming government of the seventh mandate to foster an environment conducive to fruitful economic relations and constructive participation.
