Business Regulators and ACLEDA Business Institute Partnership to Strengthen Cooperation in the Field of Public Administration in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Regulatory Authority for Public Administration (GDT) and the ACLEDA Institute of Commerce on August 18, 2023 signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in Awareness and Development. Human resources in the field of public administration in Cambodia.
The signing ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sok Dara, Director General of Public Administration and Dr. Phon Narin, Director of ACLEDA Business Institute at ACLEDA Business Institute.
The signing of this Memorandum of Understanding aims to increase the understanding and dissemination of the field of public administration to the students of ACLEDA Business Institute as a whole, as well as to provide support for the development of human resources in the field of public administration in Cambodia. Well.
The MoU signing ceremony was attended by senior representatives of regulators and subordinate units, Non-Banking Financial Services Authority, management and professional officers of the regulatory administration, management, professors and students of ACLEDA Business Institute, company representatives. The executive branch provides security services or storage services and appraisal companies in the field of public administration.
The event was also attended by Mr. Rin Ratha, Deputy Director of the Civil Registry Registration Department.
Ministry of Labor Organizes Examination for New Civil Servants for 2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has opened the "A" framework for the selection of new civil servants for 2023, with a total of 891 candidates competing, with the Ministry recruiting only 20 new civil servants.
The competition for civil servants within the framework of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training for 2023 was held at Preah Kosamak Polytechnic Institute on the morning of August 18, 2023 on nine different majors: Administration, Law, Information Management. Economics, Literature, Foreign Languages, Banking and Finance, International Relations and Accounting.
Regarding the Civil Servants Recruitment Examination of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training 2023, it is divided into two disciplines: general knowledge related to the field of employment and vocational training with a duration of 2 hours and 1 English language. 30 minutes.
The exam was co-organized by the Ministry of Public Works and monitored by the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU).
