Duke Kouch Mengly incorporates "Bokator" in part-time curriculum to help promote Khmer intangible cultural heritage and give Cambodian children more knowledge of this martial art
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly, Honorary President of the Cambodian Bokator Federation, has decided to include "Bokator" as a sport in a part-time curriculum to help promote Khmer intangible cultural heritage and teach Khmer children martial arts. This is more.
According to Duke Dr. Kouch Mengly, "Bokator" is a sport that he will include in his part-time curriculum for his educational institution, as it is the only Khmer traditional martial art recognized worldwide. As the Honorary President of the Cambodian Bokator Federation, he really wants to see more Khmer martial arts.
Addressing the official inauguration of the new branch of AII Language Center and American Intercontinental School, Sen Sok Branch on August 18, 2023, Founder, Chairman and CEO of Mengly JSC. Kouch Education expressed the hope that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, which is the staff of the Royal Government led by HE Dr. Hun Manet for the new mandate, will make efforts to include "bokator" in the state curriculum.
The duke also expressed his vision that he would create a wide range of sports at his private educational institution, including football, volleyball, taekwondo, swimming and a gym, because sports are linked to education. When people play sports and get the right education, they do not have time to commit atrocities.
Please be informed that "Bokator" is a traditional Khmer martial art that is deeply rooted in Cambodian society for centuries and continues to survive in Cambodian society until today.
The carvings on the walls of Angkorian temples are clear evidence of this martial art practice. The training of bokator from generation to generation is to strengthen the wisdom and ability to defend themselves from wild animals and enemies, as well as to protect the society and the motherland.
