In the first half of 2023, the entire insurance sector received $ 177 million in premiums
(Phnom Penh): Experts in the insurance sector in Cambodia say that the insurance sector in 2023 will continue to maintain positive growth despite the uncertainty of the global economy, especially before and after the election in Cambodia, premium growth Insurance has risen significantly.
Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, said at the official launch of Forte Lay Group's "Group Medbrow" and Group Medpro Plus "insurance products on August 18, 2023. In 2023, gross insurance premiums for the entire insurance business will receive $ 177 million.
He noted that the size of the Cambodian insurance market is growing rapidly and has great potential for future development, while in 2022, the total gross premium will increase to about 332 million US dollars, an increase of more than 10% over the same period. The same in 2021.
Mr. Youk Chamroeunrith, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Forte Insurance Company, said that before and after the election, the insurance sector did not seem to change much, there was a significant increase because people have confidence in maintaining peace. The insurance sector in Cambodia continues to maintain positive growth, while in neighboring Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam, the life insurance sector fell by about 50%.
He added that for the first half of this year, Forte's premium increase was $ 35 million, an increase of more than 10% compared to the same period last year. As for life insurance compensation, in the first half of 2023, the company paid about 600 people, an average of 3 people per day, a total of about 13 million US dollars, which is equivalent to 18% of the total construction cost. In the field of total life insurance in Cambodia.
"Our life insurance for July, the election month, is higher than June, and this August is higher than July," he said. "Firstly, because we focus on people in remote areas due to good agriculture, they have good insurance results, and recently we are releasing more products because new products will help grow the insurance sector."
He said that the global economic crisis and inflation are major challenges for the insurance sector in Cambodia, however, he remains optimistic about the insurance sector in Cambodia to continue to grow through the introduction of new products. In fact, today he just launched another new product, "Med Medpro" and Med Medpro Plus, which he believes this new product will drive the growth of the insurance industry even better.
Mr. Chiep Sopheak, Managing Director of Forte Life Life Distribution Insurance, said that Cambodians should have insurance to cover their financial risks, despite the existence of the Social Security Administration, to improve the management of medical expenses. Enough and complete. He said that in general, the cost of insurance should be between 5% to 20% of its monthly income.
According to the Director General of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator, there are currently a total of 40 insurance companies in Cambodia, of which 14 are life insurance companies. Burn 128 kg of drugs in Siem Reap
