(Phnom Penh): On August 17, 2023, the NGO announced its support for the Ministry of Economy and Finance's directive on the implementation of value-added tax on imported cigarettes, requiring business owners to import or distribute cigarettes. Continuing to import all cigarettes applies value-added and has proposed an additional tax of 500 riels per pack of cigarettes to reduce the number of deaths due to smoking in Cambodia.
According to research by the World Health Organization, if Cambodia imposes an additional tax of 500 riel on a pack of cigarettes, it will lead to a 15% increase in cigarette prices, reduce 30,000 smokers next year, prevent 10 deaths Over the next 10 to 15 years, the state tax revenue increased by more than US $ 53 million per year.
In Cambodia, 15,000 people die each year from diseases caused by tobacco use, and 33% of all deaths occur in the lowest-income population.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Economy and Finance on July 25, 2023 issued a directive on the implementation of VAT on imported cigarettes with the aim of strengthening the implementation of VAT to be transparent and consistent with the Ministry of Economy. And Finance also advises all business owners who engage in the business of importing cigarettes or distributing all imported cigarettes on the procedures for applying VAT as follows:
1. For cigarettes imported for domestic sales purposes, the enterprise shall apply VAT like other taxed import goods by collecting VAT at the rate of 10 (ten) percent for all cigarette supply in Cambodia. Value added tax paid at the time of importation or domestic purchase is allowed as a credit tax on inputs for deduction with VAT on exports.
2. For cigarettes imported for export purposes, the enterprise is allowed to pay VAT only once at the time of importation, as in the past.
