(Siem Reap): 1,200 mixed trees and 400 square meters of grass were planted on half a hectare of land in front of Angkor Wat temple near Srah Trapeang Ses under the leadership of Mr. Hang Pov, Director General and Deputy Director General. The director of the department, the deputy director and about 500 staff members of the department under the APSARA Authority planted 1,200 saplings and 400 square meters of grass in front of Angkor Wat near Trapeang Ses pond.
Mr. Hang Pov said that after the establishment of the Department of Water and Forestry Management in 2004, the department has made plans to make the Angkor resort area more trees. In the past 19 years, a total of 2 million trees have been planted in the Angkor area, not including the distribution of seedlings to public and private institutions.
He added that in 2022 and 2023, after the decision of the Royal Government to reorganize in the Angkor area to address the impact of the cultural landscape and global values of Angkor, the APSARA Authority has the opportunity to increase Maintain and enhance the Angkor resort area. From the end of 2022 to the present, more than 47,000 hybrid seedlings have been rapidly planted on vacant land around Angkor.
He added that the re-planting of grass and seedlings is the best location in front of Angkor, because this is where the APSARA Authority has prepared a building for the bridge. Drying and other uses.
