Thai Chamber of Commerce delegation visits Cambodia to seek investment opportunities
(Phnom Penh): A group of Thai Chamber of Commerce delegates have been visiting Cambodia to seek investment opportunities. During the important visit, the delegation also paid a courtesy call and received information from Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce.
In a meeting at the Ministry of Commerce on August 15, 2023, Mr. Pan Sosak extended a warm welcome to the Thai Chamber of Commerce who came to Cambodia and especially to the Ministry of Commerce now.
"Cambodia has enjoyed strong economic growth in recent years and emerged as a high-growth economy, attracting a large number of investors from around the world, especially China, Japan, Korea, the United States, the United Kingdom and the United Kingdom," he said. ASEAN members and Thailand.
Mr. Pan Sosak welcomed the Thai Chamber of Commerce delegation to explore business opportunities in Cambodia. He said the meeting would provide a good opportunity to exchange views on mutually beneficial business and investment opportunities to promote trade and investment between the two countries.
He said that in 2022, the Thai Chamber of Commerce had already led a delegation to Cambodia, and in early 2023, the Minister led a delegation from the Ministry of Commerce to attend a workshop on trade opportunities and Invest in Cambodia in Bangkok with speakers from the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
Mr. Voratat Tantimongk added that this time, the delegation will visit Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, Koh Kong Province and Sihanoukville to learn about business opportunities, invest and find business partners. In addition, the Thai Investment Council has been cooperating well with the Council for the Development of Cambodia to assist and promote investment between the two countries.
Speaking at the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak said that Cambodia has signed bilateral free trade agreements with China, the Republic of Korea and the United Arab Emirates. This shows the potential investment opportunities for Thai businessmen to invest in Cambodia to benefit from the tax benefits provided by those agreements.
"Cambodia offers long-term growth opportunities across a wide range of sectors and is well positioned as a potential hub for business and investment in the region, taking into account key factors such as strategic location, young workforce and energy access," he said. Gained a large market through GSP as well as bilateral free trade agreements.
The Minister also said that Cambodia is ready to welcome Thai businessmen to invest in Cambodia for mutual benefit. Once again, Cambodia is committed to further strengthening and expanding friendly relations and cooperation in all fields between the two countries.
It should be noted that the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand in 2022 amounted to more than 4.6 billion US dollars, of which Cambodia exported to Thailand more than 409 million US dollars and Thailand exported to Cambodia. It is worth 3.832 million US dollars.
For the first six months of 2023, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand amounted to more than 1.9 billion US dollars.
