(Prey Veng): Buddhist supporter Ieng Sotheara, a well-known Buddhist trader and businessman in Cambodia, gave tips to doctors to guide and treat patients with quality, ethics and virtues. And ethics, combined with the right techniques, the leadership and treatment of patients, as well as the daily life of the team of doctors will get good results.
This statement was made by Mr. Ieng Sotheara on the occasion of his training as a trainer in the 4th module training course on "Management and Leadership for the 6th Generation Hospital Management Officer" on the morning of 15 August 2023.
He added that etiquette, virtue, ethics for doctors as leaders in health centers is very important, doctors must adhere to a clear profession with gestures, words, sweet, careful attention with patients, clear explanations. With beautiful words, do not scare the patient, do not be rude to the patient, if all these points are applied, the patient will respect us as a good doctor, trust and treat heart.
On the other hand, if the patient sees a gesture, the doctor speaks inappropriately, blames the patient, and makes the patient feel worse. Morality is compared to the five precepts: first, do not kill, second: stealing, third: fornication, fourth: lying, cheating, and fifth: drinking alcohol, so our doctor must practice these five points.
He went on to say that for virtue to have a deeper meaning, doctors must be pious, compassionate, compassionate, by treating patients with compassion and love, treating patients like our children, our parents and Relatives. Karuna refers to the use of quality medicine to patients. Mutita must be enthusiastic about the treatment of patients who have been cured.
At the same time, Mr. Ieng Sotheara also strongly hopes that the training courses and share experiences in the Buddhist way, which focus on morality, ethics, virtues, help the doctors who participated now know how to use and share. To those around you, gradually, the virtues, ethics, ethics of doctors, combined with modern technology and machines will help the medical team to treat all diseases better.
Cambodia-Vietnam Update on Cooperation Agreement on Standard Operating Procedures for the Identification and Repatriation of Trafficking Victims
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Expertise of Cambodia and Vietnam on August 16, 2023 updated the cooperation agreement between the two governments on the standard operating procedures for identification and repatriation of victims. Human trafficking.
He stated that this document (Standard Operating Procedures for the Identification and Repatriation of Victims of Trafficking in Persons) dates back to 2009 and has been in place for more than 13 years. That is why both sides need to update this SOP.
Mr. Nhek Vannara Trafficking in persons and exploitation of human beings have occurred and are spreading everywhere in all forms, mostly organized cross-border crimes, and this crime has affected both nationally, regionally and globally.
"It is for this reason that we have come together to hold a consultative workshop on updating the cooperation agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam," he said. "Standard operating procedures for identifying and repatriating victims of human trafficking today."
