National Minimum Wage Council issues a statement on the results of the minimum wage discussion for workers for 2024 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The National Minimum Wage Council of the third mandate on August 16, 2023 opened. Discussion on the minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags sector for 2024.
The discussion was chaired by Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training at the Ministry of Labor, but the three parties, the government, unions and employers have not yet released figures.
The meeting achieved the following results:
1: Officially announced the composition of members and vice chairmen of the National Council for the Minimum Wage for the third mandate:
* Mr. Kim Chansamnang is the Deputy Chief Representative of the Workers 'Professional Organization * Oknha Dr. Nang Sothy is the Deputy Chief Representative of the Employers' Professional Organization.
2. Presented the key statistics of the seven social and economic criteria for stakeholders as a basis for negotiating the minimum wage for 2024.
3. Hear the position of the representatives of each party on the change of social and economic criteria, but the representatives of the employers and the representatives of the workers have not been able to confirm the figures, which is their official position yet, requesting the internal meeting of More body.
4: The National Minimum Wage Council of the third mandate will hold the next meeting on the morning of August 28, the 4th, the 11th, the 18th, the 25th of September and the 2nd of October, 2023.
In 2023, the minimum wage of workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags sector will be $ 200 per month, plus any additional benefits, a worker can receive between 217 to 228 US dollars per month.
