The meeting was held on the afternoon of August 15, 2023 with the participation of members of the Environmental and Social Fund Committee from relevant institutions, units under the Ministry of Environment and the Secretariat of the Environmental and Social Fund Committee.
The final draft of the "Five-Year Policy and Vision 2023-2027 of the Environmental and Social Fund and the Five Procedures" includes:
1: Standard operating procedures for fund management and projects that use environmental and social funds 2: Financial procedures for environmental and social funds 3: Procurement procedures for environmental and social funds 4: Operational procedures for fund revenue collection Environment and Society 5: Operational procedures for monitoring and evaluating projects that use environmental and social funds.
On that occasion, the Minister emphasized the importance of the Environmental and Social Fund as a supplement to the national budget to contribute to the restoration of environmental resources, biodiversity conservation, building a modern administrative system, strengthening work efficiency, reducing poverty in local communities and planning land use. In a sustainable way, for the benefit of all Cambodians.
Samdech Sar Kheng: Democracy and Elections as a Process to Participate in Preserving the Nation, People to Survive in Dignity in Accordance with the Will of the Voters
(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Permanent Security Command for Elections, affirmed that democracy and elections are a process in which to protect the nation and its people. Dignity, richness in accordance with the will of the electorate, is not a process that destroys society due to different political views.
This is according to the press release of the meeting to review the work of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 for 2 days, organized by the National Election Committee (NEC) in Battambang province.
Despite the success of the last election, the NEC believes that summarizing and evaluating past performance is essential for better future elections.
Mr. Prach Chan added that based on the summary report of the meeting reported by Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, it was found that the meeting gathered and discussed five main topics, including:
Annual voter list and voter registration - Registration of political parties, candidates and candidates, filing, receiving and resolving complaints at all stages of the election - Campaigning and media management during the election campaign Voting, vote counting and summarizing of election results - Voter training and education.
After discussions, each group identified several strengths that need to be addressed. At the same time, the Conference also identified a number of challenges to be considered and to find appropriate solutions to ensure that future elections are better.
Two elderly and chronically ill grandmothers receive food and some donations from the Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Social Affairs
(Kampong Chhnang): On the morning of August 15, 2023, two elderly and childless grandmothers who were dependent on their neighbors and had physical illnesses received Donation of food items from the Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Kampong Chhnang Province.
One of the two grandmothers, 73-year-old Pen Lon, lives in Pring Kong village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district. She has no husband and no children. She lives with her niece in the upper commune.
She is currently suffering from high blood pressure and dementia and was taken by her niece to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital. But after receiving medical attention and care from the doctors, her condition has now improved. This was confirmed by the niece who was taking care of her grandmother in the hospital on the morning of August 15.
The other grandmother is Kim Hoy, 67 years old. She also has no children and no husband, she lives in poverty and has a physical illness. Currently, she lives alone, waiting for her house in the fourth village, Sangkat Khsam, Kampong Chhnang.
