Putin praises Russia's strategic partnership with India
In a congratulatory message to President Droupadi Murmu and Prime Minister Narendra Modi on the occasion of India's Independence Day, Russian President Vladimir Putin said Moscow was "very concerned" about the situation. A special and privileged strategic partnership with New Delhi and committed to continuing to promote such relations. This is according to the release by the Russian news agency TASS on Tuesday, August 15, 2023.
"I am confident that we will continue to promote fruitful bilateral cooperation in all fields through joint efforts as well as constructive partnerships to address regional and global issues," Putin said in the message. .
"India's achievements in the fields of economy, science, technology and society are universally recognized," Putin added. "India has gained the authority it deserves on the international stage, playing a significant and constructive role in international affairs."
Russia and India view their relationship as a "special strategic partnership and privilege." Both countries share a common interest in establishing a multi-polar world order instead of a two-pole world, with the current US-led decline in the world order.
