Jurisdiction: Illegal opposition group's propaganda that "there is an internal division within the Cambodian People's Party" is intended to provoke unrest
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian authorities are investigating those involved with a number of videos posted on social media that "there is an internal split within the Cambodian People's Party", which was manipulated by extremist opposition groups to cause social insecurity.
Some videos have been posted by opposition groups on TikTok, falsely claiming that there will be a split within the CPP after the new government is formed.
Through Fresh News, Cambodian authorities have categorically rejected such distortions and claimed that the new Royal Government is committed to preventing any unrest in order to maintain peace, stability and development in Cambodia.
The organization of a distorted propaganda campaign by extremist opposition groups with clear scenarios is one of the reasons why their groups in the country have been arrested and enforced more.
