Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over a Groundbreaking Ceremony for Citizens
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of August 14, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, was honored to award medals and prepare food to more than 100 journalists who were live reporters in Samdech's programs. .
The prestigious ceremony for the journalists was held at the Peace Palace, the Office of the Council of Ministers, where Samdech Techo often receives foreign delegations.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is considered a leader who provides high interest and value to the media. Samdech Techo considers the press as an important part of Samdech's political life.
During Samdech's political life, especially as the Prime Minister for almost 40 years, all public programs always have journalists, both national and private, following Samdech Techo.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in this evening's ceremony, he would like to thank all the journalists who overcame the difficulties and made efforts to disseminate information related to Samdech's activities.
Some of the journalists whom Samdech Techo invited to receive medals and prepare food this evening have been following Samdech Techo since the 1990s.
In the role that the unit assigned to follow the news of Samdech Techo's activities, they have many memories in their careers. In particular, they have contributed to valuable social work in their careers.
This is the first time for them to receive such a medal and prepare a meal. Recipients of the award include a driver, a speaker set-up, an electrician, an internet host, and a Japanese man.
They consider today's program a great honor and a historical record of their careers as well. They considered the day program to show the gesture of Samdech Techo as a leader who has high attention to everything around him or related to the work of Samdech, whether small or large. As Samdech always said, underestimate small work can not do big work.
Journalists expressed their happiness and considered Samdech Techo Choam an epic gesture for the leader.
