General Knowledge: Don Moeung Toei Temple, Yasothon Province, is one of the oldest Khmer temples in Thailand.
Archaeological excavations have uncovered the remains of prehistoric human remains, indicating that the site has been inhabited since prehistoric times and is associated with Khmer civilization. Both the Dvaravati civilization progressed to become a town from the Phnom Kingdom period, the Chenla period, to the Angkorian period under the rule of the Khmer dynasty.
1. Prehistoric human remains, pottery and skeletons have also been used for aerial scanning technology, and the site has been inhabited for more than 2,500 years.
2. In addition to the prehistoric excavation evidence above, they also found small and large sandstone fragments, which are the structure of the Don Moeung brick temple, some stone carvings. Not only that, next to the temple, there are some carvings.
4. A Kudu sculpture depicts the Sambor Prei Kuk style art. Kudu is a kind of sculpture on ancient Khmer temples, especially in the style of Phnom Da, in the style of Sambor Prei Kuk, in the style of Prey Kmeng, in the style of Kampong Preah, etc. More related to this Kudu sculpture).
5. Two floating temples that are separated from the temple towers, because usually the pre-Angkorian Khmer art, we like to make floating temples next to the temple towers. Most of the roofs of the floating temples are decorated with Kudu sculptures, and the Kudu above may also be detached from any of the floating temples.
7. A sandstone lion sculpture has been identified by archaeologists as a form of art, in the reign of King Rajendravarman II, the Khmer king of Angkor. The lion statue was excavated underground in front of Don Moeung Toei temple in 1991.
These archeological sites have been preserved and exhibited in the Don Moeung Toei Archaeological Museum in Kham Khoeun Keo district to this day. Indeed, of the more than 100 ancient Khmer temples in Thailand, Don Moeung Toei is considered one of the oldest Khmer temples in the country. Cam Lopp (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. notifies a former salesperson named Vy Sok Pov to come and solve the case of money theft and customer fraud
