Woman in Kratie province's Snuol district denies allegations of encroachment on ethnic land and community dam land
(Kratie): The owner of Tumnup Thpong Restaurant, located in Thpong Village, Snuol Commune, Snuol District, Kratie Province, has denied the allegations in a number of local media outlets alleging that she and her husband had encroached on Stiang land. The point where the Neak Ta hut and the land of the Spong Dam are privately owned is a baseless allegation.
The owner of the Thpong Dam restaurant and the elders who live in the area all claim that the land has been occupied since the time of her husband's ancestors, when the dam did not exist until the Khmer Rouge era. After 1979, her husband's family continued to occupy the land until today.
She added that the allegations that she and her family had encroached on the land of the indigenous people were fabricated and completely slandered because it was not true that there were relatives in their villages. Everyone knows that all of their claims are documented from the beginning to the present.
As for the allegation that the occupation of Neak Ta hut was violated, it is even exaggerated that the Neak Ta hut was built by her own husband's family to worship and pray for peace in the family, not yours. Indigenous people (Stiang). She claims that the land that she and her family manage has been operating a karaoke restaurant business for more than 14 years.
