Authorities send two criminals with more than 465 kilograms of cross-border drug trafficking to court
(Phnom Penh): The Special Forces of the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police General Commission this morning, August 14, 2023, sent two criminals with more than 465 kilograms of cross-border drug trafficking to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for Proceed in accordance with legal procedures.
The crackdown took place on August 8, 2023, and was carried out on the orders of Brigadier General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Gen. Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan. Personally, Lt. Gen. Kheung Sarath, Director of the Anti-Drug Department.
Prior to the crackdown, specialized forces researched for more than two months and launched an operation to crack down on drug traffickers crossing the border from the Golden Triangle through Laos into Cambodia at two different destinations, the first target in front of the guesthouse. In the middle of Stung Prek Chrey, along the dirt road in Prek Chrey village, Sangkat Spean Thmor, Khan Dangkor, and the second target is in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok.
Please be informed that the professional officers of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes under the leadership of Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath have worked hard to crack down on drug crimes without any fatigue, in some cases, professional forces were injured and some lost their lives. Also available.
At the same time, the director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crime is highly committed to cracking down on drug offenses across the country. In fact, in just the last week, the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on more than 1.5 tons of drugs.
In addition, according to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who urged the police to crack down on drugs from Cambodia, and with the guidance of General Sant Dr. Bandith Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner for Planning. Drug crackdown, Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath is even more determined to eradicate and crack down on drugs without hesitation.
