Russian warship warns of Black Sea cargo ship
MOSCOW (Reuters) - A Russian warship fired an automatic weapon warning warning at a dry cargo ship carrying the Palo flag on Sunday, the Russian Defense Ministry said on Sunday. Travel to Ukraine in the southwest of the Black Sea. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, August 13, 2023.
Last month, Russia pulled out of the UN-Turkey-sponsored Black Sea agreement, which ensures Ukraine can transport its agricultural products to markets through the Black Sea, and warned it would consider all ships. Who traveled to Ukrainian waters that may have been carrying weapons.
The Defense Ministry said the ship was headed for the Ukrainian port of Izmail. However, the ministry said that after the inspection team finished their work, they allowed the ship to resume.
Ukraine and the West say Russia's move is tantamount to closing Ukraine's port, threatening to cut off the flow of wheat and sunflower seeds from Ukraine to world markets.
Russia and Ukraine are the world's two largest agricultural producers and major players in the markets for wheat, corn, sunflower seeds and other cereals. Russia also controls the fertilizer market. Readers' Perspectives: Cambodia Turns New Leaders with Steel Friends China
