Joint Public-Private Sector Working Group Discusses Cambodia's Potential in Upcoming Digital Economic Agreement Negotiations
Organizing this group discussion program is part of the data collection of the research of the General Secretariat of the NCDD. To analyze the strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats for Cambodia in its readiness to participate in the negotiations, as well as to organize future digital economic cooperation.
With a diverse panel of representatives from public, private, research and business associations, each group discussed the current state of digital economy development, threats and opportunities, as well as Cambodia's readiness to engage in digital economy cooperation negotiations in particular. The ASEAN Digital Economy Agreement is scheduled to begin negotiations in 2025.
