The Ministry of Economy fined Ouk Ratha $ 3 million for a large illegal land mine in Khsach Kandal district
The fine comes after Ouk Ratha's pit failed to pay income tax to the state in the mining business with an expired mineral resource license in Pok Russey Kandal village, Pok Russey commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
The Ministry of Economy gives 30 days and if there is a delay, it will be fined 2% of the amount owed every month. Inheritance donations are prohibited, bids are suspended, investment permits are suspended, construction is suspended, and the last resort is to sue.
Please be reminded that on May 26, 2023, the Joint Working Group of the Joint Commission for the Suppression of Mineral Exploitation in Kandal Province inspected the excavation site of the above company and found that this site was exploited. The license expired in 2018, and at that time, the company manager used his accomplices to block the road for the team.
After the measurement of the inter-ministerial working group, it was found that the company dug up the land for sale without paying more than 1 million cubic meters to the state, then the working group accounted and fined according to the law.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech himself can be in the Senate for only one term, because Samdech is getting older and to give our young people the opportunity to continue their leadership.
