WANG Yi, Member of the Political Bureau and Chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, will pay an official visit to Cambodia from May 12 to 13. August 2023. The visit is at the invitation of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
According to Dr. Yong Pov, it is very interesting that Wang Yi visited Cambodia for the first time after becoming Chinese Foreign Minister again, as Cambodia will soon have a new Prime Minister, HE Dr. Hun Manet. Dr. Yong Pov said that Mr. Wang Yi may bring the invitation of HE Dr. Hun Manet to pay an official visit to China from the Chinese government after HE Dr. Hun Manet became the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In addition, Wang Yi will have separate meetings with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia. The meeting will cover a wide range of aspects of cooperation within the framework of bilateral and multilateral frameworks of mutual benefit.
