The Ukrainian navy says a new temporary "humanitarian corridor" in the Black Sea was operational on Thursday and the first ships are expected to be operational in the next few days. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on August 10, 2023.
Oleh Chelik, a spokesman for the Ukrainian navy, said the corridor would be used for merchant ships stranded in Ukraine's Black Sea port and used to transport grain and agricultural products.
"The corridor will be transparent and we will put cameras on the ship and there will be broadcasts showing that this is a purely humanitarian mission and not for military purposes," he added.
The navy said in a separate statement that the threat posed by landmines in the Black Sea and the military threat from Russia remained.
Mr. Sun Chanthol received the trust from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to join the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in 2016, which is the middle of the fifth mandate.
As the Minister of Public Works and Transport for the last seven years, Mr. Sun Chanthol has worked hard to reform and bring many achievements under his authority.
These achievements include efforts to accelerate vehicle registration and renewal of driver's licenses easily, quickly and uncomplicatedly, establishing non-ministerial service facilities at the three AEON malls in Phnom Penh, malls in Siem Reap and Preah. Sihanouk.
Mr. Sun Chanthol established the Public Works and Transport Skills Training School to develop human resources in this field. The establishment of this public and transport skills training school has received great support and admiration from Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It is also remembered that when he first came to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Sun Chanthol worked hard to build the Ministry's office building at the old location near Wat Phnom, then the new office building on Street 598, giving the Ministry of Public Works and Transport officials space. Work well, there is no such thing as no seats.
In addition to the achievements described, many other achievements, such as roads and bridges, were also built and commissioned during his tenure. Many other large projects have also been initiated but are yet to be finalized. These projects include the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway project, the Phnom Penh-Siem Reap-Siem Reap-Poipet Expressway project, and the Sihanoukville Multipurpose Port Reinforcement project to expand maritime transport.
Another special historical project that Senior Minister Sun Chanthol worked so hard to study in detail from the previous government was the Prek Chik Funan-Techo project, which connects waterways from rivers to the sea of Cambodia. This project is a project that has received high support from the Cambodian people.
For the new mandate, according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during the inauguration of the third ring road, it is said that Mr. Sun Chanthol will receive the position of Deputy Prime Minister, but will no longer lead the Ministry of Public Works.
Since taking office as Minister of Commerce in 2013 and as Minister of Public Works and Transport until today, Mr. Sun Chanthol has been a government official who has been praised by the people through his efforts in Working brings benefits to the nation and its people.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that it is a rare opportunity for him to contribute to the service of the nation and the people, and it is also a happy thing for him.
