The case was completely extinguished at 10:15 a.m. by 5 water trucks, including 3 fire trucks of Sihanoukville Provincial Police, 1 vehicle of the Provincial Gendarmerie and a vehicle of Svay Yat Port. Sihanoukville 1 unit uses 2 units of water.
China suspended imports of barley from CBH Grain, a subsidiary of the CBH Group, in late 2000 after allegations of pests were found in the goods, Reuters reported. The suspension comes during a low-level relationship between the two countries as China imposed restrictions on several Australian imports, including barley, wine, coal and lobster.
"Allowing the two companies to resume trading is the result of ongoing technical discussions between our two countries ... This is another positive step," the two ministers were quoted as saying by Reuters. "Towards the stabilization of our relationship with China."
China last Saturday ended its anti-dumping and anti-subsidy tariffs on Australian barley. According to an Australian government report last year, CBH Group will be Australia's largest grain exporter by 2022. According to Reuters.
The deflation came a day after news emerged that China had suffered its worst export decline since the first day of the epidemic, as imports fell again as domestic and global demand slowed. .
The consumer price index released by the National Bureau of Statistics fell 0.3 percent in July, the AFP news agency reported.
Although the consumer price index was better than the 0.4 percent decline forecast in a Bloomberg News survey, deflation was the first decline since. The beginning of 2021 will increase the pressure on the Chinese authorities to take additional measures to support the economy.
Deflation refers to the decline in the prices of goods and services, which is caused by a number of factors, including declining consumption.
Although cheaper goods may be beneficial to purchasing power, falling commodity prices pose a greater economic threat as consumers tend to delay purchases in the hope of further price declines. .
At that time, the lack of demand forced companies to reduce production, stop hiring or lay off employees and be willing to sell discounted goods to sell their inventory, which affected profits while costs remained the same.
China experienced short-term deflation in late 2020 and early 2021 due to falling pork prices, the most widely consumed meat in China. Before that, the last period of deflation was in 2009. According to the AFP news agency.
