(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, has prepared a development plan for the Om River area near the Independence Monument in Kampong Cham City to become another tourist area in 2024. The provincial governor said so this morning, August 10, 2023, in the 51st Ordinary Meeting of the third mandate of Kampong Cham Provincial Council.
Mr. Un Chanda confirmed that in 2024, the administration of Kampong Cham province has many development plans, especially the Tonle Oum area in Kampong Cham city, which must promote the development of this area to be beautiful by gardening and widening 2 roads. Meters on both sides from the roundabout to the Independence Monument will be replanted and street lighting will be provided.
The provincial governor said that in the area of the Om River, there must be at least 3 meters of water that can be used for boats and can be prepared to build a drainage dam, while the banks of the Om River are made of concrete in levels that can be used for recreation. Also.
Mr. Un Chanda added that currently the access road to the provincial town from Neak Poan is narrow, however, the provincial administration is committed to developing this area to have a wide entrance with beautiful streets and rivers to be more attractive. To tourists for the year 2024. Announced to take the position of Governor of Svay Teap District, Svay Rieng Province, Mr. Chea Horn replaces Mr. Men Saran, who retired
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on the morning of August 10, 2023, announced the appointment of Mr. Chea Horn, Governor of Svay Teap District, to replace Mr. Men Ran, who has reached retirement age.
The provincial governor sent some important tasks as follows:
* First, to strengthen internal unity and strengthen the working system by avoiding conflicts of interest and conflicts arising from the abuse of power.
* Second, to increase cooperation in maintaining and strengthening security, political stability, security, public order, prevention and suppression of crimes, especially drug offenses, theft and gambling.
* Third: The district board of governors must prepare a clear division of roles, duties and responsibilities within the district board of governors.
* Fourth, to strive to strengthen the implementation of the OWSO in the district and provide support for the OWSO in the commune administration to work well to improve the provision of administrative services to the people more effectively. Good governance in accordance with the procedures and procedures for providing services in new structures and functions
* Fifth: To pay attention to the management and guidance of commune clerks under the administration of the district administration to properly perform their duties and responsibilities to the people.
* Sixth, the district administration must continue to promote and enhance relations and cooperation in priority areas with the neighboring districts of neighboring countries.
Seventh, the district administration must pay more attention to solving the challenges of the people raised in the public forum, especially land disputes, must strive patiently to resolve in a transparent, fair and peaceful manner based on Conflict mitigation principles Expand resolution with efforts to prevent all kinds of new conflicts from occurring effectively
Eighth, the district administration must continue to promote and enhance relations and cooperation in priority areas with the border districts of neighboring countries.
