On that occasion, Mr. Oum Rath said that the burning of drugs seized by professional forces in the past in order to focus more attention by giving priority to the people or the basic people. In formulating policies, strategic plans, action plans and other measures related to the fight against drugs.
He stated that drugs are a kind of medicine if someone who has smoked drugs will face serious crises such as loss of money, damage to health, loss of friends, parents, health and physical damage, loss of memory, escape from school, violence. In the end, family and friends are infected with all kinds of diseases and die inevitably.
Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea reminded all citizens, civil servants, students to join and stay away from drugs, because drugs destroy the destroyer of the family, the destroyer of the whole society, anyone who intends to trade drugs, please stop being Immediately at illegal activities, if you continue to commit, you really can not escape the law.
The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Laos (SEC) jointly promote the securities sector between the two countries (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Laos on August 10, 2023 Of mutual understanding on the exchange of information and mutual assistance to promote the securities sector of the two countries.
Mr. Sou Socheat said that through the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, the two sides will help each other share knowledge and experience with each other.
He said that while Laos is preparing to issue green securities, which may be held this year or next year, Cambodia will share experiences related to the issuance of green bonds. In addition, through this MoU, in October, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia will pay a study visit to Laos to study the issuance of bonds, which Laos plans to issue in dollars, which Cambodia needs to develop this experience. The securities sector in Cambodia.
He believes that through this good cooperation, the financial sector between the two countries will have closer ties with the aim of expanding the market and attracting more investors, especially foreign investors.
He also said that in the past, Cambodia has also signed a memorandum of understanding with other countries such as Thailand, Vietnam and Malaysia to expand cooperation in the field of securities in the region, in addition to other multilateral frameworks. Deputy PM Aun Porn Moniroth Asks International Monetary Fund to Continue Supporting Technical Assistance and Training for Cambodian Officials
He also requested that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) review the framework and mechanisms for sustainable public debt management, as well as continue to provide technical assistance and training to professional officers to further develop human capital and institutional capacity building of the ministry. .
At the same time, he will continue to promote technical support to Cambodia, especially the new request of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth.
The two leaders plan to discuss a number of issues, including the AUKUS security agreement, climate change and key minerals, during the four-day visit from October 23 to 26. "My visit is an important opportunity to discuss climate change, clean energy and the common goal of a strong, secure and prosperous Indo-Pacific region," Albanis said in a statement.
The White House said in a statement on Wednesday that the visit would reaffirm the US-Australia commitment to open, stable and prosperous Indo-Pacific.
Albanis' visit comes amid growing concerns about growing Chinese influence pushing the United States and Australia closer, especially the AUKUS deal. It has just signed a deal to buy nuclear-powered submarines from the United States and contribute billions of dollars to the US shipyard.
(Phnom Penh): The man who recorded the video posted on Facebook criticized and obstructed the operation of the Anti-Drug Police Department in cracking down on drug trafficking on the night of August 7, 2023 at the corner of Street 508 and 97, Sangkat Phsar Deum Thkov, Chamkarmon district, came to clarify and publicly apologize.
With the recognition, the man who stole the video appealed to the public not to follow suit, but to allow the authorities to do their job, because our actions can affect the operation to crack down on crime.
Please be informed that on August 7, 2023, the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department (A3 + A4) cooperated with the specialized force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police under the coordination of Mr. Long Sitha, Deputy Prosecutor Phnom Penh has launched an operation to crack down on drug trafficking and illegal processing in two locations.
Location 1: In front of Jelly Lake Hotel, 7th floor, Room B711, Street 345, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. Grams and nearly 100 kilograms of chemicals.
Location 2: At the point on Street 508, corner 97, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, arrested 2 suspects, male, Khmer nationality.
During the operation, some members of the public were also videotaped, posting publicity videos about the operation, which immediately affected the crackdown, which led to the mastermind escaping.
The Anti-Drug Department would like to request the public and some media to ask permission from the professional unit before posting on social media and using the content properly according to the journalism profession.
With a commitment to cracking down on drug offenses, the Anti-Drug Department has been working day and night, despite the rain and wind, so please the public and some media outlets to think clearly and find out the truth first. Post information on other social media so as not to affect the honor of the police force who work hard.
At the same time, the Anti-Drug Department would like to thank the public for their contribution to improving the forces and providing joint information on drug offenses, which is a good spirit in implementing the "3 Do 1 Report" motto. .
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An, Leader of the Cambodian Inspection Team, Meets the Vietnamese Inspection Team to Promote the Inspection Sector More Effectively
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kitti Sangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, and Mr. Bouy Ngoc Lam, Deputy Inspector General of the Vietnamese Government Inspection, held a bilateral meeting between the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and the Inspection with the Royal Government Inspection of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam at the Ministry. In the morning of August 10, 2023.
Speaking on the occasion, His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An also warmly welcomed the inspection delegation of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam to pay an official visit to Cambodia at this time as Cambodia has just concluded the National Assembly election. The seventh mandate, in which the CPP received overwhelming support, won 120 of the 125 seats in the National Assembly.
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An also warmly congratulated the Vietnamese government on its achievements and great achievements under the leadership of the Communist Party of Vietnam under the leadership of Nguyen Fu Chong, which has made Vietnam strong in all fields. Developed industrial country and has a higher prestige on the international stage.
During the meeting, the two sides also pushed for more effective implementation in accordance with the Memorandum of Understanding between our two institutions and continue to draw on each other's experiences on inspection work, resolving grievances, defamation complaints and Prevent corruption, abuse of power and the inactivity of public power aimed at eradicating corruption.
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An also mentioned the history of cooperation between the inspection bodies of the two countries, Cambodia-Vietnam. Inspection bodies of the two countries signed the first MOU on July 19, 2005, the second on February 13, 2012, the third on November 29, 2016 and the third on May 25. May 2023.
