Fisheries Administration: A 2-month-old female dolphin died from a net in Peam village, Roka Kong I commune, Muk Kampoul district.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on August 10, 2023, as of 2022, 90 dolphins live in the Mekong River, Kratie and Stung Treng provinces of the Mekong Dolphin Management and Protection Area. Which is 180 kilometers long.
The statement added that from the beginning of 2023 until now, there have been 5 newborn dolphins and 3 dead, bringing the total number of dolphins to 92.
Please be informed that during the wet season, dolphins often move out of the canyon to catch fish for food. According to biological research, baby dolphins live with the mother and breast for about a year.
Therefore, the baby dolphins that were found dead probably moved with their masters or with other dolphins from the Upper Mekong River in Kratie and Stung Treng provinces to Kandal province and were caught dead.
The Fisheries Administration calls on fishermen along the river to help monitor and protect the dolphins, a sacred natural treasure of Cambodia and the world.
