In an interview with reporters during a visit to a collapsed road in Mondulkiri province's Oreang district, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that the two projects were national projects and were still a priority policy of the CPP-led government. Therefore, the new Royal Government continues on these two important projects.
The Funan-Techo Prek Chik project, a project to connect waterways from rivers to the sea of Cambodia, was studied and inspected by the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on May 19, 2023.
Separately, the Phnom Penh-Siem Reap-Siem Reap-Poipet Expressway reached an agreement between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the China Bridge and Road Corporation (CRBC) on June 7, 2023.
The project to build a 400-kilometer expressway connecting Phnom Penh to Siem Reap and Siem Reap to Poipet is expected to cost about $ 4 billion.
The third expressway project will pass through five provincial capitals, including Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap and Banteay Meanchey.
