Britain aims to crack down on foreign individuals and companies supplying weapons to Russia for the war in Ukraine (Video inside) (London) Russia has been accused of supplying Russia with anti-Ukrainian weapons and equipment. This is according to a quote from the AFP news agency on Wednesday, August 9, 2023.
The British government has imposed 25 new sanctions on individuals and businesses in Iran, Turkey, Belarus, Slovakia, Switzerland and the United Arab Emirates, as well as Russia. Iranian drone maker Paravar Pars and seven directors of companies already under US sanctions, as well as two Turkish-based microelectronics exporters, are among the UK sanctions targets. .
"The main goal of the sanctions is to reduce Russia's arsenal, close the supply chain and push President Putin's defense industry into trouble," said British Foreign Secretary James Cleverly. The sanctions will also bar British entities from providing services to sanctioned individuals and companies, including freezing their assets stored in the UK.
The United Kingdom, the United States and the European Union have imposed sanctions on Russia over its invasion of Ukraine since February 2022.
