Sangkat Volunteers Start Restoring and Cleaning Plants in the Siem Reap River to Improve the Beauty and Landscape
(Siem Reap): On August 9, 2023, volunteers in Sangkat in Siem Reap City began to restore and clean the plants in the Siem Reap River to enhance the beauty and scenery and attract national and international tourists. Come and enjoy more.
Mr. In Savuth, Chairman of the Working Group for Plant Restoration and Cleaning in the Siem Reap River at Wat Reach Bo Stone Bridge, said that after receiving the plan from the commune chief under the guidance of the Municipal and Provincial Unity Command, he led the people's defense force and a number of people. 22 people, divided into 2 groups, the first group had to cut the lower roots and the second group had to pull the plants that had cut the lower roots and brought them to the shore.
Mr. In Savuth continued that the restoration and cleaning of this plant is very difficult due to the deep water and the plants grow from the bottom of the river, if we clean only the top, it will not be clean for a long time, so we have to dive. Go into the water to cut to the bottom of it, then use a net to drag it near the shore and lift it to the land, this way the Siem Reap River is clean for a long time.
He added that the work of his team took time and energy, so he called on the people to participate in large numbers to enhance the beauty and scenery of Siem Reap to be more beautiful and raise the image of the people. In Siem Reap as well.
Mr. In Savuth also called on the people not to throw garbage in the river and take care of the environment together, because a clean environment is for all of us.
With this, he also called on people on social media, please criticize to build, please do not criticize just to sink, this is the words of Mr. In Savuth, the head of the team to restore and clean the plants in the Siem Reap River at Wat Reach Bo stone bridge.
