In the announcement of the Ministry of Environment, which was received by Fresh News on the afternoon of August 9, 2023, the Ministry of Environment has instructed the sub-national administrative unit, provincial environment department, community, protected area and all stakeholders to Perform the following measures:
* First, educate and guide tourists who come to visit eco-tourism destinations in protected areas, especially in all eco-tourism communities to stay away from waterfalls or waterways when it rains.
* Second: There must be staff in each area and inform tourists about the risks that may occur in the future and measures to ensure the safety of tourists.
* Third: Mark the areas that may be dangerous during heavy rains, floods and other risk areas.
* Fourth: Prepare the necessary materials and equipment for immediate rescue in the event of an accident.
The announcement came after an accident occurred at Phnom O'Mal Waterfall, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province, where water flooded a young man and woman while they were resting in a tent, causing them to fall into the water, killing two people. Two others were released.
