Bavet Mayor Wants Citizens to Participate in Public Forums to Raise Problems and Requests Local Officials for Immediate Resolution
(Svay Rieng): Speaking to many people in the public forum on the morning of August 9, 2023, Mr. Lim Seang Heng, Governor of Bavet City, confirmed that all public forums, if many people participate, the authorities will seize Citizens' requests, which are an element for the authorities to resolve in a timely and effective manner, also transparent.
He said that only local people have concerns to the authorities to help solve, so the Royal Government has set up a public forum for people to participate many times as a request and concerns to the village. The district has developed continuously under the supervision of the authorities.
At the same time, in the public forum, the people also mentioned the important points that the relevant authorities and officials involved in solving, including the problem of roads, sewers, identity cards, traffic lights in the town, garbage and road traffic.
These requests were answered and accepted by the Bavet Mayor, and on behalf of the authorities, the Mayor requested the people to cooperate with the authorities in enforcing the law.
At the same time, the mayor also asked all teachers to pay attention to cooperation and educate students to keep garbage in the bin properly, and in the future the government will delegate to the city. Administrators of kindergartens must educate young children to take care of their garbage in an orderly manner and to love the environment.
Mr. Lim Seang Heng stated that for the development work at the local level, the authorities have made efforts to build a lot of infrastructure, including concrete roads, drainage on National Road No. 1 and other roads in Bavet Sangkat, and in the future there will be drainage. Sewage and wastewater treatment tanks as well.
In connection with the people's request to put traffic lights in the town in Bavet City, the official also submitted a request to the Provincial Public Works Department to study the technology according to the people's request.
Bavet City Police Chief Em Sovanrith also asked residents to respect traffic laws and not to release animals in the open, which could eventually lead to road accidents for commuters.
He added that the owners of guesthouses and rented houses must make copies of all residents' documents to the village chief, commune chief, administrative post so that the authorities can easily work. In addition, it is necessary to cooperate with the police to identify drug trafficking suspects and local suspects involved in various thefts, which is also easy for the police to detect and arrest the perpetrators and punish them along the way. Law.
