(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce has emphasized that if the price of rice on the market rises too much, which will affect the livelihood of the people, the Ministry of Commerce will intervene by releasing the government's reserve food stocks to prevent the rise. Rice prices in the market.
According to Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, at present, the price of rice in Cambodia has increased by about 20%, while the price of rice in the market has increased by about 5%.
Speaking to Fresh News on August 8, 2023, Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that although the current price of rice is rising and pushing the price of rice in the market, but not in a favorable situation. Not to worry, this is a flow of prices depending on demand and supply.
He said that if the price of rice rises to a level that affects the livelihood of the people, the Ministry of Commerce, which has Green Trade, an enterprise in charge of managing the government's strategic food stocks, will take appropriate measures according to the price increase, but for now. It has not yet reached the implementation stage.
"We have enough food to intervene in the actual situation, as we have done in the past, such as the Kovid 19 issue, in which the Ministry of Commerce has intervened in the price of rice. I would like to inform people that there should be no "Concerned that if the price of rice rises, affecting people's livelihoods more than usual due to food shortages or related to the price increase, we may have immediate measures for this case."
He said that this factor has had both positive and negative effects on Cambodia. On the plus side, farmers who used to complain about falling rice prices will get higher prices than usual, but will hurt consumers as market prices rise and if they have a steady income they will suffer. Crisis.
However, farmers who enjoy the rising price of rice should also be prepared to feed their families, because when the harvest is sold out, it will cost a lot to buy, which will affect their livelihood in the long run. Long time no see.
He said that the Royal Government should set up a task force to monitor the food production force in Cambodia and stockpiles for use and reserve until the harvest season to avoid this food crisis because when the crisis. Rice prices are likely to rise sharply and could lead to imports of rice for supply.
