More than 102 kg of drugs and 3 suspects were cracked down by the Anti-Drug Department at 2 different locations in Sen Sok and Chamkar Mon districts
(Phnom Penh): A total of 102 kilograms, 352.27 grams of drugs and nearly 100 kilograms of chemicals with a Chinese suspect and two Cambodians were cracked down by the Anti-Drug Department at two different locations in Khan Sen Sok and Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The operation was carried out on the orders of General Santibandit, the National Police Commissioner, and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
At the same time, the Anti-Drug Department also clarified and responded to the Khmer Angkor Facebook account, News and Newspapers-Social Security Channel, which misrepresented the large-scale drug crackdown operation.
During the operation, video footage was also taken from some journalists and the public, and a public video of the operation was immediately posted, affecting the crackdown, which led to the mastermind escaping.
Please also note that in the operation, the police must use strong skills and crack down on the target to protect the safety during the operation (in the past, the police risked their lives) and leaked confidential information to make the target escape. Body.
The Anti-Drug Department would like to thank the public for their contribution to improving the forces and for providing joint information on drug offenses, which is a good spirit in implementing the "3 Do 1 Report" motto.
The suspects and exhibits are currently building a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings.
At the same time, the Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes, Lt. Gen. Kheung Sarath, is highly committed to cracking down on drug-related crimes across the country. In fact, in just the last week, the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on about 1 ton of drugs.
