Speaking at the ASEAN Day event, the Indonesian president said: "We know that the situation in Myanmar is still full of challenges. "But we also need to make it clear that this situation can only be resolved with the political will of all parties."
Widodo said the ASEAN countries must continue to work together to find a way out of the Myanmar crisis. For this year, Indonesia is the rotating chair of ASEAN and will host the ASEAN Leaders' Summit in September. Jakarta has pursued what it calls "silent diplomacy" with the Burmese military regime in an effort to push for its consent to sit at the negotiating table.
According to Widodo, ASEAN's efforts to resolve the Myanmar crisis will continue in line with the five-point agreement reached with the Myanmar military government two years ago. However, the Myanmar military government did not abide by the agreement.
ASEAN has been at odds over how to communicate with Myanmar's military government since the 2021 coup, and has banned Myanmar from attending any high-level meetings due to a lack of action. Agree on 5 points. Thailand, meanwhile, has taken a different path from ASEAN's joint efforts by holding informal talks with Myanmar's foreign minister.
