Phnom Penh Police Crack Down on 2 Criminals with More Than 58 Kilograms of Drugs
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Bureau of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police investigated and cracked down on 2 suspects and confiscated 58 kilograms of 848 grams of mixed drugs. This was confirmed by Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, to Fresh News on the afternoon of August 8, 2023.
Specialists then searched and found 10 more drugs (methamphetamine) weighing 10 kilograms hidden in the bottom of the truck to transport drugs.
Currently, the suspects and exhibits have been sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with legal proceedings.
