(Phnom Penh): In an effort to promote tourism products and packages, the Malaysian Tourism Promotion Council on August 08, 2023, in collaboration with the Cambodian Travel Agency, organized a Malaysian Tourism Workshop in Phnom Penh to gather by appointment. Cambodia-Malaysia Tourism Corporation (B2B), including a binding agreement between travel agents, hotel representatives, resorts and product owners from both countries.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents (CATA), also said that the Tourism Networking Forum is a new event to strengthen cooperation between Cambodia and Malaysia in the tourism industry. This meeting plays an important role in providing great opportunities to bring closer cooperation and understanding among tourism consumers.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin added that Malaysia has always been a Top 4 choice for Cambodians for travel for various purposes such as relaxation, honeymoon, health check and business.
On that occasion, Ms. Pot Rany, Head of Marketing of the Malaysian Tourism Promotion Council in Cambodia, said that we will encourage and support new tourism package initiatives to bring more Cambodian tourists to. Malaysia. We hope to encourage our tourism business partners to promote Malaysia Tourism with confidence to be successful in Cambodia.
