(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 8, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), met with Mr. Thongloun Sisouli, Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party and President of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, via video. .
During the meeting, Party General Secretary Thongloun Sisoulith warmly congratulated the CPP on its landslide victory in the 7th National Assembly election and praised the CPP's core role. The Cambodian people under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen are excellent and visionary guides who have received strong support from the entire Cambodian people.
At the same time, the Secretary-General also sincerely congratulated His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on the appointment of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet as the Prime Minister of Cambodia on August 7, 2023. This important historical event has the full support of the Cambodian people.
Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit expressed his strong belief and full support for the Royal Government of the 7th mandate to continue to build and develop Cambodia to be more prosperous and also committed to continue to strengthen the good relations between the ruling party. And the people of both countries.
Samdech Techo, President of the Party, sincerely thanked Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit for congratulating and fully supporting the Cambodian People's Party and the new Royal Government, which will be led by HE Dr. HUN Manet, which reflects the strong brotherhood and solidarity. And a comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership between the two countries.
Samdech Techo praised the remarkable achievements of the Lao people under the leadership of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party, led by Mr. Thongloun Sisoli, who brought continuous progress in economic development. Society has also enhanced Laos' prestige and increasingly important role in both regional and international forums.
The leaders of both parties celebrated the ASEAN Day on August 8 as all ASEAN member states are celebrating the 56th anniversary of the founding of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations. Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo also reaffirmed Cambodia's full support for Laos as the chair of ASEAN in 2024.
The two leaders stressed the importance of continuing to strengthen close ties and strong solidarity, mutual support and cooperation in all fields between the parties, the government and the people of the two countries, especially focusing on Focus on training the youth to take turns to maintain and nurture the excellent and long-lasting relationship between the two nations.
The leaders of the two parties also agreed to continue to strengthen cooperation in the multilateral framework, including the UN and ASEAN, as well as to further promote closer cooperation in the sub-regional framework, especially the three frameworks of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam. Mekong Sub-Region Cooperation, which will contribute to the strengthening of peace, stability and prosperity in the region and the world.
At the end, Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, invited Mr. Thongloun Sisouli, Secretary General of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party and other Lao leaders to visit Cambodia. At the same time, the Secretary-General also invited Samdech Techo and Cambodian leaders to visit Laos at an appropriate time.
