On the morning of Monday, August 7, 2023, in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, addressed the 2023 ASEAN Intercultural and Interfaith Dialogue. Joko Widodo, President of the Republic of Indonesia.
The conference is also attended by religious, cultural, government officials, civil society representatives of ASEAN member countries and other countries in the region.
The theme of the conference was "ASEAN Common Civilization Values: Building a Center for Harmony to Strengthen Peace, Security and Economic Prosperity."
In the afternoon of the same day, the ASEAN Secretary-General addressed the 44th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly. On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General called for stronger cooperation between ASEAN and the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly and encouraged ASEAN Member States to promote social responsibility and sustainable policy-making in ASEAN. Both national and regional levels.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized that the ASEAN Secretariat is ready to establish closer and more meaningful cooperation with the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly to better contribute to the process of building the ASEAN Community.
Afterwards, the ASEAN Secretary-General met with Lee Jang-keun, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to ASEAN. During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on preparations for the 24th ASEAN-ROK Summit in September and discussed ways to enhance closer cooperation as ASEAN and the Republic of Korea will Celebrate the 35th anniversary of the dialogue partner relationship in 2024.
