According to the latest data released by the Tourism Marketing Department of the Lao Ministry of Information, Culture and Tourism in July, the highest number of international tourists visiting Laos was from Thailand, Xinhua reported. 668,595, followed by Vietnam with 398,937 and China with 317,604.
The number of tourists increased significantly compared to the first six months of 2022, when only 42,197 foreigners visited the country on tourist visas.
Since the Lao government reopened the country for foreign travelers and the Sino-Lao railway was opened, people from other countries have flocked to the communist country.
The railway is a popular means of transportation and passes through Luang Prabang and Udomsay provinces, with many places of interest for tourists, including adventure activities.
As the China-Laos railway serves as a major tourist infrastructure, Lao authorities estimate that more than 360,000 Chinese tourists will visit Laos by 2023, up 21 percent from the previous year.
The Lao Tourism Authority and tour operators have improved services at hotels, guesthouses and restaurants, as well as added more facilities in tourist areas to provide a better and more attractive experience for tourists. According to the Xinhua news agency.
