Banteay Meanchey Military sends two suspects to court in connection with drug theft and use
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie sent two suspects to the Provincial Court on August 6, 2023 for legal action in connection with a case of theft and drug use.
The two suspects were arrested by the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie in collaboration with the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Office and the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie in the case of motorcycle theft (aggravating circumstances) and illegal drug use. At 06:40 on August 4, 2023, behind O'Ambel High School in O'Ambel Village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Yan Sovann, Commander of the Serey Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie, said that the first suspect: Yot Ratana (aka Heang or Hea), male, 24 years old, currently lives in Kbal Spean 2 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. 2. Name: Yon Tola, Male, 36 years old, currently living in Chan Kiri Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect, Yot Ratana (aka Heang or Hea), admitted that he had stolen the victim's motorcycle. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie builds a case file and sends it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of researching and cracking down on crime, said that the crackdown was coordinated by Mr. Keut Vannareth, a prosecutor at the provincial court.
The two suspects have now been sent by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau to the Provincial Court, and on Sunday afternoon, August 6, 2023, the procedure will be followed. The motorcycle was returned to the owner by the military police.
