In the Xenozoic, there is the formation and melting of ice, called the "ice age." In addition, the emergence of large, elongated mountain ranges, the birth of animals and humans, and the evolution of the continental surface as it is today, followed by the emergence of a number of mammals, such as elephants, horses, camels, grazing animals, and the growth of objects. Other.
