(Phnom Penh): The ingenuity of the Khmer people to use zero zeros dates back to before the Angkorian period, while some people in the world do not yet know this zero, such as Greek, Roman, Latin. The original does not use the number 0.
Historians refer to this door as the inscription K.127, which contains 21 lines of pre-Angkorian Khmer script, especially on the fourth line, the first zero inscription in Khmer history and regional history. It writes about the date 604 AD (604).
This inscription attracts scholars because it dates from 604 AD to 682 AD during the reign of Queen Jayaraja Devi (680-738), a queen in the Chenla period.
This proves that this zero is very old and very important in arithmetic, which proves that Khmer is good at mathematics, despite the influence of India, the use of numerical positions in the calculation of the astronomical system of The Khmer people are still the most unique people in mainland Southeast Asia.
It is considered that if there were no zeros, there would be no advanced mathematics like today. Funeral Service for Mr. Sam Prohmna, Member of the Constitutional Council
