Check out the security camera footage below: Commentary: For American politicians, taking the time to "blame them" does not equal taking time to think about how to deal with the US economy. Back
In May 2023, Fitch added the US sovereign credit rating to its list of negative monitors. The official downgrade could be seen as a sign of further despair and dissatisfaction with the continued decline in US government governance capacity.
Meanwhile, Fitch's statement indicated that the US fiscal situation in the next three years will continue to be bleak and government debt will continue to rise. This is seen as a second warning to Washington that America's "huge debt" should alert you and that the future of a debt-ridden economy is alarming.
As of July 31, the US government's debt stood at $ 32.6 trillion, equivalent to nearly one US citizen owed nearly $ 1 billion, according to the US Treasury Department. Hundreds of thousands of US dollars. Fitch predicts that by 2025, the US government debt-to-GDP ratio will reach 118.5 percent.
The third warning sign is about the US reputation, which may accelerate the "dollarization" process. The South Korean government said on Aug. 2 that to prevent turmoil in financial markets caused by the US credit rating downgrade, it would strengthen market controls.
The reason why the US dollar became an international currency depends on government credit. If the loan is damaged, you will have to reconsider. For some time now, from the world's major energy sources, such as Latin America, the Middle East and Africa, to Europe and the Asia-Pacific, which has a large US ally, more and more countries are planning to "de-dollarize." Already.
After Fitch downgraded the US credit rating, several US government officials reacted angrily and angrily. For American politicians, taking the time to "blame them" is not the same as taking time to think about how to deal with the US economy as well as restore its prestige.
Towards Cambodia's Economic Development
For more than 30 years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has paid close attention to the garment, footwear, tourism and some sectors of the construction sector due to the export momentum of these sectors and the growth of foreign direct investment. This policy has made the people prosperous and their families often happy.
The cassava sector accounts for up to 4% of the national economy, with about 100,000 families in 13 provinces growing it. Every year, the investment capital for cassava cultivation is about 300 million US dollars on more than 600,000 hectares. Most of the exports are fresh cassava and chips through the provinces bordering Cambodia and Thailand, where Cambodia earns more than $ 700 million annually.
Figures from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries show that exports of processed and unprocessed agricultural products accounted for up to 30% of total exports in the first three months of 2023.
Cambodian agribusinesses have said that in order for farmers to prosper, the development of agro-industry is essential to create added value from agriculture, participate in the national economy and generate income for farmers.
Currently, according to a World Bank study, agriculture contributes less than 10% of annual rural incomes compared to urban growth by 2020.
In the medium term, the Cambodian economy is expected to return to full potential at 6% due to the first: the export of goods and services, the second: the flow of foreign direct investment through free trade agreements. Newly approved, and thirdly, the growth of private sector investment, including the development of government infrastructure.
These are the benefits that international forecasters say that until 2025, the Cambodian economy will continue to grow at a rate of up to 6.3%, with the participation of the industrial sector, which is up to 10% compared to agriculture and Services grew by 1.5% and 6% respectively.
By 2025, the government will be able to attract foreign direct investment worth about 5 billion US dollars, which in 2022 will have a net investment of about 3,500 million US dollars. This figure indicates that the Cambodian government is likely to be able to develop a richer country to improve the lives of farmers and create jobs for all young people in the medium term.
