Former Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad, 98, has left the Cardiology Hospital after a four-day stay.
A source close to the former Malaysian prime minister revealed on Thursday that Mahathir was sent to the National Institute of Cardiology in Kuala Lumpur on Tuesday for a medical examination. He also said that Mahathir had left the hospital.
In recent years, Mahathir has suffered a number of heart problems, including at least two heart attacks and has undergone at least two cardiovascular surgeries. Mahathir was taken to hospital in December 2021 and January 2022 and spent several days there for medical check-ups.
The 98-year-old former leader is one of Malaysia's most influential political figures, having twice served as prime minister for a total of 24 years. He led Malaysia for the first time from 1981 to 2003 and returned in 2018 at the age of 92, but his coalition government collapsed in 2020 due to internal divisions.
