Their statements are inaccurate, especially in relation to local realities, which leads the Special Rapporteur to make one-sided and biased assessments.
2. The election process, in which 18 parties compete, is a clear testament to true multi-party politics and equal opportunities within the limits of the same law as other countries respecting the rule of law. Strict adherence to the election law is necessary, and non-compliance will have consequences.
4. Statements by observers confirm that the election was free, fair, transparent, peaceful, in an environmental environment and in strict accordance with the law. The independence and professionalism of election officials and institutions is properly recognized.
5. The claim that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who is expected to hand over power to the eldest son, is a completely baseless allegation, which shows the limited understanding of the Special Rapporteur or the deliberate denial in Understanding Cambodian legal procedures. The appointment of the Prime Minister must be carried out in accordance with a thorough democratic process at both the party, election and parliamentary levels.
