Understand Kanes in Cambodian society
(Phnom Penh): The National Museum of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts on August 4, 2023 published an article related to "Preah Kanes in Khmer society". In that article, it is written that Kanes is a deity in the myth of Brahmanism, which shows him in the form of a human body and the head of an elephant with a mouse as a vehicle. He is the son of Preah Iso and Princess Borvati.
He is a deity representing knowledge and avoiding obstacles as a deity who overcomes obstacles but can also create obstacles. According to the inscriptions, he has many names, such as: Kanisvor, Kanapati, Srey Kanapati, Maha Kanapati, Viknes, Kna Pati, Vikhen, Svar Vinayok, etc. Brahmins respect and honor Preah Kanes in all programs, such as starting work, traveling, building houses, writing books, and so on.
After hearing this news, Princess Borvati was very sad. Seeing this, Iso ordered the army to search for the first human or animal head they encountered, then they first encountered an elephant, cut off the head and handed it over to Iso to attach to it. Viknesvor's body. That is why Viknesvor became a konchon (elephant) called Preah Kanes since then.
