More than 780 kg of drugs smuggled through Cambodia with 6 criminals
(Phnom Penh): Special forces of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police launched an operation to crack down on more than 780 kilograms of cross-border drug trafficking criminals from the Golden Triangle through Laos-Cambodia to Taiwan, China by sea. .
The operation was carried out on the orders of Brigadier General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Gen. Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath, Director of the Anti-Drug Department. .
In a public appearance on the morning of August 4, 2023, the Anti-Drug Department said that after receiving intelligence from the DEA, the Anti-Drug Department's specialized force has been investigating for more than four months. To search for drug criminals, a group of Chinese (Taiwanese) organizations that smuggled drugs across the border from the Golden Triangle through Laos-Cambodia continued to Taiwan, China by sea.
A total of 6 suspects, male, Chinese (Taiwan) were arrested and 785 pieces of ketamine weighing 789,781 kilograms, 4 cars, 2 motorcycles, 7 mobile phones and 8 bank accounts were seized. Account.
Currently, the suspect and the above-mentioned exhibits have prepared a case file and sent it to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with the procedure.
Please be informed that the Anti-Drug Department, after Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath came to lead the work, cracked down on many major drug crimes in a row. At the same time, Lt. Gen. Kheng Sarath is highly committed to cracking down on crime like rain across the country.
