ASEAN is stepping up economic cooperation with the United Kingdom and Russia (Video inside) (Bangkok): ASEAN is stepping up talks with the United Kingdom and Russia in order to boost economic cooperation. This is according to a report by the Bangkok Post this week.
The purpose is to discuss and monitor the progress of the Economic, Trade and Investment Cooperation Plan, as well as preparations for the ASEAN-UK, ASEAN-Russia and ASEAN-Europe Economic Ministers' Meeting this August.
Duangarthit said during the ASEAN-UK Summit that the two sides reviewed the progress of the 2022-23 Cooperation Plan, focusing on strengthening economic, trade and investment ties through 11 cooperation areas, including Connecting the ASEAN-UK supply chain, opening up digital innovation markets and developing small and medium enterprises (MSMEs).
In addition, the two sides discussed projects aimed at promoting public-private partnerships, financial services and sustainable growth. The results of these discussions will be presented to the ASEAN-UK Economic Ministers for consideration this August.
Regarding the ASEAN-Russia meeting, the two sides discussed the ASEAN-Russia trade and investment cooperation plan and the ASEAN-Russia Economic Cooperation Plan and the Eurasian Economic Commission, the Bangkok Post reported.
Key activities include preparing a report on the transformation of MSMEs into digital enterprises and holding a roundtable discussion on e-commerce cooperation this month. High-level policy dialogues, senior official meetings, and workshops on digital change were also held last year.
The progress of the ASEAN-Russia Cooperation Plan will be reported at the ASEAN-Russia Economic Ministers' Meeting this month.
