Speaking on the occasion, Dr. Heng Sok Kong welcomed all leaders, delegates and young people from countries in the Asia-Pacific region to participate in the 2023 Youth Exchange Forum in Cambodia now.
He also informed about the peace and rapid development of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the vision that will turn Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030 and High-income countries by 2050.
On that occasion, Dr. Heng Sok Kong also informed about the active participation of young volunteers, including young volunteer doctors in the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia until Cambodia is successful as a country that can control Kovid disease. 19 The best in the world. In addition, Dr. provided 7 recommendations to our youth forum as follows:
* First: Engaging with local private sector organizations: Encourage Asia-Pacific Youth Exchange participants to collaborate and interact directly with local companies in Cambodia. This will give them a first-hand understanding of the role of the private sector in achieving the SDGs and opportunities for youth participation in post-Kovid-19 rehabilitation efforts.
* Second: Direct project implementation: Includes practical sessions and workshops that focus on building the capacity and skills of young people to implement projects in accordance with the SDGs. This will allow participants to apply their knowledge and learn how to plan and implement effective initiatives that contribute to sustainable development.
* Third: Facilitate cultural understanding and interconnection: Organize structured sessions that promote interaction and collaboration between young people from different countries in the Asia-Pacific region. This will allow for the exchange of ideas, sharing of best practices and building partnerships for future SDG-related projects.
* Fourth: Decision-making empowerment: Provide opportunities for young people to actively participate in decision-making processes related to sustainable development that can be achieved through group discussions, training. Or workshops that focus on youth inclusion and meaningful participation in policy making at various levels.
* Fifth: Promoting Youth Volunteering: Emphasizing the importance of youth volunteering as a powerful tool to support the achievement of the SDGs. Demonstrate successful youth-led volunteer initiatives, share inspiring stories and provide guidance on how participants can engage in volunteer activities to make a positive impact in their community.
* 6: Contribute to knowledge and research: Encourage participants to research or write articles about their experiences during the Asia-Pacific Youth Transformation. This will contribute to research on youth contribution to sustainable development with a specific focus on the SDGs. Provide publishing opportunities for outstanding work and encourage participants to share their findings and insights with a wider audience.
Finally, Dr. Heng Sok Kong requested the coordinator of the City Tour so that all young people from Asia and the Pacific could see the real progress of Cambodia under the shadow of peace and development. Wish our young people to be happy and safe when they return to their respective countries.
