Taiwan vows to tighten secrecy after military official accused of espionage
(Taipei): Taiwan's Defense Ministry has vowed to step up anti-espionage efforts after a military official was arrested on suspicion of gathering intelligence for mainland China. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, July 3, 2023.
The latest espionage case comes at a time when Taiwan's relations with mainland China are at an all-time low as Beijing has stepped up military and political pressure on the claimed island.
Taiwan's Defense Ministry on Wednesday responded to a local media report: "One soldier, one with the surname Hsieh, and the other recruited by China to gather intelligence."
"The ministry condemns a small number of individuals ... for committing this crime against the people and the country," the defense ministry said in a statement.
"In the face of Chinese communist infiltration, the military will continue to strengthen anti-intelligence education and increase security vigilance," the statement added.
