(Phnom Penh): After being the Prime Minister of Cambodia for more than 38 years, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided not to continue in office. The position of high responsibility for the destiny of the nation and the people of Cambodia will be handed over to Dr. Hun Manet, the eldest son of Samdech and elected by the Standing Committee of the Cambodian People's Party.
In the inauguration ceremony of the third ring road on the morning of August 3, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirmed that the assignment of roles to young people now to ensure the stability and development of Cambodian society. In the long run.
The decision to bring down the national heritage now is a surprise and also an event in another turning point in Cambodia's history. Samdech Techo Hun Sen began his political career as Prime Minister on January 14, 1985. For more than 38 years, as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has worked hard to solve national problems, to build national development from the ashes of war, to solve the hunger of the people.
Many great achievements have been made in Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo, such as bringing peace, national unification, boosting the national economy from the status of a poor country to a low-middle-income country, improving livelihoods and The lives of the people have improved and also raised the reputation and prestige of the Cambodian nation to the international arena again after the humiliation of a hundred years due to the crisis of war.
As the Prime Minister, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always values the well-being of the people and always communicates with people from all walks of life with the deepest emotions.
The achievements of Samdech Techo's leadership and attention to the nation and the people of Cambodia made the people feel sorry and sympathy when Samdech Techo announced his resignation as Prime Minister.
Residents of Kien Svay district who attended the inauguration of the Third Ring Road said that they miss Samdech and will always remember Samdech Techo's merits for the nation and people of Cambodia.
However, they respect Samdech Techo's decision to arrange a successor, which is the most appropriate thing.
