(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, met with a US congressional delegation to discuss strengthening trade between Cambodia and the United States.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed ways to strengthen trade and investment cooperation between the two countries.
The Minister informed about the results of the recent elections held in July 2023 and the recent progress in expanding the Cambodian market, such as the signing of regional and bilateral free trade agreements, as well as Improve the business and investment environment to attract more investment.
In addition, Minister Pan Sosak also asked the US Congress to renew its GSP system. Especially for some goods such as clothes, shoes and travel goods. The Minister believes that the renewal of the GSP system will strengthen trade cooperation between the two countries by providing mutual benefits.
Finally, the Minister also called on US companies to invest more in Cambodia to reduce the trade deficit between the two countries, as well as to benefit from each other.
