The Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to learn the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings. People who believe in Buddhism always celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible.
For each pagoda during the three months of the rainy season, it is not allowed to travel far beyond the day and night, unless there are important duties such as parents who are seriously ill or going to perform dharma, etc., determined to return Return within 7 days.
