(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of August 3, 2023, explained four reasons that led to Samdech decided to leave the post of Prime Minister of Cambodia for the seventh term.
The four reasons are: First, the transfer of power to the youth is now stable and secure, Second: The readiness of the youth to take turns, Third: Samdech continues to hold the position of leader of the ruling party, which is Two-tiered belt for peace and development, and fourth: overwhelming support for the new Prime Minister, Dr. Hun Manet.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made on the occasion of the inauguration of the third ring road on the morning of August 3, 2023.
Samdech continued that there were two scenarios that have been set out: 1: the old cabinet can continue to lead the country for a year or two and then continue to the next generation and the second scenario: is for the youth to start from the beginning of the mandate. Given the favorable conditions, the Party Standing Committee decided to select the second, the new Royal Government as a youth from the beginning of the mandate to give full power to the successor.
For the second reason, Samdech stated that the younger generation came to lead when they were well prepared to receive the care of the elderly, and they are no longer young for the Prime Minister of the seventh term, Dr. Hun Manet became Prime Minister at the age of 46, more than when Samdech became Prime Minister 14 years ago.
Samdech added that the mandate cabinet, which is a group of young people, is capable enough, with some already serving as deputy prime ministers, ministers and secretaries of state in various ministries and institutions. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked for the understanding of the old minister must dare to sacrifice to give the role to the youth to take turns.
