On July 26, 2023, after the announcement of the provisional election results showing that the CPP had won more than 6.3 million votes, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that he would not run for office. The post of Prime Minister for the 7th term of the Royal Government was transferred to Dr. Hun Manet as another candidate decided by the Cambodian People's Party.
Samdech said that the transfer of young people is now more stable than when Samdech, as well as senior officials of the Cambodian People's Party held office until old age. Samdech questioned how many prime ministers have relinquished power like Samdech when he was able to be prime minister for another 5 to 10 years, but it is not a good thing to stay in office until old age. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that regarding this leadership arrangement, two scenarios have been mentioned, the first is to consider that the old group may continue to lead the Royal Government in the new term for another year or two and have left and handed over. For the next generation, the second scenario is for you to take turns starting from the beginning of the mandate.
"Based on the conditions and conditions as well as the favorable situation, the Party Standing Committee has decided to choose the second scenario for the new government to leave from the beginning without a transition by the old people to do so," he said. "We give full power to those who take turns, to be able to do their work throughout the mandate."
"And they are no longer young compared to me. I was in power when I was prime minister, only 32 years old, but now the new prime minister is 46 years old," he added. "They are 14 years older than me and this group has trained enough, some of which have been in the government for a long time."
