Ten suspects involved in the shooting death of a Vietnamese man in Boeung Keng Kang district have been sent to court while other factions are fleeing
(Phnom Penh): After careful research leading to a series of crackdowns on 10 male and female suspects, including 9 Vietnamese, one Cambodian involved in the shooting of a Vietnamese man, causing death in the middle The day in Boeung Keng Kang district was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the afternoon of August 3, 2023.
It should be noted that on July 29, 2023 at 01:30 noon, a murder case occurred caused by an unidentified suspect using a car and a motorcycle with two small arms. The victim, 37-year-old Nguyen Tun Hung, a Vietnamese national, was shot dead on Street 360, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 1, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh, and died at the scene.
In total, during the operation, specialized police arrested 15 people, including 10 people involved in the shooting. During the arrest, the police confiscated 3 cars, 1 motorbike, 2 small arms, 2 bullets, 5 bullets, some blue pills and some white powder, as well as two drug scales.
Although 10 suspects were arrested and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action, the specialized police force has not yet completed its operation, which is still searching for some more suspects. More than 20 kg of drugs were burned in Svay Rieng province
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Men Vibol set some goals to improve the effectiveness of prevention and fight against drugs in Svay Rieng, with the following key points:
* First, to pay attention to the implementation of the circular and message of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, as well as the content of the topic in this year to come out as real activities and practical results at the local level to jointly reduce and eliminate Discrimination and stigma of drug addicts.
* Second, we must continue to pay more attention to the implementation of the Royal Government's order on the strengthening of anti-drug measures, safe village, commune and village policy. In particular, the implementation of the five measures of the campaign against illegal drugs.
* Third: To continue to promote education better, more active and active by continuing to strengthen and expand cooperation and movement for participation and support from all components of society to ensure that all target groups. Get an education and a better understanding of the law and its effects.
* Fourth, the competent forces and local authorities at all levels must increase, strengthen and pay attention to promote the implementation of administrative measures and the strict implementation of legal measures for targets that are prone to or occur in drug offenses, especially in Casinos, hotels, guesthouses, rental houses, nightclubs, karaoke and complex areas.
Fifth, all competent authorities must inspire people to be more active in providing information from criminals who intend to secretly produce, process and trade drugs in the province.
* Sixth: The commanders of the armed forces of all kinds must pay more attention to educating, instructing and strengthening the management of their forces as strictly as possible to avoid being involved in drug crimes and with drug criminals.
Seventh, the Armed Forces of all kinds and local authorities at all levels, especially in the border areas, must strengthen the control mechanisms at the border gates in the province as strictly as possible to prevent the import of narcotics. All kinds.
* Eighth: All administrative police stations must pay attention to managing and clearly grasping the targets of drug sales and distribution, especially migrants who come to stay temporarily, engage in other occupations in their localities and must be cracked down on. The time when a crime occurs.
9th: To continue to strengthen the capacity, quality and effectiveness of drug detoxification mechanisms in existing health centers and hospitals in the province to work better and more effectively to ensure that drug victims receive services. Drug neutralization and rehabilitation.
* 10th: Call on parents and guardians of all students to increase the monitoring and monitoring of their children's education regularly and work closely with the teachers in charge of each class as a mechanism to remind Let their children escape the onslaught of drugs.
