(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police on August 3, 2023 issued a statement regarding the posting of false information on Facebook named TNM, which was posted on social media on the 2nd. August 2023: Drug crackdown on Russey Keo school, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The Quick Reaction Team of the Anti-Drug Department of the National Police would like to inform the public that:
1: On July 30, 2023, after receiving information and requests from the people on the illegal distribution of drugs in Russey Keo school, the expert group (A5) of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes visited During the search, the perpetrators ran away and detained only two young men and brought them to the department for questioning.
After questioning, it was found that the two young men actually used drugs, especially e-cigarettes. Authorities have stopped educating people about the dangers of using drugs and using e-cigarettes, which they mistaken for illegal. The Anti-Drug Department then invited the guardians to ensure that they were educated and rehabilitated in the community according to the procedures.
2: The images and audio recordings included in this broadcast are not related to the operation of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes, which is the malicious intent of the Facebook owner, TMN, in order to deceive the public, discredit the authorities and protect the perpetrators. Only.
