Iranian Revolutionary Guards conduct surprise military drills Wednesday as US boosts military presence in the region
Tehran: Iran's paramilitary forces on Wednesday launched a surprise military exercise on the Arabian Gulf as the US military increased its presence in the region. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on August 2, 2023.
Iran has not given a reason for initiating the exercise, although such shocking exercises have taken place in the past.
The Pentagon said the deployment was in response to Iran's recent attempts to threaten the free flow of trade in the Strait of Hormuz and its surrounding waters.
About 20 percent of the world's oil passes through this strait that connects the Arabian Gulf to the world, which the United States considers important to its national security and to keep global energy prices stable. .
