(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as relatives, families and accompanying delegates on August 2, 2023, offered candles, incense, flowers and many other offerings to God. Samma Samput will bring Preah Vossa candles, relics and some suffixes to the monks waiting for Preah Vossa at Wat Mony Sovann called Wat Champouk K'aek in Chbar Ampov district, Phnom Penh.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, a clear Buddhist supporter in Buddhism, who has always led officials at all levels of the Cambodian Red Cross and many other officials, brought many relics, including suffixes, to the monks at the pagoda to support. And raise the banner of Buddhism, the state religion, to flourish.
No matter what the circumstances, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen always pays attention and cares about the lack of monks in the pagodas, in fact, the rainy season has arrived.
According to the Buddhist tradition, all monks in Cambodia are invited to enter the rainy season for three months from the first day of the month of Assad to study the Dharma. The annual rainy season is held during the rainy season, when people as well as monks find it difficult to travel and travel from place to place, and it is time for monks to practice their studies. Discipline is also consistent.
