The following is the full text of the invitation letter of the General Department of Taxation: Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued a sub-decree on the transfer of functions in the field of education, youth and sports to the municipal administration.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this sub-decree aims to improve the management and provision of effective education, youth and sports services, quality, accountability, transparency, environment and social equity by narrowing decisions, accountability and accountability. Management and provision of these services to municipal, district and khan administrations throughout the country.
According to the sub-decree, the main points include:
Assign 3 functions in the field of education to the municipal, district and khan administration, including: 1: Early childhood education management function 2: Primary education management function 3: Non-formal education management function
The specific functions and activities for each of the above functions are set out in Annex 1 of this sub-decree.
The 14 municipal administrations in Battambang province must continue to manage and implement the above three functions in the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 182 dated December 2, 2019 on the functions and structure of the municipal administration and Sub-Decree No. 184 dated December 2, 2019 on the functions and structure of the district administration and this sub-decree.
Continue to delegate 3 administrative support functions in the field of education, youth and sports to the municipal, district and khan administration, including: 1: Administrative support functions to secondary education institutions 2: Administrative support functions to youth development work 3: Administrative support functions Administration to physical education and sports.
The sub-functions and specific activities for each of the above functions are defined in Annex 2 of this sub-decree.
