Warsaw: Poland on Tuesday said it was rushing to send more troops to the country's eastern border after accusing Belarus, a close ally of Russia, of encroaching on its airspace. Military helicopters. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, August 2, 2023.
The Polish Defense Ministry said it was sending additional troops and resources, including combat helicopters, and also reported the incident to NATO as the Belarusian Chargé d'Affaires was summoned. Enter to provide interpretation. The Polish military initially claimed that no border violations had taken place, but later acknowledged that it had taken place.
The Belarusian Defense Ministry denied Polish claims and said that Warsaw immediately changed its mind about the incident, apparently after consulting with its foreign counterpart. Minsk has even accused Poland of using false accusations as a pretext for mobilizing its forces on the border.
Tensions between Poland and Belarus escalated after Russian Wagner mercenaries were stationed in Belarusian waters in July and Wagner fighters recently helped train troops. Belarus, in particular, is a city not far from the Polish border.
