(Mondulkiri): National Road No. 76A in Mondulkiri Province collapsed into a 50-meter-long waterfall at O'Ngei point in Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district, Mondulkiri province, between km 91 and km 99.
Mondulkiri provincial governor Thong Savun has ordered a temporary halt to traffic, waiting for authorities to clear the bypass to ease traffic at the crash site.
He said that on the afternoon of August 2, the authorities, together with professional officials from the Ministry of Public Works and provincial officials, cooperated to use bulldozers to build a new bypass to temporarily facilitate people's travel.
Major General Lor Sokha, Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, said that the section of National Road 76A that collapsed completely at O'Ngei was completely suspended. The base forbids people from passing through.
On that occasion, the commissioner also donated raincoats and food to the forces stationed at the collapse.
