He added that Buddhists, who are devout Buddhists, often celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible.
The governor added that Buddhism is the state religion that we all believe in and obey because Buddhism provides psychological education to do good deeds and help each other to live in a society. By harmony.
He said that Buddhism has played an important role in educating moral society as a shelter for the education of local children and as a place for young people from rural and urban areas to continue their education.
He said that the field of Buddhism has made an important contribution to the Royal Government in educating and teaching people to do good deeds, recognize sins and help develop the society to prosper.
He called on the masses to join in maintaining the precious peace and give all of us the opportunity to celebrate and enjoy all kinds of freedoms.
