(Phnom Penh): A delegation from the Singapore Business Federation and 23 other company representatives visited Cambodia to explore market and investment potential, especially to seek cooperation and business opportunities in Cambodia after the parliamentary elections. Seventh of the National Assembly.
The delegation of the Singapore Business Federation and the representatives of the Singaporean companies met with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on the morning of August 1, 2023 to inform them about the mission to find opportunities. Investment and business in Cambodia.
He said the visit of the Singapore Business Federation delegation was a positive sign for Singaporean businessmen and investors about Cambodia, which has managed well the spread of Kovid-19 and opened up opportunities for international investors and tourists to return. Return to Cambodia to participate in economic recovery.
However, the General Secretary also informed the delegation about the achievements and developments of the past 25 years, Cambodia still faces many difficulties and obstacles, such as the negative effects of geopolitical and economic tensions, fierce competition. Among developed economies, climate change, natural disasters, and the spread of pandemics are among the worst.
He added that in relation to the policy agenda for socio-economic development in the next five years of the Royal Government, which will be led by the Cambodian People's Party, with the future of the next generation of leaders with energy and ability to build. The basis for achieving the vision of Cambodia 2050 as a high-income country.
In this spirit, the Royal Government will implement the first phase of the Pentagon political program and strategy, which will focus on enhancing governance and institutional capacity, creating a conducive environment for socio-economic development, human capital development, economic diversification and growth. Competitiveness, private sector and employment development, sustainable and environmental development, and digital economic and social development.
