Monks are required to stay at the pagoda for three months during the rainy season and are not allowed to travel long distances during the day unless they have important duties, such as their parents who are seriously ill or determined to perform dharma. Return within 7 days. This festival starts from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
On that occasion, Major General Sithi Loh also paid a courtesy call on General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Government Working Group, and Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province. All monks, grandparents in Svay Chek district.
Major General Sithi Loh also paid a courtesy call on the monks and nuns, and all the monks and nuns, and the generals, colonels, deputy commissioners, district police chiefs, commanders, grandfathers, grandmothers and grandfathers. All friends who attended the ceremony, please approve the director of the respective merit and wish to receive good health and the four blessings of the Buddha: age, class, happiness, strength, do not be lazy.
The ceremony was held at Trapeang Neak School in the above commune village in the presence of Mrs. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross and colleagues, including Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee of Kampong Chhnang Province.
During the meeting and distribution of humanitarian donations to the above people, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent greetings and thoughts on the life and health of Grandma and Grandpa. And all the people who live in Tang Krasang district, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province.
On that occasion, the First Deputy Secretary-General also brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, urging all people to take care of their health, drink boiled water and food. Get enough nutrients, avoid foods that taste too salty or too sweet, which can lead to high blood pressure, cancer, or other illnesses.
At the same time, during the rainy season, be careful of natural disasters, floods, hurricanes, typhoons, as well as diseases caused by mosquitoes, such as dengue fever, malaria or diseases caused by poor hygiene. She also called on young people and local authorities to take good care of the elderly parents in the village, do not abandon them and avoid this problem.
