Cambodia-China Friendship Radio The Cambodian Cashew Federation urges cashew processing companies in Vietnam to buy cashews directly from farmers without going through a broker (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): An Dara, President of the Cambodian Cashew Federation, urges cashew processing companies in Vietnam Buy cashews directly from farmers or communities without having to go through a broker to get farmers value added.
An Dara is pushing this because at present about 85% to 90% of cashew sales to processors in Vietnam are done through brokers, while Vietnam is the country that buys more than 95% of raw cashew nuts from Cambodia. And the two countries are also fenced countries that are easy to transport.
An Dara's urging came during a meeting with the President of the Vietnam Cashew Association this weekend at the Cambodian Cashew Association headquarters in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
He said that the Cashew Federation wants large companies with Vietnamese standards to receive raw cashew nuts from Cambodia, as currently processing of cashew products in Cambodia is still low, about 5%, while Cambodia is in The largest producer in the world. Therefore, Cambodia needs Vietnam to buy raw cashew nuts for processing.
He added that direct purchase from farmers can be done through cooperation with the Cambodian Cashew Federation, and the Cambodian Cashew Federation will strive to help farmers to harvest and dry cashew nuts to meet standards.
At the same time, both sides want to seek mutual support in order for Vietnam to share experiences and help promote processing in Cambodia, as Vietnam has nearly 20 years of experience in processing cashew products.
As Cambodia prepares for the World Cashew Conference, he invited the Vietnam Cashew Association to join and share the experience of organizing the forum. In addition, I would like to see Vietnamese processing companies show how to process Vietnamese cashew products in this forum to promote the processing of all kinds of meat and cashew nuts in Cambodia.
"What the cashew federation is trying to do to help the processing of the Cambodian cashew sector in line with the national policy on cashews, which plans to process 25% in 2027 and 50% in 2032."
