Dr. Chea Serey Issorn, the first woman to become the Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The appointment of the new Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia is a wise decision that requires careful selection because This task requires outstanding elites with deep knowledge as well as experience and outstanding work.
On July 29, 2023, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, ordered the appointment of Dr. Chea Serey as Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The appointment is a testament to Cambodia's growing human resources to a world where outstanding and capable women serve as the country's central bank leaders, most of whom are men.
A report by the International Monetary Fund (IMF) shows that of the 190 IMF member countries, only 26 are female leaders serving as finance ministers and only 17 are central bank governors. . This figure means that only 11.3% of women leaders hold leadership positions in the two main economic policy institutions: the governor, the central bank and the finance minister.
Dr. Chea Serey is the most suitable person for the position of Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia because she has deep knowledge and a clear vision for a long time to work and lead the Cambodian banking system to achieve many good results. International stage.
After graduating with a bachelor's and master's degree in New Zealand and the United Kingdom, she attended the first generation of senior students at the Lee Kuan Yew School of Public Policy and later earned a PhD in Economics. PhD) from the University of Adelaide, Australia.
Under her skillful and wise leadership, the payment system infrastructure has been modernized, especially the introduction of the new "Bakong" modern payment system, which uses blockchain technology, facilitating the transfer of money from one bank to another. Easy, fast and secure.
She is also the Chairman of the Board of Credit Bureau (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. (CBC), the first and only private credit sharing system in Cambodia. She has played a leading role in establishing the CBC, which has helped make Cambodia the seventh largest country in the world in terms of ease of access to credit, according to the World Bank's 2017 Business Report.
She also chairs the Cambodian Economic Association, a network of leading economists and experts in the country for roundtable policy discussions and promoting evidence-based policy-making.
She has always been active in promoting the use of the riel through direct discussions with stakeholders, researching and implementing policies to promote the use of the riel. In addition, she is a prominent Cambodian figure on the international stage in the field of finance and innovation.
She is often invited to speak at various national and international conferences on topics related to the Central Bank, ASEAN Banking, FinTech Finance and Digital Currency, and has been invited as a keynote speaker at In many popular international media such as CNN, CNBC and CGTN.
Financial experts have expressed optimism about the appointment of Dr. Chea Serey as the current Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, and said that the appointment was in response to her great efforts and dedication. In the past, to raise the profile of the Cambodian financial sector in the region and on the international stage, as well as to set an example for other women to strengthen women's rights in economic activities.
Dr. IN Channy, President & CEO of ACLEDA Bank, considers Chea Serey as the mother of digital banking and the creator of ethics for banking and financial institutions through her leading role in establishing the Credit Bureau of Cambodia (CBC) and the payment system. Famous Bakong.
For Social Work In addition to career success, Dr. Chea Serey is the Co-Founder and President of the Children's Fund, which focuses on the well-being of poor children in Cambodia and raises awareness about disability, physical and intellectual disabilities. Save the Children has initiated the first "Hearing Day" in Cambodia and has focused on raising mental health awareness among university students.
In addition, she is a board member of Smile Cambodia, whose mission is to give children with cleft lip and palate a new smile by providing free surgery and actively supporting the mission of the Eye Foundation. Khmer through the leadership of young volunteers to support the program of the Foundation to examine and operate on eyes, ears, nose and throat for patients for free.
