This year marks the 25th anniversary of the win-win strategy that Prime Minister Hun Sen has put in place to achieve complete peace in Cambodia in late 1998.
Since the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, Cambodia has transformed both economically and politically into an active player on regional and global forums promoting peace, multilateralism, the rule of law and international cooperation as an economic nation. Fastest growing in Asia.
Receiving international financial investment is absolutely necessary and the Cambodian people are always grateful. But the important thing is to use these funds carefully for the public good. Although investment has doubled, if budgets and financial resources are misused due to poor planning or corruption, development will be hampered.
In contrast, Cambodia's economy grew at an average annual rate of 7.7% between 1998 and 2019, making it one of the fastest growing economies in the world. Recently, after the outbreak of Kovid-19, the Cambodian economy continued to recover in 2022 with real growth of 5.2%, according to the World Bank.
On July 23, the 7th National Assembly Election was held successfully, peacefully, transparently, professionally and with high sovereignty and legitimacy, which is the seventh general election since 1993 since the democratization. Is restored and is moving forward to become a more mature and strong democracy.
Observers need to abide by the code of conduct set by the NEC, and they have the right to observe without being banned. In addition, 18 political parties also participated in the election, emphasizing the space of political freedom guaranteed by the Cambodian Constitution, the nation's supreme law.
