Taliban, US hold first formal talks since re-emergence in Afghanistan (Video inside) (Taliban): Taliban leaders meet US officials in Qatar for first time since returning He returned to rule Afghanistan two years ago. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, August 1, 2023.
Taliban Foreign Ministry spokesman Abdul Qahar Balkhi said Monday that the two sides discussed confidence-building measures during the two-day talks, which included lifting sanctions. Travel bans, as well as the handover of Afghanistan Central Bank assets frozen abroad, the fight against drugs and human rights issues.
According to a State Department statement during the talks, the US delegation included Special Representative Thomas West and Special Envoy for Women, Girls and Human Rights for Afghanistan Rina Amiri. He expressed grave concern over the detention, crackdown on the media and restrictions on religious practice, and called on the Taliban to address the issue.
Since taking over Afghanistan in August 2021, no country has officially recognized the Taliban as a legitimate government. Faced with international condemnation over restrictions on the education of Afghan women, it is also facing a humanitarian crisis, with almost half of its population of 23 million dependent on the World Food Program (WFP).
