The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has stated that the drop in inflation in Cambodia was mainly due to lower oil prices and a slowdown in food prices, while core inflation was low.
Core inflation, meanwhile, continued to slow to 1.5% in the second half of 2022, 3.8% and 5% in the first half of 2022, mainly due to the already strong base at the same time last year. The effect of lower food and fuel prices.
The National Bank of Cambodia also stated that maintaining the stability of the exchange rate contributed to lower inflation in the first half to a low of about 1.2%.
At the meeting to review the results of the first half and the direction of the second half of 2023 of the National Bank of Cambodia, Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia said that while the value of the US dollar in the international market tends to increase. The riel has been kept stable at an average of 4,094 riel per US dollar, similar to the same period last year, to protect the purchasing power of the riel as well as the income of vulnerable people.
He added that due to dollarization, exchange rate fluctuations have a direct and rapid effect on inflation in Cambodia, because when the riel depreciates, the prices of goods and services will rise immediately. Thus, in addition to lower fuel prices and lower food prices, the stabilization of the riel exchange rate has contributed significantly to lowering inflation.
According to a report by the National Bank of Cambodia in 2023, growth is expected to continue at around 5.5% and inflation is projected to fall to around 2%. The decline was due to lower oil prices, which are projected to slow as global economies grow slower than last year and the global supply chain improves.
Cambodia's $ 18.4 billion in international reserves will allow for the import and export of essential goods and services for seven months in the event of an emergency. This is according to the first half report and work direction for the second half of 2023 of the National Bank of Cambodia.
According to a report by the National Bank of Cambodia, "This increase in reserves is due to the increase in foreign investment income, gold prices and deposits of the Royal Government and banking and financial institutions at the National Bank of Cambodia." "
According to the report, the high level of international reserves indicates the ability to maintain a stable exchange rate, confidence in the national currency, the basis for foreign borrowing, and provide adequate protection to meet liquidity needs in the face of external crises.
International Reserve Investment is carried out flexibly, and investment risks are carefully managed and monitored and in accordance with the National Bank of Cambodia's Investment Guidelines to ensure the safe, liquidity and accessibility of international reserves. Appropriate income.
In early 2023, the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) updated its investment guidelines, adjusting the component of investment and currency reserves to meet growing demand for liquidity and the ability to seize opportunities from interest rate fluctuations. Marketing.
The National Bank of Cambodia continues to focus on increasing investment in green bonds and bonds related to the social environment and governance issued by major international financial institutions in China, South Korea, Japan and Europe.
Please be informed that according to the explanation of the National Bank of Cambodia, international reserves are the property of a country that is internationally recognized and controlled by the monetary authority to be used in case of need, such as financing the balance sheet if there is a need for intervention. Exchange markets to control exchange rate fluctuations and maintain confidence in the national currency and economy.
