Book of Historical Witnesses: Diary of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): 2023 is the 50th anniversary of the birth of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej.
Taking this opportunity, the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Center of Cambodia is honored to announce the release of a Khmer translation of the 1973 Royal Record recording of the historic journey of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. .
The book is entitled "Historical Witnesses: The Diary of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia", a unique historical document that reflects the Queen's direct observation of the Queen's mission and travels. He went to the liberated area of the Cambodian National United Front in Cambodia.
Her Majesty the Queen accompanied by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Cambodia, began his journey by airplane from Beijing to Hanoi and then continued by car. Along the Ho Chi Minh Trail towards Siem Reap / Angkor Wat, crossing parts of the Sihanoukville Trail in about 39 days.
His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, a personal letter of his experience on the original text in French. In 2021, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia granted the Royal Thai Documentation Center to the official translation of his diary into English to provide a wider learning opportunity for the general public.
Not only that, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, His Majesty the King also granted permission to the Documentation Center of Cambodia to officially translate his diary into Khmer. The Khmer translation of the Royal Diary of the Queen Mother has been completed and published by the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
The Khmer translation of this diary is very important to historians and all Cambodians. The Queen's Diary is a reference to the most important and priceless historical record, describing a unique period for all Cambodians.
At present, 4,276 diary books of the Queen Mother of Cambodia in the Khmer language have been distributed to the public in six provinces by the staff of the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
Mr. Youk Chhang confirmed that the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Center of Cambodia will publish a book on historical witnesses: the diary of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, 100,000 copies to be distributed to the general public in the next 3 years .
