(Phnom Penh): A family with six young children who were evicted by their owners because they did not have money to pay their rent, has now returned to live in their own house with unparalleled excitement and joy No comparison.
Mr. Thuch Tou and his wife and six young children were confiscated by Mr. Min Kimsan, the owner of Borey Sen Monorom, for failing to pay the rent for the last three years. Thuch Tou and his wife and children have been evicted for almost six months. He tried to seek intervention and mediation with the owner to return to live in the house. But the search for intervention has not yet shed light on any solution.
After the news was published on Fresh News and informed to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo also introduced to Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh to meet with the owner of the Borey and the owner to find a solution that can be obtained. Each.
Under this guidance, on the morning of Monday, July 31, 2023, the Governor of Phnom Penh called the owner of the Borey and the owner to talk and also reached mutual understanding and favor. The owner of the Borey also allowed Mr. Thuch Tou to bring his wife and children back to live in his house.
Being away from home, having lived peacefully for more than five months, made Mr. Thuch Tou and his wife and children miss home very much. Mr. Thuch Tou and his wife and children did not expect to have the opportunity to return home.
After receiving mediation, Mr. Thuch Tou did not hesitate to leave Phnom Penh City Hall immediately, he brought his wife and six children back to his home. Home is a necessary need for everyone to be a shelter for life. Mr. Thuch Tou and his wife and children showed a big smile when they returned to their shelter.
Both Mr. Thuch, his wife and children are very happy. Mr. Thuch Tou expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as the Governor of Phnom Penh, who came forward to coordinate with the owner of the Borey to return to live in the house.
Mr. Thuch Tou said that the help of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit is a great blessing for him and his family and throughout his life he will never forget this merit.
It should be noted that Mr. Thuch Tou bought a house in the above Borey in 2015 for nearly 30,000 dollars and had to pay nearly $ 400 per month in installments for more than 10 years.
Mr. Thuch Tou came to live in the house above for more than 6 years and also paid in installments for about 5 years. The Kovid Crisis 19 The war in Ukraine and the rivalry of superpowers have had a devastating effect on Cambodia's economy, and Thuch Tou, a glassblower and tricycle rider, has also affected his daily income. Mr. Thuch Tou was no longer able to pay the installment to the Borey as in the contract, which led to the Borey owner confiscating the house.
Leaving the house for almost 6 months, the house is covered with dust and spider webs. When he arrived home, Mr. Thuch Tou and his children cleaned the house to live happily with a smile.
