Ms. Pum Chantyny requested the Red Cross branches in 4 target provinces to continue to implement sustainably in the program to promote humanitarian activities and community health to be successful.
(Kandal): Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross requested the Red Cross branches in 4 target provinces: Kandal, Tbong Khmum, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin to continue to implement sustainable programs in promoting humanitarian activities and community health successfully. .
Ms. Pum Chantyny made this request during the closing ceremony and handing over of the program to promote humanitarian activities and community health to the four target branches of the Red Cross at the branch office of the Cambodian Red Cross in Kandal province on the morning of July 31, 2023.
Ms. Pum Chantyny said that the program to promote humanitarian activities and community health with the financial support of the European Union through the International Federation of Red Cross, Red Crescent and Finnish Red Cross, the Cambodian Red Cross has been implementing 194 goals in 20 villages, 20 communes, 10 cities. Districts in Kandal, Tbong Khmum, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin provinces for the past 3 years.
The Humanitarian and Community Health Promotion Program aims to contribute by improving the well-being of vulnerable people by implementing three main activities: first: epidemic preparedness, second: disaster management / Climate change and 3: Institutional development.
Ms. Pum Chantyny added that after the completion of the program to promote humanitarian activities and community health, as the European Union has changed its priorities, operations and risk reduction work, so each target province must show its ownership and responsibility. It continues to carry out humanitarian activities and community health in a sustainable and highly effective manner.
