(Phnom Penh): Representatives of Ta Prohm village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh, have filed a complaint to the Chbar Ampov district governor to intervene in a case where a rooster farm where hundreds of roosters are disturbing their daily lives. Of them.
A letter from a villager states that a rooster farm located along National Road 1 in Ta Prohm village, Prek Eang commune, caused a lot of noise, seriously affecting the rest of the lives and learning of the roosters. Hundreds of heads rang out day and night.
Residents said that in the past, local officials had given instructions several times, but the farm owner refused to listen. Therefore, people ask the authorities to take action on this case, because it affects people living around, especially the elderly with physical illness and children who need to rest and study.
