Royal Government issues sub-decree on "Identification of disability by social model and basic rights"
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has issued a sub-decree on "Identification of disability by social model and basic rights." According to a sub-decree issued by the Royal Government of Cambodia, this sub-decree aims to determine the mechanisms and procedures for the identification of disabilities according to social norms and basic rights.
The sub-decree has the following contents:
* First: Develop and manage a disability identification database system to have a common standard of information technology for disability management as a basis, set a target code for people with disabilities to improve the quality of life, access to social services "Development for the rich. Disabilities and used as data to target social assistance programs and social security systems in the social protection system.
* Second: Provide ID cards for people with disabilities to make it easier for people with disabilities to receive benefits, social protection systems and other social services with equity and environment in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
