Lt. Gen. Thet instructs Phnom Penh police to believe in government leadership to safeguard peace, stability and development
(Phnom Penh): In front of more than 700 police officers of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, instructed the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Force to believe in the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia in order to Preserve peace, stability and lead the country to further development after the 7th legislative election.
Lt. Gen. Thet made this instruction on the morning of Monday, July 31, 2023, when he led more than 700 police officers of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to inspect the force and salute the flag.
Lt. Gen. Thet also instructed the Phnom Penh Police Force to continue to strive to respect the rules and regulations of the National Police Force, especially to set a good example for the people.
