(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has been supporting economic growth by maintaining price and financial stability, developing the banking and payment system to promote economic growth and development in various sectors in the Cambodian economy. Affected by the slowdown in global economic activity.
This is according to Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia on the occasion of the opening of the meeting to review the work results of the first half and the work direction of the second half of 2023 of the National Bank of Cambodia held on July 30. 2023.
Meanwhile, in a situation where the value of the US dollar in the international market tends to increase, the riel has been kept stable at an average of 4,094 riel per US dollar, similar to the same period last year, to protect the purchasing power of the currency. Riel as well as the income of vulnerable people.
He added that due to dollarization, exchange rate fluctuations have a direct and rapid effect on inflation in Cambodia, because once the exchange rate depreciates, the prices of goods and services will rise immediately. Thus, in addition to lower fuel prices and lower food prices, maintaining the stability of the riel exchange rate has contributed significantly to lower inflation.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the Cambodian banking system has been further developed and the stability of the banking system has played an active role in promoting economic activity and maintaining practical financial stability, despite the tight financial conditions in the global financial situation. Three in the United States collapsed in early 2023, raising concerns in international financial markets, and the Cambodian banking system remains strong and resilient.
