(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ny Phally, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, Deputy Secretary General of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia (CCHR) and Chairman of the Working Group for Monitoring and Evaluation of Clean Beaches Issue a plan to collect seagrass from communities and traders enjoying Angkol beach to be converted into natural organic fertilizer for use in agricultural crops.
During the mission to inspect, evaluate and improve beaches and canals in Kep province on July 27, 2023, Mr. Ny Phally led the team to compete in the 4th Clean Beach and 1st Clean Canal Competition. 2023, with the participation of representatives of the Kep Provincial Administration and relevant departments and units around the province, observed a lot of sea flute debris scattered on the beach.
Mr. Ny Phally, Team Leader, set out a plan to procure and help find markets for these sea flute waste by asking the community and traders who enjoy Angkor Beach to clean the beach and collect sacks for daily use. To be converted into natural organic fertilizer used in agricultural crops.
This innovative plan has been hailed and supported by the community and local authorities, which will not only promote the regular maintenance of sanitation and the clean environment in the Angkor area, which is an important indicator of support. This beach is not only a candidate to win in the future, but also to promote the development of Angkol beach as an attractive tourist destination to prepare to receive national and international tourists to relax.
It should be noted that after the launch of the plan to turn the sea waste into money, there are currently about 1,100 bags of sea flute waste to be used in the cultivation of agricultural crops.
