EU suspends financial aid, security cooperation with Niger after coup
The European Union (EU) has suspended financial support and security cooperation with Niger immediately following a military coup in Brussels, the country's top diplomat said on Saturday. That. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Saturday, July 29, 2023.
Niger is a major recipient of Western aid and a key EU partner in helping to curb irregular migration from sub-Saharan Africa. For 2021 to 2024, the European Union has provided $ 554 million to improve governance, education and sustainable growth in Niger.
Khan Sen Sok Tax Branch Manager Purchased a Book to Distribute to Subordinates
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heang Srun, Head of Taxation, Sen Sok Branch, purchased 100 copies of the book "Heritage of the SEA Games and the first ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia in the Techo era" to distribute to his officials and their families to read and document in Sports history in Cambodia.
Mr. Heang Srun stated that this book is very important to show the excellence and national honor of Cambodia in the era of peace on the international stage, and to encourage the author, he also bought this book directly from the author. Heang Srun also encouraged other officials to have this book in the library, both at home and at work, as a support document.
Please be reminded that the book "Legacy of the SEA Games and the first ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia in the Techo era" compiled by Mr. Chhay Sophal, a veteran journalist and journalism lecturer at some universities, was officially launched on the 21st. Last July under the presidency of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information.
This book contains many pictures related to sports, especially pictures of many officials who have lit up sports both at home and abroad, as well as in view of watching sports and the opening and closing ceremonies of the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games.
The book also presents some off-stage stories about sports, related to the ideology and political geography of the superpowers at the start of the Cold War, which divided the right-wing (liberal bloc) and left-wing The communist bloc) and since these two sports were officially established, Cambodia has never organized a single event until 2023.
The book also captures images of the process of asking for fire and torch, sports and parades in the country and to 10 other countries in Southeast Asia until the official opening day of the Games.
Mr. Chhay Sophal recalled the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, saying that Cambodia is a small country with a big heart and money can be spent only on honor and reputation, and leave it to the next generation to know. .
At a time when the world is facing an economic crisis from the war between Russia and Ukraine, and the intervention of NATO and its allies, as the global Kovid-19 pandemic continues and climate change is a major global concern. These are great achievements and have brought the prestige and excellence of the country to the international stage as the host of the above two sporting events.
