Mr. Khieu Kanharith Presented Candles in Remembrance of Monks to 27 Monks in Koh Sotin District and Meet with Muslims in Koh Sotin Commune
The ceremony of handing out candles and gifts after the ceremony took place on the morning of July 29, 2023 at Chhon Hall, Wat Por Rithi, also known as Wat Tnaot, Village 11, Koh Sotin Commune, Kampong Cham Province.
Donation of Vesa candles as well as food and suffixes to the monks on this occasion to burn, offer sacrifices to God and study the Dharma of the Dharma of our Master Samma.
The Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to learn the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings. People who believe in Buddhism often celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible.
For each pagoda during the three months of the rainy season, it is not allowed to go far away at night, except for important tasks such as parents who are seriously ill or going to perform dharma, etc., determined to return. Return within 7 days.
The rainy season is celebrated every year from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
Give suffixes to 27 monks, 10,000 Riels per person, the committee of 27 pagoda abbots, 10,000 Riels per pagoda. Along with the candle offering ceremony, Reaksmey Hang Meas Company contributed $ 2,000.
On the occasion of the candle lighting ceremony, Minister Khieu Kanharith conveyed the message of greetings and memories from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to all leaders, civil servants and people throughout Koh Sotin district and thanked them. All who went to the 7th parliamentary election, which took place on July 23.
The minister said that all religions do not teach people to do evil, but to teach people to do good.
A large number of countries do not allow Muslims to wear uniforms and robes or to wear religious hats to school and to take photographs with ID cards or passports. In Cambodia, however, it is permissible to wear it without having to remove the krama or hat.
On the other hand, the Cambodian Muslims living in the country have full rights without any religious conflicts. On this occasion, Mr. Khieu Kanharith and she brought money and rice to the mosque in the 13th village, Koh Sotin commune.
Ministry of Economy opens "Insurance Forum 2023" in Kampot Province
(Kampot): Mr. Ros Silva, Secretary of State and Vice Chairman of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority and Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Non-Financial Services Authority The Bank opened the "Insurance Forum 2023" on July 29, 2023 in Kampot province.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Chantha, Deputy Governor, Representative of Dr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot, Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, Mr. Huy Vatharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, accompanying delegates and stakeholders. Many.
On that occasion, senior officials of the Ministry of Economy and Finance introduced nine important tasks to the insurance regulator and all stakeholders, including:
* First, strengthen the management of the insurance market by continuously setting out the necessary regulations and taking timely action to ensure compliance with the insurance laws and all relevant regulations.
* Second: Strengthen the monitoring and evaluation of all insurance companies to ensure strong confidence in the financial market and high professional marketing operations.
* Third: Promote the development of the insurance sector by strengthening and expanding cooperation with all relevant institutions, both domestic and foreign, especially promoting the implementation of compulsory insurance as defined in the laws and regulations in force.
* Fourth: Increase consumer protection by promoting dispute resolution mechanisms to build public confidence in insurance services in order to boost growth in the insurance market with great potential.
* Fifth: Study and make efforts to design insurance technology systems such as management technology and control technology to ensure the effectiveness of management, control and development of the insurance sector in Cambodia.
* Sixth: Strengthen the implementation of insurance and related regulations in force.
Seventh: Build and strengthen professional skills in the Cambodian insurance market, strive to develop new products to serve market demand, such as agricultural insurance products, disaster insurance products and women's insurance products.
* Eighth: Strengthen and improve customer service by ensuring professional and responsible service delivery, as well as for the sale of insurance products and customer compensation.
* 9th: Actively participate in the adoption, adaptation and innovation of insurance technology systems to promote the development of the insurance sector in Cambodia.
With the growth of the insurance industry, the size of the Cambodian insurance market will increase to about $ 332 million in 2022, contributing to the Cambodian economy at a rate of about 1.17% of GDP and insurance density of $ 20.53. Per person.
These two key indicators indicate that the Cambodian insurance market still has great potential for growth in the future, and also indicates that the Cambodian insurance market is still challenged by the lack of public awareness of the benefits of insurance that this factor requires. To disseminate and educate the public more about the content and benefits of insurance.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thuch Tou and his wife and six other children were evicted by Mr. Min Kimsan from the house where they used to live for 6 years because they did not have money to pay in installments. The loss of his home left Thuch Tou, his wife and children homeless and their children out of school.
In order to get a house where he used to live peacefully with his family, Mr. Thuch Tou sought the favor of Mr. Min Kimsan, the owner of the Borey and the relevant authorities, but to no avail.
The above story was narrated by Mr. Thuch Tou that in 2015 he went to buy a house in Borey Sen Monorom, which is the city of Mr. Min Kimsan. This Borey is located in Kantouk Cheung Village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Thuch Tou bought the house from the beginning, measuring 5 meters by 16 meters, with a floor height of about 27,000 US dollars. But he did not have all the money to pay, he paid 180 months in installments for $ 389.
After entering the house, due to the small size of the house, many family members, Mr. Thuch Tou, built two more floors for about $ 30,000.
Mr. Thuch Tou has already paid off the house for about 63 months, equivalent to about $ 25,407. However, this payment was canceled and failed to be paid in early 2021 due to the crisis caused by Kovid 19 disease, which caused Mr. Thuch Tou to lose his income and not be able to pay in installments.
Since then, the owner has filed a lawsuit to seize the house, not allowing Thuch Tou and his children to return to live in the house.
After receiving Samdech Techo Hun Sen's recommendation for negotiations between the Borey owners and home buyers to reduce the amount of the installment, Mr. Thuch Tou was very happy. He tried to negotiate with the landlord to reduce the amount of monthly installments and increase the payment period, but the landlord refused and continued to demand the confiscation of the house from him.
Mr. Thuch Tou respectfully requested the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, as well as the relevant authorities to intervene to facilitate this issue so that he can afford to pay more than $ 100 per month in installments. Can go back to live in his house.
Regarding the above case, Fresh News has not yet been able to seek confirmation from the owner of the Borey, Mr. Min Kimsan. Mr. Sok Lou thanked the people who voted for the CPP and thanked the team at all levels for their hard work.
