Cambodia receives $ 12 million in commercial gambling revenue, up nearly 16% in the first half of this year, but lower than planned
(Phnom Penh): In the first half of 2023, Cambodia earned about 12 million US dollars from commercial gambling, an increase of nearly 16% compared to the same period in 2022.
Ros Phirun, secretary-general of the Gambling Commission of Cambodia, told Fresh News that revenue collection from the gambling industry was still low and slow, with revenue collected for the first six months of this year. Only 29.6% of the national budget law, which requires the gambling industry to collect more than $ 42 million this year.
He hopes that in the second half of 2023, revenue from commercial gambling will increase after the influx of international tourists.
He said the commercial gambling sector lost almost all of its revenue during the 1940 epidemic and began to recover gradually, which he predicted would recover after 2024. From Cambodia, the implementation of the law governing all sectors of commercial gambling has been strengthened, which will increase revenue.
Mr. Ros Phirun also said that currently, the Royal Government has issued licenses to 181 companies in the field of commercial gambling, including 87 licenses to renew business licenses that meet the requirements, and the renewal of unlicensed licenses. Completion of 91 full conditions or provisional licenses and 3 new licenses granted to new start-ups.
Currently, the Royal Government has licensed and allowed only two types of gambling, including casino and lucky gambling. Separately, for electronic games, the Royal Government does not have a license or permission to operate in Cambodia.
