Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Holds Last Mediation Meeting with More Than 20 Families Invading Canadia Land
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration on the morning of July 28, 2023 held a coordination meeting with more than 20 families related to the illegal occupation of land by Canadia Company at Otrao point, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district. Sihanoukville Province.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led by Mr. Bou Vathana, Director of Inter-sectoral Management of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall, and cooperated with the competent authorities, representatives of the people and more than 10 out of 26 families participated in Sihanoukville Provincial Hall.
In the past, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has mediated and resolved this land dispute outside the court system, and as a result, about 85% of the people agreed to accept Canadia Bank's settlement policy by agreeing to accept the plot size of 5 meters by 20 meters. M and agree to dismantle other structures and stone fences from the above ground location voluntarily.
The people who agreed above, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration facilitated the paperwork to prepare for the registration of land titles on the plot of land provided by the bank. On June 08, 2023, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration organized a lottery ceremony and handed over the lottery numbers to the people who agreed with Canadia Bank's settlement policy. In particular, only about 20 families still do not agree to accept.
On behalf of the provincial administration as well as the relevant authorities are still trying to explain, guide, coordinate and continue to deal with the actual win-win policy, this morning, more than 10 families out of 26 families came to the meeting to listen to the guidance of professional officers of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration.
After researching the team found that the occupation of the people is the encroachment on the private land of others through a group of brokers who acted to seize the land to sell to the people. Other citizens at low prices. The brokers then collected money from the people who bought the land, claiming that the money was used to run land titles for the people.
For the group of brokers who carry out the above activities, the Land Dispute Research Team of Sihanoukville Provincial Police has already identified the target, including 3 people as follows:
According to the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, in the press release, the people were warned that if they continue to violate the law, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration will strictly enforce the law without exception for those who and the masterminds who try Incite to encroach on illegal land possession and bring them to justice.
