With Cambodia's vast experience and expertise in mine clearance and as a war-torn country, the Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has decided to send more than 8,000 peacekeepers under the auspices of the United Nations. Participate in ensuring the safety of people in nine countries around the world, including the Republic of Cyprus.
