(Phnom Penh): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) issued a statement on the election process of the 7th National Assembly on Sunday, July 23, 2023.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News on July 28, 2023, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia claimed that it had sent a total of 41,333 members to observe polling stations across 25 polling stations. Capital-province in the event of the 7th legislative election on Sunday, July 23, 2023 recently.
Based on the report received from its observers across the country, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia would like to evaluate the process of the 7th National Assembly election as follows:
* 1: During the election campaign: The 21-day election campaign was conducted in accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures of the election in force. All political parties contested the election campaign vigorously and smoothly under the atmosphere of security and good order, especially no cases of intimidation or violence were reported during the election campaign. .
* 3: Ballot Counting: The ballot counting process was conducted with the participation of all stakeholders, including agents of political parties, national and international observers, as well as various national and international media agencies. This reflects the transparency, accuracy and openness of the vote counting process in accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures in force related to the election.
