Discussions between Wang and Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan include the latest developments in Ukraine as well as the global financial system. The two foreign ministers also discussed the development of economic and trade relations between Turkey and China.
During the talks with Wang, Erdogan expressed hope that Turkey-China would strengthen their cooperation as the two countries play a key role in global and international affairs, the president's office said in a statement. Area.
Customs duties will be reduced step by step. According to the Ministry of Industry and Trade, the agreement will eliminate tariffs on at least 86% of Vietnamese products and 93% of Israeli products. The two countries are expected to increase bilateral trade from $ 2.2 billion last year to $ 3 billion in the near future.
The free trade agreement will help Vietnamese companies export goods and gain access to Israeli markets for goods and technology at more competitive prices. Vietnamese companies will also have easier access to other markets, such as the Middle East, North Africa or South Europe.
In return, Israeli companies will be able to gain access to ASEAN and the Indo-Pacific region, as well as other major economies to which Vietnam has signed free trade agreements.
The new free trade agreement is the first to be signed by a West Asian country with Vietnam. Israel is now the third largest export market and the fifth largest trading partner for Vietnam in West Asia. According to VN Express.
