Crude oil prices fell to more than $ 83 a barrel.
LONDON (Reuters) - Oil prices fell on Wednesday as investors watched a meeting of the US Federal Reserve, which is expected to raise interest rates amid rising US crude supplies.
Crude prices rose for four weeks as investors rushed to buy on signs of tighter supply, with output cut by the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC) and its allies, as well as promises by Chinese authorities. The world's second largest economy.
However, there are concerns about whether China, the world's second-largest oil consumer, will actually be able to increase support for stimulus policies.
Taiwan's weather bureau has issued strong winds and rain warnings for the southern part, including Kaohsiung, a major port city. More than 4,000 people were evacuated, mostly from the mountainous areas of southern and eastern Taiwan, with torrential rains of up to 0.7 meters in some areas and up to 1 meter of rain. Predicted.
All domestic flights were suspended and some international flights were canceled. Rail services between southern and eastern Taiwan were also closed. The typhoon cut off electricity to more than 15,700 families across Taiwan, but most were restored.
