Two companies from Korea and Japan interested in investing in cashew oil refinery in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): At least two companies from Korea and Japan are interested in setting up a cashew oil refinery in Cambodia.
Neak Oknha said that in order to build a bio-energy refinery from cashew shells, KIER may seek partners with Cambodian companies to process cashew nuts for export and to collect additional cashew shells from other refineries. As oil. In addition, the waste or charcoal left over from the refining will be processed into fertilizer.
He added that if the factory operates in Cambodia, it may need a large amount of cashew shells, as the plant may need to produce 2 tons per hour or 20 tons per day. However, the new technology needs to be recognized by both governments.
Uon Silot, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh News on July 26 that it is good news that Korean companies are interested in processing cashew products in Cambodia, especially the extraction of cashew oil.
He said that at present, Cambodia does not have the capacity to produce 5,000 tons to supply the Japanese company, while currently Cambodia can only produce 3,000 tons of cashew processing enterprises in Cambodia are small and small in size. No.
He said that in order to be able to produce and supply a large number of cashew shells, Cambodia must set up a processing plant and help local enterprises increase their processing to have more shells left to supply the refinery. That is why the Cambodian Cashew Association is trying to cooperate with SME banks to get capital for enterprises to expand their production even bigger.
According to the president of the Cambodian Cashew Association, the current price of cashew nuts in Cambodia is quite high, at $ 120 per ton. He added that when Cambodia can sell both shells and meat, it will encourage Cambodia to compete with neighboring countries.
He also said that a company from Singapore was currently negotiating to set up a semi-finished factory where local enterprises could sell semi-finished products to the company so that the company could produce finished products and export them. The company is a standard company. After the establishment of this Singaporean company in Cambodia, the production of cashew shells will increase.
According to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association, there are currently more than 700,000 hectares of cashew plantations in Cambodia. In 2021, the world production of raw cashew nuts was about 5 million tons, of which Cambodia produced 1,180,000 tons, accounting for 24% of total production, making Cambodia the largest producer of cashew nuts in the world. The world. In 2022, Cambodia produced 690,000 tons, second in the world.
