(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of July 26, 2023, delivered a special message regarding the process of organizing a new Council of Ministers. Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced his resignation as Prime Minister on August 22, 2023 and handed over to HE Hun Manet on the evening of August 22, 2023.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen will be appointed by the King to be the President of the Supreme Council of the King. Samdech Techo Hun Sen will be the President of the Senate to replace Samdech Say Chhum after the Senate election on February 25, 2024.
The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Okas to deliver a special message related to the process of organizing the new Cabinet:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will not continue as Prime Minister in the new term.
* Samdech Techo stated that the hasty resignation of the Prime Minister is a prelude to long-term stability, which is the foundation for development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the inauguration of Hun Manet as Prime Minister did not skip the procedures.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after Samdech resigned from the Royal Government, Samdech will be appointed by the King to be the President of the Supreme Council of the King.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Sar Kheng, Samdech Tea Banh and Samdech Men Sam An will also be appointed as the King's personal advisers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will also become the President of the Senate instead of Samdech Say Chhum after the Senate election on February 25, 2024.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not interfere in the work of Hun Manet as Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Hun Manet will become the Prime Minister in about three weeks.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the resignation of the Prime Minister is a great sacrifice to ensure the peace of the nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this resignation is in compliance with the royal example of King Norodom Sihanouk in the transfer of the throne.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the King will appoint His Excellency Hun Manet as Prime Minister on August 7 to form a new Council of Ministers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that on August 22, the National Assembly will convene under the chairmanship of the dean, and in the evening the Council of Ministers will be sworn in.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he will end his position as Prime Minister on August 22, 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that Dr. Hun Manet will be the Prime Minister on the evening of August 22, 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Hun Manet's inauguration as Prime Minister does not require any foreign support, only enough support from the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed confidence that Mr. Hun Manet will receive support from the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Hun Manet's becoming Prime Minister went through at least four stages: internal party unity, must be elected to the National Assembly through general elections, and be appointed by the King. Prepare the Royal Government and pass the approval by the National Assembly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested all ministers who could not continue to hold office, please understand and there must be a sacrifice.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the opposition for trying to insult Samdech and Mr. Hun Manet until the CPP received more than 82% of the people's support.
