(Siem Reap): The skill of preserving and repairing stone is another clear job among the many skills that are being done daily in helping to maintain, repair and protect ancient temples in the Angkor area.
A young expert, Mr. Sao Rattanak, who is working on repairing stone carvings of dragon recipes at Banteay Samre temple, considers that the skill of preserving and repairing stone treatment requires the utmost patience, if not patience, it is not only It is not possible to preserve and repair the damaged ancient stone, and it turns into the destruction of ancient stone or sculpture.
Mr. Sao Rattanak, 29 years old, is a former trainee who attended the training course "Stone Conservation Skills" under the cooperation between APSARA Authority with the Stone Conservation Group and GIZ from 2013 to 2015 and is a native of Siem Reap. That the work of conserving and repairing the stone encounters many difficulties, including assembling the stone, treating the stone, and cleaning the stone, because some stones have decay on the stone, which requires great care.
Properly covered, it will withstand a great deal of adverse conditions. In addition, at the temple repair sites, some sites are so small that it is not possible to take tools to help, especially lifting heavy stones. Therefore, patience and attention as a result of the best results are the only motivators that can motivate the work to help the archeology to be strong again.
At present, there are still a small number of experts in the field of conservation and restoration of ancient temples in Cambodia. APSARA Authority is cooperating with GIZ Germany in training this skill on the next generation of Cambodian children in order to increase the human resources in this field in the near future. Sihanoukville Administration Destroys Many Illegal Electronic Games After Crackdown
