The Ministry of Economy recommends the implementation of VAT for the business of importing or distributing cigarettes from August 1.
According to the instructions, in order to strengthen the implementation of VAT for transparency and consistency, the Ministry of Economy and Finance would like to advise all business owners who import or distribute cigarettes about the procedures for applying tax. On the following value-added:
1. For cigarettes imported for domestic sales purposes, the enterprise shall apply VAT like other taxed import goods by collecting VAT at the rate of 10 (ten) percent for all cigarette supply in Cambodia. Value added tax paid at the time of importation or domestic purchase is allowed as a credit on the import tax deductible with the export tax.
3. The enterprise must file a declaration and pay tax in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance sincerely hopes that all enterprises engaged in the business of importing or distributing cigarettes will pay close attention to the effective implementation of the guidelines. This instruction is effective from August 1, 2023 onwards. Cambodia Informal Entertainment and Support Services Association issues statement in support of the process and preliminary results for the 7th National Assembly election
