The following are the ASEAN member countries that have general elections to elect leaders:
2. Philippines The first elections were held in 1935.
3. Cambodia had its first elections in 1946 but has been suspended since the war in 1970. It was not until 1993 that elections were held until today.
4. Myanmar The first elections were held in 1947 after secession from India and independence from Britain.
5. Singapore First elections were held in 1948.
6. Malaysia The first elections were held in 1955.
7. Indonesia The first elections were held in 1955.
