(Siem Reap): Phnom Kulen is a historical and natural tourist attraction for tourists. Previously, climbing Kulen Mountain was possible only on the side of Banteay Srei with the red gravel road, while in the upper part of Svay, it is not possible to climb on Kulen Mountain.
On Phnom Kulen, there are also many people living. The people living on Phnom Kulen are under the administration of Svay Leu district. Apart from that there is no way to go down to Svay Leu district and that on that mountain, they also have no way to travel.
People on this mountain, if they have to go down from the mountain to seek various services from the Svay Leu district authority, are required to travel down to Banteay Srei district and travel to Svay Leu district, which is nearly 100 kilometers away. This road problem has made it very difficult for people to live and earn a living.
Not only the people, the officials who have to go up to solve problems or provide other services are also difficult because they have to drive far.
Mr. Horn Hon, a resident of Phnom Kulen, described that since he came to the top of Phnom Kulen, there has never been a road to travel and to go down to Svay Leu district. People want to go down to Svay Leu district is able to travel on foot for a long time. If you buy groceries or consumables, only carry or pile.
Seeing the hardships of the people on Phnom Kulen like this, the Royal Government decided to build a concrete road for people to travel. Construction of the road began in 2017. This concrete road was built from the town of Svay Leu district up to the mountain and through the village of the people. Currently, this concrete road was built to Preah Ang Thom on the ridge of Phnom Kulen, which is about 23 kilometers long.
According to the Royal Government's plan, this road is planned to be built from Preah Ang Thom down to Banteay Srei district as well. After the road is built, people will no longer face difficulties. In addition to the construction of the concrete road, the authorities also run the electricity network for the people in the mountains to use.
The people of Phnom Kulen, who used to suffer because there is no road to travel, expressed their happiness after having a road to travel up and down the mountain quickly.
After the concrete road connecting Svay Leu town to the mountain, Phnom Kulen is not as calm as before. People at the foot of the mountain as well as tourists from near and far often visit Phnom Kulen.
Along with the easy access road, the people also requested the Royal Government to check the money taken to visit Phnom Kulen by Nokor Kork Thlok Company of Duke Sieng Nam.
The Nokor Kork Thlok company of Duke Seang Nam has been setting up checkpoints to take money from people who go to visit Kulen Mountain for many years. In the past, the company only set up checkpoints on the road from Banteay Srei district, but now the company has also set up checkpoints on the concrete road from Svay Leu district.
Many tourists climbing Mount Kulen mistakenly believe that the ticket price was taken in exchange for the construction of a concrete road. Mr. Sat Pov, Governor of Svay Leu District, pointed out that the concrete road is a project of the Royal Government to build for people to travel without having to pay for crossing.
According to the staff, the ticket price for admission to Phnom Kulen resort for foreigners is $ 20 per person. Separately, Cambodians pay 5,000 riel for a car, 3,000 riel for a family car and 1,500 riel for a motorcycle.
People do not seem very happy with the money and request the Royal Government to adjust the money. Unhappy because the company has set up checkpoints on the transit route, so some passengers just pass through the mountain also have to pay, even if they do not visit the Phnom Kulen resort.
