Please be informed that the third ring road is an important road to reduce traffic congestion and facilitate traffic in Phnom Penh, on the other hand, is the internal connection and integration of special areas connecting ASEAN Highway and Economic Corridor. The Greater Mekong Subregion is important in facilitating cross-border transportation, promoting international trade, and turning the land on either side of the ring road into a development zone.
The construction of the third ring road, nearly 53 kilometers long, passing through Phnom Penh and Kandal province was opened on January 14, 2019. The groundbreaking ceremony for the important transportation and travel of Cambodians was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Wang Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
This road has a width of up to 27 meters for the city, for out of town, the width of the road is 25 meters. This road has street lights for urban roads and ornamental trees for suburban roads.
The third ring road has four flyovers (crossing National Roads 4, 3, 2 and 21) with a total length of 1,000 meters. Construction of 2 bridges across the Bassac River at Anlong Chen Island with a total length of 996 meters (including the 630-meter-long East Bassac Bridge and the 366-meter-long West Bassac Bridge). Construction of 6 medium and short bridges and 113 sewers of all kinds.
The road will cost a total of 273 million US dollars, which is a concessional financing from the Chinese government, and the Royal Government of Cambodia contributes to the impact of demining and unexploded ordnance, taxes and royalties.
