Chinese high-level delegation to visit North Korea this week
SEOUL, July 24 (Xinhua) - A high-level Chinese delegation will travel to North Korea this week for a visit, the North's official KCNA news agency reported on Monday. Recognized for the first time since Pyongyang closed its borders to prevent the spread of Kovid-19. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, July 24, 2023.
North Korea closed its borders in early 2020 for all trade and diplomatic exchanges, even with its main economic and political ally, China.
The agency said Li, who is also vice chairman of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, will visit North Korea to "attend the commemoration of the 70th anniversary of the victory of the Great Patriotic War." Great. ”
North Korea refers to July 27, 1953, the date when the ceasefire ended the Korean War was signed as Victory Day. Many events are expected to mark the 70th anniversary this year.
It should be noted that technically, North and South Korea are still at war because the fraternal countries do not have a peace agreement with each other. North Korea last week detained a US soldier who had illegally crossed the inter-Korean border, putting Washington in a new diplomatic standoff with the nuclear-armed state.
