ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Delegation (AIPA) issues statement that successful Cambodian elections allow Cambodians to exercise their civil and political rights
(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Delegation (AIPA) issued a statement on the 7th National Assembly Election in Cambodia after observing this year's National Assembly Election in Cambodia on the 23rd. July 2023.
The purpose of this statement is to provide an overview of election observation activities throughout the election process. The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Delegation (AIPA) commends and commends the Government of Cambodia and the Cambodian people for their commitment to democratic principles and their efforts in organizing and administering this electoral process.
This statement was made on the basis of direct participation to assess the information provided in the pre-election briefing session and the facts reflected on a case-by-case basis. Observations were made on the entire voting process, including the opening and closing of polling stations and then the counting process.
The statement added that the presence of election officials, party agents and local observers helped maintain transparency and accountability throughout the voting and counting process. The NEC has played an important role in ensuring an effective election process. The delegation was very impressed to see the release of preliminary results on time, which enables stakeholders both inside and outside the country to monitor the progress of the election.
The delegation concluded that the 2023 National Assembly elections in Cambodia were successfully held, allowing the Cambodian people to exercise their civil and political rights through universal and secret suffrage, governed by national and international law.
