Private doctor escapes after injecting 5-year-old girl
(Kampong Chhnang): A 5-year-old girl died of seizures immediately after the local doctor gave her two injections because she had a cough and a slight fever.
The victim, 5-year-old Kim Chantey, lives in Chambok Prasat village, Krang Ska commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province. She died after her parents took her to a private doctor's house in Phum Plou Ko, Banteay Preal commune, Rolea Bier district.
Mr. Yim Sophal, Deputy Inspector of Criminal Planning of Rolea Bier District Police Inspectorate, told Fresh News on the afternoon of July 24, 2023 that this case occurred since the evening of July 22, 2023, he just received information at This morning, July 24, 2023, because the parents of the victims just reported to the administrative post on the evening of July 23.
He added that in connection with the above, according to the information he received, the girl's parents initially took the girl to the home of a private doctor named Ho Thong, a 45-year-old female resident. Phum Plou Kor village, Banteay Preal commune, Rolea Bier district.
After the doctor injected two needles into both of the girl's thighs, she immediately developed blood clots when she saw them, so the doctor gave her a serum and asked her parents to take her. The victim was taken to the Provincial Referral Hospital for emergency treatment.
He added that the medical examination showed that this private doctor had been receiving treatment at the local level for many years without the permission of the Department or the Ministry of Health, and had not undergone any training. The medical profession.
So far, the doctor escaped from the base this morning, not knowing where he went into hiding, the authorities are continuing to investigate, but this case, he is building a case. Procedural referral story.
Prak Von, director of the Kampong Chhnang provincial health department, also told Fresh New News that he had just received the information this morning and would investigate it carefully. If it is found that the doctor does not have a medical certificate, it is a medical professional error, so not only the victim is the complainant, even the health department can have the right to sue the above person. Also.
