On that occasion, Akka Moha Upasika, a Buddhist supporter, also dedicated this great merit to the seven ancestors, especially Akka Moha Upasika, a Buddhist supporter, Nhan Leng, please accept and enjoy in good health, do not be greedy.
Please note that 6 pagodas also received facilities, including construction suffixes, including: Wat Chambey, Wat Champa, Wat Kampong Tralach, Leu Wat, Krong, Wat Chao Fa Chuon, Wat Prob Phcha, (Serey Techea). Each pagoda received rice, noodles, fish, drinks, pure water and other facilities, along with four suffixes, donated 120,000 riels, construction suffix 60,000 riels. To more than 10 grandparents, each of whom received 20,000 Riels.
The Cambodian People's Network Association issued a statement stating that the 7th National Assembly election was smooth, fair, transparent, free and fair.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian People's Network Association (LNFA) on July 24, 2023, issued a statement on the 7th National Assembly Election, which was conducted smoothly, correctly, transparently, freely and fairly. Good order.
In a statement, the Cambodian People's Network Association stated that in the process of the 7th National Assembly election on July 23, 2023, with the permission of the National Election Committee (NEC). The Cambodian People's Network Association (LNFA) has sent staff to participate in election observation as national observers at polling stations and polling stations in the capitals / provinces.
The Cambodian People's Network Association said that on the basis of independence, democracy and neutrality, the national observers of the Cambodian People's Network Association observed:
1. In the 7th National Assembly election in 2023, 18 political parties competed. Voters cast their ballots freely, with happy faces and willing to support their favorite political party through ballots.
2. The general atmosphere, both before and on election day, was calm, free of coercion and violence. In addition, the counting of ballots went smoothly, with the participation and scrutiny of national / international observers and observers of political parties in a responsible and professional manner.
3. According to preliminary figures, about 8,213,260 Cambodians, or 84.58%, cast their ballots, the highest number in many democracies around the world. This figure confirms that Cambodians have the political maturity and awareness to vote in order to express their will and choose the leaders of their favorite and confident countries.
(Phnom Penh): The Association of Environmental and Social Lovers on July 24, 2023 issued a statement supporting and accepting the preliminary results of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 on the basis of independence, democracy and neutrality. .
Through a nationwide review, the Association of Environmental and Social Lovers would like to express its appreciation for this smooth, accurate, transparent, free and fair election process and declare our support for the electoral process. By the NEC Which is an independent institution from the initial stage to the announcement of election results.
At the same time, the Association of Environmental and Social Lovers would like to congratulate the Cambodian People's Party, which was overwhelmingly voted by the people throughout the country to win 120 seats in the National Assembly of the 7th legislature to form the Royal Government to lead the country for 5 years. Next year.
(Phnom Penh): A group of civil society organizations, including a network of associations, issued a joint statement on July 24, 2023, expressing its full support for the election results for the 7th legislature 2023 organized by the National Committee. The National Election Commission (NEC) announced the provisional results on the evening of July 23, 2023, which shows that the Cambodian People's Party is proud to receive an overwhelming majority of votes.
Through the joint statement, civil society organizations observed: "The process as well as the announcement of the results is really transparent, free, fair, just, true democracy, there is no coercion, oppression, intimidation, all Cambodians go to the polls. With a smiling face, satisfied and happy together.
The CSOs stated that in order to maintain this great value, the CSOs, including the youth network, would like to express their support for the results announced by the National Election Committee (NEC) and would like to join in the celebration as well. Satisfied with the Cambodian People's Party, which received overwhelming support from the Cambodian people across the country on this national election.
