ASEAN Secretary-General Delegates Assess Cambodia Elections Peacefully, Orderly and Non-Violent
(Phnom Penh): After the successful completion of the mission to observe the 7th National Assembly Election 2020 in Cambodia from 21 to 23 July 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, ASEAN Secretariat and the ASEAN Secretariat Delegation Assess overall that the election process was peaceful, orderly and non-violent.
In addition, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also released a message through the website of the ASEAN Secretariat as follows:
During the mission, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn and officials from the ASEAN Secretariat observed key events in the election process, including the election campaign, the opening and closing of polling stations and the polling stations.
On 21 July, the last day of the election campaign, the ASEAN Secretariat team observed the campaign by various political parties in Khan Chamkar Mon, Khan Meanchey and Khan Sen Sok. Despite the scattering of rain, the people who participated in the election campaign expressed their excitement, and the political parties that organized and marched the election pointed out the democratic space that was given to all parties.
For the 2023 multi-party election, 18 political parties are vying for 125 seats in Cambodia's lower house of parliament. According to the National Election Committee, there are 9.7 million registered voters for this election, and according to preliminary results from the National Election Committee, the turnout was high. 84.58% across 23,789 polling stations nationwide.
This is the sixth election observation mission that the ASEAN Secretariat has responded to at the request of ASEAN Member States and dialogue partners. ASEAN fully respects the sovereignty, political independence and territorial integrity of ASEAN member countries.
