Representatives of the Central Asia-Pacific Democrats International (CAPDI) delegation confirmed that international observers were on hand to carry out their work diligently. On election day, July 23, 2023, observers observed that the polling stations were open from 7:00 am and that there were sufficient election materials and that the election officials were performing their duties professionally.
CAPDI further stated that the election process was conducted in accordance with the law in force and adhered to the principles of open democracy for the people to exercise their rights.
CAPDI notes that verifying voters with voter ID cards is an important way to avoid identity fraud. On the other hand, the use of some public places as polling stations, such as schools, pagodas, is also a saving for the election.
Representatives of the International Conference of Asian Political Parties (ICAPP) confirmed that after the closure of the polling station at 3 pm, it was observed that the election officials carried out the most careful vote counting under observation by National / international observers, representatives of political parties, national / international journalists, etc.
