On Facebook, on July 23, 2023, Mr. Sok Phea, Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party in Oral District, stated, "Out of compassion, I led the team to visit her at home and Take an ambulance (donated by Tycoon Ly Yong Phat) to take her to the Kampong Speu Provincial Referral Hospital and cover all medical expenses.
Through the voicemail on the evening of July 23, 2023, after the election closed, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the results of the turnout of the 7th National Assembly election today with the provisional results. 8,177,053 people, equivalent to 84.21% of the registered voters, went to the polls, which is a significant increase compared to the 2022 and 2018 elections.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "At this point, we can conclude that the people have clearly participated in the democratic movement in Cambodia. The people really want peace and prosperity with the roof of peace that we have and want to leave. "Far from extremist groups, which they have always destroyed."
With reference to the provisional results, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the activities of the opposition group that obstructed the election and destroyed the ballots by drawing a cross as they organized a telegram group to take a cross-section photo. Lottery sent to Mr. Sam Rainsy, who took this issue as a challenge.
"Now we are waiting to see how many ballots are crossed, because the leaders of the extremist group have made it clear that which ballots are the ballots that support them, so there are ballots," he said. How many ballots are crossed and the ballots are invalid or the ballots are usually considered as a percentage.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen scolded the opposition, which operated in a telegram called "Sabai Sabay", which marked the ballot and sent it to its boss in Paris. Samdech confirmed that Samdech already knew those identities in the country, but Samdech asked not to be afraid
"You can come out and confess with the authorities, with the NEC, especially with the authorities, because the movement to destroy the ballot is a crime that must be punished. Please wake up and confess with the authorities," he said. "In the nearest place, otherwise legal action will be taken."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that the NEC will distinguish between invalid ballots and cross ballots. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers that those who went to the polls supported the call of the King, the Royal Government and the NEC. Samdech also thanked the people who went to the polls.
