Greek authorities say more than 19,000 people have been evacuated, including more than 16,000 by land and more than 3,000 by sea to other islands. It describes it as "the largest wildfire evacuation ever" in Greek history.
However, no casualties have been reported so far.
In the meeting to disseminate the 7th National Assembly Election on the evening of July 23, 2023, President Prach Chan thanked the people who participated in the 7th National Assembly Election as the results Preliminary nationwide estimates put the turnout at 84.58 percent of the nearly 10 million registered voters.
Mr. Prach Chan said, "I call on all parties concerned to remain silent to create a good atmosphere after the election and wait for the official election results released by the NEC."
NEC Chairman: The 7th National Assembly Election Process was Successful and in a Quiet, No Violence and No Threat (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC) On July 23, 2023, it was confirmed that the election process for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023 was successful and in a calm environment with security, safety and public order.
This statement was made during a meeting with stakeholders on the summary of general events of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023. This meeting was held at the National Institute of Education on July 23, 2023.
He said that even before the election day, there were cases of heavy rain and fires that caused damage to some election materials, the election went smoothly.
Mr. Prach Chan stated that "With the good cooperation of the mechanisms and structures of electoral security at all levels with the NEC and the Election Commission at all levels, the election process was successful and in the atmosphere. "Calm, safe, secure and public order, no violence, no threats."
Regarding the election security situation, the Permanent Security Command of the Election and the NEC have issued joint guidelines on the activities and organization of election security agencies in the campaign to protect the election process for the 7th legislative election in 2023 to control The situation will ensure that the election runs smoothly and safely and securely.
In the process of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, the NEC recognized and issued certificates to many national and international observers, including: National observers, a total of 89,562 from 134 non-governmental organizations Yes, the government and international observers total 604 from 61 institutions. In addition to election observers, political party agents and many national and international journalists also participated in monitoring the election process.
"For this election, we have spent a lot of money, a total of about $ 50 million," he said.
He said that considering the people on the NEC voter list, a total of nearly 10 million people, it can be said that can pay for each citizen about 20,000 riel.
Mr. Tep Nytha added that the NEC's main expenditures were on election equipment, more than half, and nearly half on the salaries of more than 150,000 election officials. There are more than 140,000 short-term election officials, while more than 10,000 NEC officials at the national and capital / provincial levels are working for a long period of 3-8 months.
90 national and 7 international observers hold a press conference to present the results of the general observation of the election process in the constituencies and their general conclusions
(Phnom Penh): The Civil Society Coalition Forum said that 90 national observers and 7 international observers will hold a press conference to present the results of the general observation of the election process at the polling stations. And their general conclusions.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News. Coordinated the work of 360 national observers from 90 NGOs and national associations (for 25 capitals and provinces) and 56 international observers from 7 institutions (10 countries) to observe the election process. Appointment of the 7th legislature, which will take place on Sunday, July 23, 2023.
Following the completion of the election observation on July 23, 2023, the 90 national observers and the seven international observers will hold a press conference to present the results of the general observation of the election process at the polling stations and their conclusions. General of national and international observers.
According to reports from national and international observers, the Civil Society Forum has made seven preliminary conclusions:
1: The overall situation of the 7th National Assembly election process was conducted in a good, calm atmosphere and there was no significant disturbance or violence.
2. The people who went to the polls exercised their right to vote in large numbers, with joy and fearlessness.
3: NEC polling station officials Performed roles and responsibilities with high responsibility, accuracy, transparency and professionalism.
4. At the polling stations, national and international observers, including agents of political parties, participated in monitoring the election process from the opening of the polling stations to the closing of the vote count.
5: So far, there are no irregularities or inactivity or any complaints that occur at the polling station.
6. The situation of the process of the 7th National Assembly election in 2023 was smooth, free, transparent and without any disturbance or coercion.
7: Overall, the success of the 7th National Assembly election shows that the NEC. Maturity and authority in managing the election process in the Kingdom of Cambodia to ensure independence, sovereignty, transparency and fairness, professionalism and non-political bias.
