Arrested a young man and sent him to the police after he found a photo of a ballot with a cross in his mobile phone
(Phnom Penh): Officials of the National Election Committee (NEC) on the morning of July 23 arrested a young man and sent him to the Stung Meanchey II Police Administration Post after he took a photo of the ballot box. See a cross.
The suspect who crossed the ballot and was found in the phone by NEC officials was Sat Oun, male, 35 years old, living at No. 9, Concrete Street, Group 9, Prek Toal 1 Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey II, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh (Election number 389).
According to a source from the NEC official, the suspect, Sat Oun, went to the polling station 0804 in a secret room and recorded the ballot in his mobile phone at 9:30 AM. At that time, the head of the 0804 office, who was a suspect, asked to check the mobile phone that he took in the secret room, also saw the picture of the ballot box marked in the mobile phone and arrested the suspect.
The suspect is currently being detained by the National Election Committee (NEC) and sent to the Stung Meanchey II Police Administration Post to continue the proceedings. Ms. Nhem Morakot leads 325 blind people to vote at Kork Roka Primary School in Kork Roka Sangkat, Khan Prek Pnov
