Mr. Mak Horn said this after he and his family participated in the election of the 7th legislature on July 23.
He spent days traveling tens of thousands of miles to vote in his homeland, volunteering. "The ballots I cast in the ballot box are for peace," he said.
He saw that the election was 100% acceptable, although they adhered to the principle of first come, first served, but also favored the elderly, the disabled, pregnant women, etc., which he was satisfied with. Seriously.
It is up to each individual to decide whether this election is fair or not, but for him it is understood that it is in accordance with the law, he likened it to applying for a contest. An exam, when the conditions are set, this document, that document, and the candidate does not meet the requirements, the committee can not accept the candidate to participate in the competition. Mr. Mak Horn added that.
He added that if the party we love does not participate in the election in this term, we can also vote for another party to fulfill their duties as citizens and wait for the next term, the party we love can stand and wait for us to vote for that party. There is nothing wrong with that. He likened it to wanting to eat soup so that if we do not stir or hit the ingredients, we can also eat dried fish and smoked fish.
He was upset because he regretted that when he was abroad, people only heard that Cambodia was brutal, the people were ignorant, but when they arrived in their homeland, it was obvious that it was not like the accusations made by foreign politicians. . That is why he still misunderstands the past.
He does not support those foreign politicians who are still obstructing and inciting the people not to go to the polls, if they go to the polls, they will have to cross out, which is an act of inhumane and inspiring destruction.
He added that in 1979, Cambodia was almost reduced to ashes, and after his return to his homeland, he was overjoyed, not realizing that Cambodia during the war had become a prosperous Cambodia. Development is not like now and I believe that development will continue as long as there is peace.
