Mr. Itthiphon Bunprakong thanked Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, for inviting the Thai delegation to observe the 7th National Assembly election. He added that this is the first time for him as chairman of the NEC of the Kingdom of Thailand to visit abroad, the Kingdom of Cambodia, which has close ties and is a member of ASEAN. He felt happier than going to European countries.
Mr. Prach Chan, President of the NEC, welcomed Mr. Itthiphon Bunprakhong and all his colleagues who were interested in the Kingdom of Cambodia and came to observe the 7th National Assembly election.
Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, further informed that in general, the election process has four stages, and HE also briefly explained each stage of the election process:
• Voter List and Voter Registration Stage
• Registration of political parties and lists of candidates
• Election campaign phase
Voting phase, counting ballots, allocating seats and announcing election results.
Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, further informed that the election in Cambodia is organized to participate in recommending the rules and procedures of the election from all stakeholders, including political parties, non-governmental organizations. And election-related institutions.
Regarding the preparation of election materials, Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, said that the election materials had been delivered to the destination. Some areas have to be transported by air, others have to be transported by elephants due to heavy rains, difficult roads and more water.
Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, further stated that the NEC shall exercise its powers independently based on the laws in force as stipulated in the Constitution, the Law on Elections, including the rules and procedures for elections. .
After listening to the speech of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, Mr. It Thiphon Bunprakhong expressed his deep gratitude for the information received at this time about the history of the election in the Kingdom of Cambodia and the process of organizing. Election of the 7th legislature.
