US to provide $ 400 million in military aid to Ukraine
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States plans to make an announcement as soon as next Tuesday on a new $ 400 million military aid package for Ukraine, US officials said Friday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, July 22, 2023.
Washington provided Ukraine with 155mm DPICM cluster munitions fired from the Howitzer artillery system in July. The package will be the 43rd package the United States has approved for Ukraine since the Russian invasion, which began in February 2022, with a total value of more than $ 41 billion.
