Residents of Kirivong District, Takeo Province Celebrate the Achievement of Precious Memories "Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Kirivong Cultural Park"
This public park was built on the initiative of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An and was built under the direct efforts and coordination of Mr. Sok Sokan on behalf of the family of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An.
This cultural park was built using sediment reclaimed from the lake in order to increase the amount of water stored in the lake, reduce the risk of water shortage in the dry season, reduce flooding in the rainy season and for Serve the public, especially the people of Takeo and Kirivong districts.
This cultural park is located along National Road 2 next to the Tonle Sap Reservoir in Kampong Village, Preah Bat Choan Chum Commune, Kirivong District, Takeo Province. The park was started in 2020 and is currently under construction and will be completed in the near future. Please note that a library building will also be built in the next step.
The people of Kirivong district, as well as the whole of Takeo province, expressed their happiness and admiration for the presence of this new cultural park.
This achievement will help to enhance the beauty of Kirivong district, especially to attract national and international tourists, which will improve the family economy of local people, strengthen the bonds of solidarity and communication between people and people. People, as well as contribute to the promotion of public welfare, protection of the environment and nature, as well as promote the preservation and dissemination of Khmer culture more widely.
