Watch the interview with Mr. Dim Sovannarom as follows: What is the current mindset of young people about the development of Cambodia?
(Phnom Penh): The mindset of the youth has changed from generation to generation depending on the first: education, the second: technology and the third, the support of the government leaders of each country. More than 30 years ago, most people lacked knowledge due to war, political stalemate, and a number of social issues that left them lacking in all decisions on development work in Cambodia.
But so far, people, especially the younger generation, have made positive changes and become more involved in social work and development in Cambodia through direct involvement with the government or participation in the private sector to develop Cambodia.
If we look at the structure of the Cambodian labor force, there are about 200,000 young people every year, a new labor force added to the labor market or the total Cambodian labor force. Some of the most energetic young people are looking for jobs in the city, some are migrating abroad, some are learning technical skills, and some have the opportunity to pursue higher education. But their desire is to have a job with a decent income to support themselves and their families.
About 6 million young people in Cambodia aspire to decent work that comes from sustainable economic development. The group of young people between the ages of 15 and 35 have a different mindset from their parents who were brave and dared to take action to support development in Cambodia, often referred to as the new generation. .
Some are called the new generation because, firstly, they grow old in a time of peace and stability, secondly, they live because of regular elections, and thirdly, they live because of strong economic growth and structural changes. Work fast.
Estimates by development agencies in Cambodia show that the current poverty rate has dropped below 10% through youth employment in the garment, construction and tourism sectors.
However, what the government is doing now is gradually responding to the aspirations of young people that they need not only the right to life, but also the right to progress and a quality of life. Dignity and his heart.
All of these issues have led the Royal Government of Cambodia to develop policies to support youth employment, such as industrial development policies, national employment policies, and migrant workers' policies. And all policies aim to increase the capacity of youth and provide opportunities for all youth to get jobs, education and participate in development activities in the national employment community to boost their family economies.
In addition, the Cambodian Constitution also gives every Cambodian youth the right to stand for election and the right to go to the polls to elect their preferred representatives in accordance with their aspirations for a decent and sustainable job creation process in the future. This. Currently, the Cambodian population between the ages of 15 and 40 accounts for almost half of the total Cambodian population.
Responding to this young people's mindset, Transparency International Cambodia's study in 2022 found that the aspirations of Cambodian youth expect public service delivery to improve in the next five years. First: 43% of young people believe Second, 40% of young people think that the poverty rate will go down and thirdly, 38% of young people think that the quality of education will improve.
By: An Sithav, President of ACLEDA Bank: Although the election is approaching, there are no rush to withdraw money from the bank like in the 2013 election, as deposits in the banking system increased by more than 8%, showing confidence in the political and economic stability of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The 7th National Assembly election will be held on July 23, 2023 tomorrow, as the election approaches, it is observed that no people rush to withdraw money from banks like before During the election 10 years ago.
Since the election campaign began on July 1, 2023, business and investment activities have been normal.
He said that in the previous election, people were very worried, in fact, the election in 2013, the deposit decreased, the election in 2018, the deposit did not decrease, did not increase, that is, remain stable.
Dr. In Channy stated, "For the 2023 election, no one is afraid to withdraw money from the bank, not only the growth of deposits has increased and increased to a greater extent. "Savings are an important basis for measuring the credibility of the banking and financial sector during national elections, which shows that the public trusts the banking sector."
From January to June 2023, deposits amounted to 6,747 million US dollars, an increase of 8.75 percent, a figure that shows the strength and confidence of the people in the banking sector.
