BEIJING, July 20 (Xinhua) - Xi Jinping, secretary-general of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) and chairman of the CPC Central Military Commission, presided over the second meeting of the CPC Central Committee on Tuesday. To study the protection and processing of farmland, use of saline and alkaline soils and other issues.
Xi Jinping emphasized that food security is a top priority of the state and that farmland is the foundation of food production, so it is important to increase the protection of farmland, fully enhance the quality of farmland and pave the way for agricultural production. Promote the diversified production capacity of the agricultural sector.
The meeting stressed that at least 120 million hectares of farmland must be guaranteed, developed into modern farmland, actively developing all types of non-traditional farmland and actively increasing scientific research and development. Technology and production investment.
