Under the vision of the country must be protected, the people must be served, the law must be obeyed, crime must be suppressed, General Sao Sokha has fully contributed to peace and stability in the turning point of Cambodia's political history from July 21, 1978 to July 21, 2023 is only 45 years old.
Born in November 1961, Sao Sokha was born in Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province, to a father named Sao Saing and a mother named Kong Sovann, as well as five siblings (he was the eldest). Unfortunately, his mother, father, three younger siblings died during the Khmer Rouge regime, and one sister died of a disease in 1972, leaving Sao Sokha in shock and grief, becoming an orphan living alone.
Education History From 1981 to 1983, Sao Sokha was assigned to train in political science and public administration in Vietnam. In 1985, he was sent to study in the Soviet Union for political science and public administration training. Another 2 years.
From 1983 to 1989, he was the director of the Department of Youth in the Army of the Commissioner of Political Affairs, from 1989 to 1991, the Deputy Commissioner of the Political Commissioner, from 1991 to 1993, the Chief of the Joint Forces of the Cambodian Armed Forces. In Kampong Thom province, from 1993 to 1999, he was the Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie.
In 1999, Brigadier General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie, was promoted to the rank of Major General and promoted to the position of Commander of the National Gendarmerie, prompting the development of the Gendarmerie. It is an important force in contributing to the protection of territorial integrity, peacekeeping, security, public order and social security under the General Guide of the Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
General Sao Sokha is also a strong symbol for the campaign to crack down on encroachment and destruction of natural resources and actively participate in the suppression of all crimes, strengthen law enforcement, rescue in the event of a disaster. At the same time, participated in promoting arts, culture, sports and the spirit of philanthropic activities, contributing to social work, etc.
In addition, General Sao Sokha always ordered the commanders of all units and capitals-provinces to pay attention and implement 7 points, including: food, clothing, accommodation, health, education, transportation, entertainment. And solve difficulties, praise and encourage.
General Sao Sokha is a Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, a Senior Officer of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, who has sacrificed his life, energy and life. Life stage for loyal forces under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
