(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mai Hong Sreang, a former member of the Committee of Directors of the Candlelight Party, came out to reject Mr. Sam An's claim, accusing him of arresting Mr. Eng Sroy and Ms. Vong Runny to force them to surrender to the CPP.
Mr. May Hong Sreang made this statement in response to Mr. Oum Sam An, a former CNRP lawmaker, who wrote on his Facebook page that the arrest of Mr. Eng Sroy, Executive Director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Candlelight Party, and Ms. Vong Runny, president of the National Women's Movement of the Candlelight Party, is to force them to surrender to the CPP by preparing a draft letter of surrender.
Through a live broadcast on his social network at 9 o'clock on July 21, 2023, Mr. Mai Hong Sreang claimed that the Cambodian People's Party led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has never made a letter to force anyone Including Ms. Vong Runny, President of the National Women's Movement, the Candlelight Party, unlike what Mr. Sam Sam An mentioned.
The arrest of the two individuals, Mr. Mai Hong Sreang said, was carried out in accordance with a court order related to incitement to cause serious chaos and social security, that is, made with good reason, not arbitrary arrest. That no.
It should be noted that the Executive Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Candlelight Party and the President of the National Candlelight Party Women's Movement were ordered by Ms. Yi Sok Vouch, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on July 19, 2023. .
On July 17, 2023, Phnom Penh authorities arrested two members of the Candlelight Party in accordance with a court order in connection with the election riots.
Pursuant to the new Article 142, the Law on the Amendment of the Election Law, which came into force on July 4, 2023, states that inciting, harassing or preventing people from going to the polls or destroying ballots is a crime. . This offense is fined from 5 million to 20 million riels, regardless of other criminal penalties.
