The estimate comes ahead of next week's closely monitored Bank of Japan policy meeting, when the council will formulate its new quarterly forecast and discuss whether the economy will recover. Is making progress in achieving its sustainable 2% inflation target.
In a mid-year review of its forecast, the Japanese government expects the economy to grow 1.3 percent in the current fiscal year ending March 2024, down from the 1.5 percent forecast in March. January due to declining exports caused by declining global demand.
But the government also expects strong spending and capital expenditures to boost growth, forecasting 1.2 percent growth in fiscal 2024. According to Reuters.
Heavy rain and gusts of up to 150 mm are expected in parts of Beijing and Hebei from Thursday to Sunday, with heavy rain and thunderstorms expected, Chinese media reported on Thursday. Floods are expected to hit the Hai River basin in the next three days.
The Ministry of Water Resources has been preparing a reservoir to prevent flooding from the mountains caused by heavy rains. The main effort will focus on evacuating people from the danger zone first. The ministry also sent three teams to the affected areas.
