2: Continue to avoid taxing family farmland, help farmers expand production and find markets for agricultural products, allocate and provide land ownership to poor landless families under the conditions of social land concessions, continue to provide land to people who live and enjoy the location. State land in accordance with the principles, laws and procedures in force and continue to promote the prevention and enforcement of the law on all illegal encroachment on state land in all forms.
3. Continue to grant the right to occupy, enjoy and transfer the rights of stalls to vendors in the state market. Across the country and improve people's livelihoods by reducing the cost of water, electricity and stabilizing food prices in the market.
4: Continue to improve the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats and continue to develop all communes / sangkats to have adequate electricity and clean water, full telecommunication services, improve irrigation system and improve communication roads and build new roads. Maintain and convert from dirt roads to paved or concrete roads.
6: Continue to promote the provision of quality, safe, effective and equitable health care services to the people. Expand primary schools to all villages, expand secondary schools to all communes and increase high schools in districts so that young people have access to education, vocational training and employment. Mr. Tith Chantha led more than 3,000 members to march the closing campaign of the 7th National Assembly election in Tang Kork district
