(Phnom Penh): Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Winthean expressed confidence that the process of the 7th National Assembly election in 2023 will be smooth, fair and transparent and acceptable.
The Ambassador made this remark during a special guest visit to inspect the election campaign this morning, July 21, 2023, the last day with Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee. (NEC).
"I am honored to be a witness in the 7th National Assembly election," said Wang Winthean. And in the campaign, I see that every party that has run its campaign smoothly and is free, the people can freely express their position. "I believe this is a peaceful, transparent and fair election and all people can choose their party of their own free will."
The Chinese ambassador said that for the 7th parliamentary election in 2023, it has deployed 12 observers from the Chinese Communist Party, government and non-governmental organizations. Well.
It should be informed that this is the first time that the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, as a special guest, has personally observed the election campaign in Cambodia, as the previous mandate has never been like this.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), claimed that the election process in Cambodia from one mandate to another mandate is running smoothly and better.
On the occasion of inspecting the last day of the election campaign in Phnom Penh this morning, July 21, 2023, together with Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia as a special guest, Mr. Prach Chan affirmed that the process is more ongoing. Good because the political parties in Cambodia are more mature and respect each other.
Mr. Prach Chan said, "Each politics is more understanding, more experienced, more mature, respect each other, have a moral framework, so there is no problem to affect each other. "If we look at the better environment from one mandate to another, both the election campaigns of the political parties and the organization of the NEC are more experienced in accordance with the rules and regulations of the election."
During the last 20 days of the election campaign, all 18 political parties have been campaigning in their respective constituencies. In addition to the street parades, political parties often meet with the public and visit people's homes, handing out leaflets and performing arts to show each party's policies.
The NEC chairman also claimed that the overall atmosphere of the election campaign as of July 21 was good, security was good and order was maintained due to the cooperation between all election commissions. Classes with the competent authorities create good conditions for political parties to take turns to take action.
Regarding the complaints of political parties, Mr. Prach Chan said that the NEC also received about 30 complaints, most of which were online due to some social media campaigns violating the post-election special election law. Amendments to the election law. All of those complaints came from dissatisfied citizens and political parties.
At the same time, Mr. Prach Chan also confirmed the number of international observers who participated in the observation of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, more than 400 people from 60 institutions around the world, including the Prime Minister. Parliament and former high-ranking officials of all those countries as well.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. You Srey Leap was recently appointed by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as an Advisor to the Ministry of Interior with the rank of Director General. Mrs. You Srey Leap is the wife of Mr. Chit Ponnara.
Ms. You Srey Leap is a Cambodian woman who actively participates in humanitarian and social work to alleviate the hardships of the people, especially those in rural areas who have contributed to the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing poverty. .
As of June 2023, Ms. You Srey Leap has led a team of volunteer ophthalmologists to examine, treat, measure, give medicine and glasses to local people in Pursat province 7 times, 3 times in Veal Veng district, 1 time in Kandieng district. Phnom Kravanh district once and Krakor district twice, providing eye examinations and providing glasses to nearly 10,000 people free of charge.
In addition to Pursat province, Ms. You Srey Leap has led a team of volunteer ophthalmologists to examine, treat, measure, give medicine and provide glasses to local people in Battambang and Kandal provinces many times.
In addition, Ms. You Srey Leap once again gave hope and smiles to the nearly 200 elderly grandparents who have severe eye problems that can lead to blindness. She participated in leading a team of volunteer eye doctors. The mind underwent successful rescue surgery as well.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen warmly welcomed the invitation of the Speaker of the Malaysian Parliament, which provided a great honor and valuable presence in strengthening bilateral relations, as well as witnessed the democratic process of parliamentary elections. The seventh mandate is going well.
He recalled a trip in 2000 when he traveled to Kampong Cham province, where there were bumpy roads that he likened to a boat trip on the waves. He described reading many books on the history of Samdech and understood that the process of hard struggle, going through hardships, breaking up families to liberate the country from the Khmer Rouge regime and leading the country to progress to national unity. Leaders of ASEAN countries should practice and learn from.
On bilateral relations, Samdech Techo said that the bilateral relations between the two countries have undergone a series of exchanges, with progress in all fields, especially trade. "We have exchanged visits in the past, especially the visit of Malaysian Prime Minister Inwa Ibrahim to Cambodia in early 2023, further strengthening and expanding bilateral ties," he said.
The Prime Minister and Speaker of the National Assembly of Malaysia agreed to further strengthen and expand the ASEAN framework that we need to help each other, especially on climate change, food security and increase connectivity between the two countries. In the energy sector, renewable energy use and cooperation on food production, food supply in the region is stable.
He said that in the past, ASEAN seemed to look at the outside as its own, but the situation in the Kovid era encouraged the ASEAN countries to consider relations and exchanges to help each other in the ASEAN framework, especially in the field. ASEAN Star.
The President of the Malaysian Parliament wished Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the Cambodian People's Party success in the upcoming elections on July 23.
