The 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games make people more aware of the value of peace, as the saying goes, "Sports live in peace." Asia-Europe University International Relations Students Visit Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on the Occasion of the 65th Anniversary of Cambodia-China Diplomatic Relations
(Cambodia) - As Cambodia and China have agreed to designate 2023 as the Year of Cambodia-China Friendship, the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia celebrated the 65th anniversary of long-standing Cambodia-China diplomatic relations on Wednesday. July at the Chinese Embassy.
The Ambassador shared some important aspects of Cambodia-China relations, highlighting the strategic leadership, the historic official visit of the leaders of the two countries, as well as the development and support. Each other to achieve a better common community.
Wang added that the traditional ties between Cambodia and China, established and carefully maintained by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, Mao Zedong and Zhou Enlai, as well as previous Chinese leaders, are: A treasure that both peoples share.
The Ambassador also recalled the diamond cooperation between Cambodia and China, which prioritizes six key areas, including political cooperation, production capacity and quality, agriculture, energy, security and people-to-people exchanges. And the people of both countries.
"The fruitful relations between Cambodia and China have been remarkably achieved due to the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI). "Cambodia has benefited greatly from this initiative, which is reflected in the establishment of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and the Techo Heritage National Stadium." This was confirmed by Ambassador Wang Vinthean.
"On October 12, 2020, China and Cambodia formally signed the Free Trade Agreement (CCFTA) and the agreement officially entered into force on January 1, 2020," he said. 2022 ago. "The free trade agreement between Cambodia and China is a new milestone in the development of bilateral economic and trade relations, which will improve the well-being of private institutions and people of both countries."
Regarding the CCFTA agreement, the ambassador stressed that the Chinese side is currently promoting the export of coconuts to the Chinese market after Cambodia achieved the export of mangoes, bananas, lentils and other agricultural products to the Chinese market.
In addition to trade cooperation, the Ambassador also praised the progress of community-building development of a common future between Cambodia and China, saying, "Building a community of a common future for humanity is an important step to promote prosperity and development." Development. ”
Finally, Ambassador Wang Vinthean pledged to work with the Cambodian side to provide more scholarships to Cambodian students and encourage youth exchanges between the two countries.
The event ended with a variety of Chinese snack tasting sessions.
It should be noted that 2023 is the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between China and Cambodia and the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
