An Dara, President of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia, told Fresh News that the conference will be attended by more than 500 participants from 40 countries around the world, all of whom are workers and entrepreneurs in the cashew industry, such as processors, growers, leaders. Exports and sellers of cashew processing and packaging equipment.
He added that currently, the Cambodian Cashew Federation, together with the Ministry of Commerce, will cooperate with the delegates of the World Cashew Conference to organize this conference more smoothly.
He encouraged all cashew growers and cashew entrepreneurs in Cambodia to attend the conference, and the Cashew Federation will invite a number of international institutions, especially those that buy the most cashews in the world. He is from the United States, Europe, China, Japan, Korea, Australia and countries from the Middle East, as well as Vietnam, which is the largest exporter of cashew nuts.
By hosting the first World Cashew Conference in Cambodia, he expects Cambodia to receive more buyers of finished cashew products from those major countries.
He added that this is a good opportunity to attract investors in cashew processing as the government has shown great interest in the sector after the rice sector through the introduction of a national policy on cashew nuts and New investment law to boost the cashew sector, increase exports of processed products, which promotes the growth and sustainability of processing in Cambodia.
He said the conference was also an opportunity for communities and cashew growers to meet with the same growers, buyers and processors, making their products more marketable.
"According to the national policy on cashews, Cambodia will process 25% of cashews by 2027 and 50% by 2032," he said. "I think if after this conference we can get a big investment of about 20 to 30 standard companies, I think we will achieve this national policy on cashews."
Uon Silot, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh Nesws that the organization of the first World Cashew Conference in Cambodia shows that Cambodia has great potential and is one of the strongest countries in the cashew production that investors. Not to be overlooked.
"We sincerely hope that this conference will help attract more investors to focus on recycling in Cambodia, as well as showcase Cambodia's tourism potential to the world, and that we will give this opportunity to our members," he said. Of the conference to see the sea of cashews in three provinces may be Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Kampong Cham or Kratie. We will send him to see how the sea of cashews or the scope of Cambodia's cashews? ”
According to the Cambodian Cashew Federation, the World Cashew Conference, which takes place from February 1 to 3, 2024 in Siem Reap, will also feature Cambodian cashew products and processing equipment.
Please be informed that according to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association, the current area of cashew cultivation in Cambodia is more than 700,000 hectares. In 2021, the world production of raw cashew nuts was about 5 million tons, of which Cambodia produced 1,180,000 tons, accounting for 24% of total production, making Cambodia the largest producer of cashew nuts in the world. The world. In 2022, Cambodia produced 690,000 tons, second in the world.
