(France, Paris): Pho Phalla, currently living in Paris, France, has announced a major charity plan, he will launch a cycling campaign through eight European countries to raise money from philanthropists for Angkor Hospital for Children.
This large campaign will start from July 25 to September 3, 2023. He will ride through the city and through some European countries such as France, Switzerland, Luxembourg, Belgium, England, Italy, the Netherlands and Germany.
Pho Phalla, a native of Kampong Chhnang province, left for France in early 2022 with his wife, an official of the Embassy of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Paris. Pho Phalla said that under French law, the families of diplomats like him were not allowed to work full-time anywhere.
So every day he went to volunteer. Therefore, in his spare time, he always rides a bicycle for health, but while seeing the need for the Angkor Hospital for Children's Support Fund so that the hospital can continue its mission to help Cambodian children sustainably, he came up with the idea of riding beyond health to ride. Benefit this Cambodian child.
For this mission, he requested the cooperation of Angkor Hospital for Children directly. In addition, he also sent letters of notification to five Cambodian embassies in Europe seeking support for the mission. As a result, he said that some of the Cambodian embassies responded positively, that is, they supported and promised to continue to spread his mission to help expand the scope of news to raise funds to help Cambodian children through the above hospitals.
This is the first time for a charity ride, but the second time for an actual general campaign. In June and May, Pho Phalla also ran his own 4,000-kilometer cycling campaign. At that time, he rode to celebrate Cambodia hosting the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th Para Games.
For the first charity ride, Mr. Pho Phalla stated that he did not have any sponsors, but relied entirely on donations from philanthropists, including local Cambodians and part of the European Union, especially the eight countries. At the destination, he had to cross.
