(Phnom Penh): A free trade agreement is a mutual tax exemption agreement between one country and another on an agreed product. The FTA is not only a product tax exemption agreement, but covers many areas, including services, investment, trade facilitation, and the removal of non-tariff barriers.
Separately for the multilateral free trade agreement is the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) with 15 members.
At present, those free trade agreements are gradually benefiting Cambodia, which we can see with the eyes of export data to the markets of all those countries.
The RCEP Agreement entered into force on January 1, 2022. The agreement, which includes 15 ASEAN members and five free trade partners, including Australia, China, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand, was launched in 2012 in Phnom Penh.
The RCEP is the largest trade agreement in the world, with an estimated population of 2.2 billion, or 30 percent of the world's population, and 28 percent of world trade.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, for the whole of 2022, Cambodia's exports to RCEP member countries amounted to 6,344 million US dollars, an increase of 7%. For the first six months of 2023, Cambodia exported goods worth 4071 million US dollars, an increase of 24 percent compared to the same period in 2022, only 3281 million US dollars.
In the first six months of 2023, Cambodia's exports to China amounted to 713 million US dollars, an increase of 17 percent compared to the same period in 2022 only 612 million US dollars.
The CKFTA Agreement entered into force on December 1, 2022. The agreement has significantly contributed to boosting trade volume between the two countries. The government expects the agreement to further boost Cambodia's exports to Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
In the first six months of 2023, Cambodia's exports to South Korea amounted to 143 million US dollars, up 28 percent from 111 million US dollars in the same period in 2022.
* Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates (CEPA)
The CEPA agreement was signed on June 8, 2023. However, the agreement has not yet entered into force, pending the completion of each country's internal procedures.
