(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, on the morning of July 20, received 100 new books entitled "Legacy of the SEA Games and the first ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia in the Techo era".
Speaking at the book reception, Mr. Khieu Kanharith confirmed that this is an important document related to the history of sports in Cambodia and the region, and he commended the authors for the idea of compiling this event for the public.
The book's compiler, Chhay Sophal, said the book would be officially launched on Friday afternoon, July 21, but he handed it over to the Ministry of Information first today.
The nearly 600-page A4 book recalls the history of the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games from the very beginning, as well as the history of regional sports in Cambodia, why Cambodia failed to participate and did not organize for 64 years. Cambodia has left countries in the region as well as the world in awe.
Mr. Chhay Sophal continued that as we all know that Cambodia was able to organize these two great events because Cambodia is completely peaceful, able to keep safe athletes and foreign guests, as well as have enough infrastructure to serve. International sports competition, not losing to countries around the world, and good in many countries.
