A young man who was crippled for life in the violence in Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province in 2016 has not yet received $ 20,000 in court compensation while the perpetrator is in prison
(Phnom Penh): One of the victims in the incident of beating with sticks by two perpetrators in Po village, Kraing Svay commune, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province on December 23, 2016, caused serious head injuries and is now paralyzed. That and for life now has not yet received $ 20,000 in compensation as determined by the court through the Judgment No. 105/26 f dated June 20, 2018 by Trial Judge Ros Bophana .
According to Fresh News on July 20, 2023, the victim's family claimed that through the horrific incident in 2016, until now, the victim named San Pisal lives in Boeung Snong village, Lvea commune, Preah Sdach district. He was severely paralyzed by a head injury and was rushed to an emergency room in Vietnam.
However, after the incident, two perpetrators were arrested by the police under the command of the National Police General Commissioner, Yon Vanna and Long Lay, living in Po village, Kraing Svay commune, Preah Sdach district and sent to school. First, Prey Veng province for legal punishment.
Through a series of court proceedings, on June 20, 2023, the court sentenced the perpetrator to five years in prison and reimbursed the victim $ 20,000.
However, despite the court ruling, the families of the victims have not yet received a single riel from the perpetrators. The families of the victims have appealed to the judiciary to intervene legally so that the victims can receive the compensation set out in the verdict, while the widowed mother needs more money to continue. Treating a son who falls seriously ill.
