(Phnom Penh): Khmer Krom students have expressed the view that Khmer Krom who came to live in Cambodia should not oppose or hate the Royal Government is leading the country. Opposition to the Royal Government did not benefit the Khmer Krom and increased the pressure on living conditions.
Thach Vanna, a Khmer Krom child, was born in Khleang province and came to study in Cambodia in 2013. Thach Vanna is currently studying for a PhD in Political Science in Moscow, Russia.
Vanna came to Cambodia because she wanted to have the opportunity to study, especially to know about her home country. Arriving in Cambodia, Vanna became a priest to find study opportunities. After receiving a scholarship and studying in Russia for a year, Vanna left the seminary. For about 10 years, Vanna has overcome many difficulties in order to capture the knowledge that is her main goal in fleeing from the Khmer Krom to Cambodia.
Living in Cambodia for about 10 years, Vanna noted that the Khmer Krom who came to live in Cambodia were opposed to the Royal Government and often sympathetic to the opposition. According to Vannak, the Khmer Krom objected to the Royal Government because they saw that the Royal Government had good relations with the Vietnamese government, which was the guardian of the Khmer Krom today.
Thach Vanna did not want to see the Khmer Krom come to Cambodia against the Royal Government. Vanna gave the view to the Khmer Krom that no matter what the Royal Government from any political party must have a good relationship with the Royal Government to get a good environment for living as well as livelihood.
Vanna explained that only the Royal Government is in charge of the affairs of the state, so if there is poor communication, it is not beneficial for the Khmer Krom.
(Tbong Khmum): Ou Raing Ov district is a territory located in Tbong Khmum province with a total population of over 100,000 people. The district is also a highly agricultural land.
In the past 5 years, under the leadership of the Royal Government, the Cambodian People's Party in Orang Ov district has achieved many achievements to meet the daily needs of the people under the priority policy of "people, roads, water, electricity".
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and a member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, was appointed by the Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the Chairman of the Orang Ov District Assistance Team.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth not only contributed ideas and ideas to build and develop Orang Ov district. Mr. Sophalleth and his team also donated personal funds to help Orang Ov district under five priority areas: people, roads, water, electricity and social security work.
Based on these priority areas, Mr. Eang Sophalleth and his team always organize a program to distribute student materials during the school year to promote education and seek scholarships for students who have failed to dig water wells in schools. Launch a "smooth road" campaign to promote the construction of concrete roads and the clearing of dirt roads to facilitate travel.
In addition, Mr. Sophalleth and his team also installed sala lamps, which he called "angel fire" on the backs of people's houses.
Regarding security, Mr. Eang Sophalleth paid close attention to the fight against drug trafficking, which is a great disaster for the nation and its people. Therefore, Mr. Sophalleth launched an incentive program by giving one million Riels to the authorities who arrested a drug trafficker and donated $ 5,000 to Na Chhean commune to completely eliminate drug trafficking.
Born in Tbong Khmum province, Eang Sophalleth still has a strong desire to help the people and develop his homeland. To this end, Mr. Sophalleth appealed to nearly 60,000 Orang Ov residents on the voter list to go to the polls on July 23, 2023 and vote for the 18th Cambodian People's Party (CPP). Angels sprinkle flowers.
