Mr. Chea Chanto planted 400 saplings as a souvenir at Tang Krasang Santuk High School
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kampong Thom Province, planted 400 saplings as a souvenir at Tang Krasang Santuk High School in Kampong Thom Province.
Mr. Chea Chanto stated that forests are very important natural resources not only to sustain human life, animals, protect against climate change, reduce natural disasters, but also provide greenery, beautiful environment as a valuable heritage for Even the next generation.
Mr. Chea Chanto reminded the participants to plant trees together to create good memories to celebrate the 9th of July because the 9th of July was organized by the Royal Government. Up every year for the main purpose of actively contributing to the development and conservation of the forest sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto further stated that forests are very beneficial for human beings and animals and are classified as renewable resources because forests can come from non-drought sources or grow permanently or grow fast. In addition to providing excellent habitat for all kinds of animals, the forest also provides oxygen for them to breathe, helping to improve the atmosphere, stabilize the temperature and cause regular rainfall.
That is, forests help preserve the environment and reduce natural disasters such as hurricanes, floods and other droughts. At the same time, forests also help prevent soil erosion and maintain groundwater sustainability.
Mr. Chea Chanto called for more attention to be paid to planting trees to protect the forest and wildlife in order to increase the number of happy children and grandchildren, especially to plant trees in pagodas to become places. Monorom deserves to be a place of worship for Buddhists, and the participation in planting trees now also shows the solidarity and closer connection between the youth of the National Bank of Cambodia, the elder and the youth of Tang Krasang High School.
Not only on social media, on July 19, 2023, Mr. Sophalleth also brought a group of journalists from Phnom Penh to taste "Noodles, Orang Ov".
