(Phnom Penh): A group of Khmer Krom youth living and studying in Cambodia encouraged all Khmer Krom living in Cambodia to go to the polls on July 23 and called on the Khmer Krom in Cambodia The CPP-led government should not be considered an enemy.
But now some Khmer-Krom have changed their minds by turning to the CPP. The change is because they see that what they used to think and evaluate the CPP is not right.
Mr. Soeung Sotheany, President of the Khmer Kampuchea Krom Charitable Association, is a Khmer Krom born in Preah Trapeang province. Mr. Sotheany came to Cambodia to study in 2001. Mr. Sotheany now has a wife and children to support a strong family in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Soeung Sotheany in 2013 was also a supporter of the former CNRP with some Khmer Krom friends. But now Sotheany has a different view of the CPP.
Mr. Sotheany considered what he thought of the CPP in the past to be incomplete or obscure of the CPP leadership.
Now, this young Khmer-Krom has clearly seen the CPP-led policy on national sovereignty, without any satellite like before.
In addition to national sovereignty, Mr. Sotheany also highly valued the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, making Cambodian society prosperous and building a reputation on the international stage. What makes Mr. Sotheany even more satisfied with the CPP's leadership policy is its policy of building transportation infrastructure, especially the "Prek Chi Funan-Techo" project, which connects transportation from the river to the sea. Cambodia.
Mr. Sotheany was also interested in the CPP's policies for leading the country in the new term. In particular, practical action brings tangible results, not just word of mouth.
