Cambodia-China Friendship: Steps from Diamond Cooperation Towards a Common Destiny Community in a New Era
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-China friendship, which has a history of nearly two thousand years, has continuously evolved and deepened, no matter how times have changed or how globalization has changed.
The biggest turning point in the relationship between Cambodia and China was the establishment of diplomatic relations on July 19, 1958, which indicated the direction for the development of the two countries and the strengthening and expansion of friendship between the people of the two countries in accordance with Principles of equality, friendship, mutual respect and mutual benefit.
For the past 65 years, the people of both Cambodia and China have mourned and helped each other, deepening their friendship day by day. High political trust has become a solid foundation of the relationship between the two countries, which has never had any class conflicts or hostile actions.
