(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Chairman of Orang Ov District Local Strengthening Committee, urged the people of Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province to vote for the Cambodian People's Party on July 23 so that he has the opportunity to help further develop Ou Raing Ov district.
On the morning of Wednesday, July 19, 2023, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, together with the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Ou Raing Ov district, continued to campaign for the people's election. During the campaign, Mr. Eang Sophalleth and his team met with traders in O'Raing Ov Market and also visited people in Mean commune.
In that meeting, in addition to highlighting the achievements of the nation under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government from the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Eang Sophalleth also highlighted some achievements in the Orang Ov district, which the team participated. The construction for the people in the sixth mandate as well.
In terms of lighting, Mr. Eang Sophalleth has installed solar energy lamps, which he calls "angel lights", on the back streets of more than 20,000 houses. Mr. Sophalleth also cooperated with the authorities as well as local law enforcement forces to strengthen the policy of safe villages and communes.
Through these works, they have contributed to improving the lives of the people in Orang Ov district. During the meeting with business people as well as people this morning, Mr. Sophalleth asked people to vote for the Cambodian People's Party, the symbol of the flower angel No. 18 on the ballot for him and his team to contribute to the development. Achieve the development plan he planned.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth also showed how to mark the ballots correctly as instructed by the National Election Committee, without following any incitement that is detrimental to the democratic process in Cambodia.
New handover for local people in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham provincial administration plans to build more than 14 kilometers of rubber road connecting Arak Tnaot commune to Tuol Sambour commune
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, this morning, July 19, 2023, led a team to inspect the progress of roads in Stung Trang district.
According to Mr. Doul Sun, Technical Officer of Kampong Cham Provincial Investment Planning Office, the current Dey Krahorm road from Kilo 10 village in Arak Tnaot commune to Tuol Sambour commune in Stung Trang district is more than 14 kilometers long.
Mr. Doul Sun said that after the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda inspected the progress of the road, planned and sent experts to study to prepare the road development plan to become a DBST paved road. Therefore, the technical team and authorities of Arak Tnaot and Tuol Sambour communes are currently studying the road.
Mr. Duol Sun confirmed that the road is planned to be more than 14 kilometers long, 7 meters wide, rubber mats equal to the sidewalk 3 meters on both sides. But the construction date, he did not know yet.
