Serey Kosal Holds a Get-Together with 300 People in Yeang Udom Village and Calls for All to Vote
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Serey Kosal, Member of Parliament of Banteay Meanchey Province and Phnom Srok District Assistance Team on July 19, 2023, met with about 300 people in Yeang Udom Village and members from various parties. 48 people, including members of the Candlelight Party and the National Unity Party.
On that occasion, Mr. Serey Kosal reiterated the duty of the Cambodian people to go to the polls without believing the unfortunate words of the opposition, especially this election is a big election to elect a new government.
At the same time, Mr. Serey Kosal also instructed the people to go to the polls in large numbers by voting for the Cambodian People's Party, as well as to show solidarity to maintain peace and national development.
At the same time, Mr. Serey Kosal continued to call on the people to understand the tactics of Mr. Sam Rainsy's unscrupulous politicians not to participate in the election of the Candlelight Party and explain the reasons for the non-participation of this party to the people. .
On that occasion, Mr. Serey Kosal brought a visit from Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who always took care of the well-being of the people, maintaining peace, political stability until now.
Mr. Serey Kosal stated that after the liberation on January 7, 1979, the whole of Cambodia was liberated from the black-shirt regime and the whole people were resurrected. Citizens are being restored and established everywhere in the country.
Mr. Serey Kosal also called on the people to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia in the seventh term and support Dr. Hun Manet as the next prime ministerial candidate.
The ceremony ended with a happy meal and a meal of noodles and ice cream together to show solidarity and friendship.
