According to the report of the Svay Rieng Provincial Police, the Svay Rieng Provincial Police would like to confirm the following: On July 18, 2023 at 3:30 pm, people reported to the authorities that they saw staff Paris East Casino Company smashed the glass of the 6th floor building at the back and shouted for intervention.
Immediately after receiving the above information, and with the coordination of the prosecutor's office, the relevant authorities and authorities went to the scene and found a total of 35 employees of the Vietnamese casino company, 10 women, gathered not working in the building. The 6th floor will also see damage to equipment, tables, chairs and computers of some companies.
Authorities summoned the 35 Vietnamese nationals to the Bavet City Police Inspectorate for questioning. After the initial interrogation of the 35 employees, they told the police that they were protesting for intervention related to certain working conditions.
