(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Dangkor district together with the working group on the morning of July 18, 2023. Bring Preah Vossa candles, as well as various budgets and relics to the monks who remember Preah Vossa at two pagodas, Wat Prek Thleung and Wat Keo Mony in Sangkat Prek Kampus, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
The rainy season, which lasts about three months, is a time when monks find it difficult to perform Ben Bath because it is the rainy season. Due to this reason, the Cambodian Buddhists always have a ceremony to offer Preah Vesa candles for lighting in the temple, as well as to offer various gifts for the monks to eat during the rainy season, which is difficult to perform Ben Bath.
The offering of Preah Vossa candles with many gifts is given to the monks now to respect the Buddhist tradition of the Buddha and to alleviate the difficulties of the monks during the rainy season. Quarter at the pagoda, during which time the monks could not go to Ben Bath because of the rainy season, the Buddhists were busy farming their respective fields.
