The book "Samdech Heng Samrin in the field of parliamentary diplomacy" published shows one of the achievements of the National Assembly
(Phnom Penh): The book entitled "Samdech Heng Samrin in the field of parliamentary diplomacy" was released to the public in July 2023. This book describes the achievements of the National Assembly under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, especially the success in the field of parliamentary diplomacy.
Parliamentary diplomacy is one of the tasks of the National Assembly on the international stage, among the many tasks of the National Assembly in serving the nation and its people, such as drafting laws, representing the people, and monitoring the implementation of the law.
Samdech Heng Samrin's book on parliamentary diplomacy states that in general, diplomatic work is perceived as the work of the executive branch, which is carried out through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the head of diplomacy in each country. But in the last decade, the legislature, which has a central role to play in representing the nation and the people as a whole, has been actively involved in international cooperation activities in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
Mr. Keo Piseth, Director of the Office of the President of the National Assembly, stated in the book that although not all of the activities of the President of the National Assembly in leading the National Assembly for more than three terms, but this book shows some parts of Samdech's noble mission in promoting the honor of the National Assembly of Cambodia as well as the nation as a whole on the international stage.
Samdech Heng Samrin's book on parliamentary diplomacy is nearly 300 pages long and is divided into five major chapters. In addition to focusing on parliamentary diplomacy, the book also highlights the history and achievements of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and many other people from the beginning.
Please be informed that under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia has been actively involved in promoting and promoting the diplomatic sector of the National Assembly in order to promote and promote dialogue, cooperation and sustainable development in Cambodia. On the international stage. KOICA is committed to expanding the professional development of technology communication systems in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) is committed to expanding cooperation with Cambodia on building professional skills in the field of technology communication systems for Cambodian youth and bringing the experience of professional development in their country to train the Cambodian people. .
The Minister stated that the project to build capacity and create an environment in ICT skills of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) in Cambodia is very important to contribute to the development of TVET in Cambodia, especially to support the vocational training plan. Livelihoods for 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country, which the Royal Government of Cambodia will start by the end of 2023.
He stressed that the Government of the Republic of Korea considers Cambodia to be the second most important country in the region in helping to develop TVET skills and is also committed to bringing its national skills training experience to help train the Cambodian people. Develop people's livelihood, develop the national economy as well.
It should be noted that the project to build capacity and create an environment in ICT skills of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) in Cambodia for 5 years from 2023-2027, which aims to contribute to improving the quality of TVET through Improve the curriculum and training environment and strengthen the capacity of technical teachers in the field of ICT.
