According to the Minister, the Ministry plans to build about 1,000 antenna towers in Phnom Penh and thousands more in all provinces in Cambodia.
He said that in the first six months of 2023, the Ministry has built about 200 antenna towers, or more than 20%, taking more than a year and a half to complete.
He pointed out that the construction of the tower in Phnom Penh has been delayed due to some challenges.
He added that in the provinces, the Ministry is currently testing and studying to build antenna towers in all provinces, each of which needs at least 100 to more than 200 poles. Construction in the provinces may be easy to build quickly, not as difficult as in Phnom Penh.
He said that apart from the construction of antenna towers in Borey in Phnom Penh, the Ministry has set up eight working groups to work on this work in each Borey.
According to Mr. Chea Vandeth, there are currently more than 100 Boreys in Phnom Penh, but of these, the Ministry has identified 68 Boreys with a large population to build 88 poles, starting from Borey Peng Huoth.
He said that in a year, the Ministry has worked to build about 70 poles in the Borey, and the remaining 18 poles have not been built because some people do not allow the construction because they understand that the antenna poles affect To health.
