A journalist who used the names of big news organizations to ask for money from officials in ministries and institutions was arrested by the authorities
(Phnom Penh): A journalist who used to impersonate and use the names of major news organizations, including Fresh News Unit, to go to Chhat to ask for money from officials in various ministries and institutions was arrested by the Anti-Technology Crime Department of the National Police. Arrest warrant issued by Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
An official from the Anti-Technology Crime Department told Fresh News on the afternoon of July 19, 2023 that the suspect who was arrested by the police, 30-year-old Moul Rattanak, was the editor-in-chief of Senathipady newspaper in Trapeang Cheung village, Kraing district. Thnong, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he had acted fraudulently and used the names of major media institutions to solicit money from officials in these ministries since 2021. In case the officer does not give the money as requested, he threatens to publish inactive stories.
The suspects are currently being investigated by the Anti-Technology Crime Department.
