(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that the 2023 general election will not only be a contest for parliamentary seats between the 18 registered parties, but also a contest between parties. 18 with extremists who want to ruin the election even more.
On the morning of July 19, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said on Twitter: "In the 2023 general election, in addition to the competition between 18 political parties registered to compete for seats in the National Assembly. "We still have competition between the 18 parties participating in the election and the extremists who want to ruin the election."
"Extremists ordered by prisoners to flee from prisons to a political party in the country have found every way to undermine the democratic process by trying to disrupt elections, such as campaigning against the people," he said. Vote and destroy ballots, etc. On July 23, 2023, will the democratic forces participating in the election be more or less than the forces destroying democracy, destroying the elections? "Let's wait and see."
According to the new Article 142 of the Law on the Amendment of the Election Law, which came into force on July 4, 2023, inciting, harassing or preventing people from going to the polls or destroying ballots is a crime. This offense is fined from 5 million to 20 million riels, regardless of other criminal penalties.
