(Phnom Penh): The National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes through the Telegram System on Suspicion of Illegal Logging at Mang Yang K Rubber Development Company in Vern Sai District, Ratanakkiri Province.
Brigadier General Eng Hy, spokesman for the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes, said on July 19, 2023, immediately after receiving the information, Brigadier General Sao Sokha, Chairman of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Crimes. Natural resources send this information to the provincial level for direct inspection if the crime is actually cracked down on.
After receiving information from the national level, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province and a member of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes, confirmed that the trees published by the media were of the district mango trees that people planted in Vern Hoy village, Hat Pak commune, Vern Sai district, and people cut down 17 pieces from 0.50 meters to 1.20 meters in length and 4.20 meters in total.
Brigadier General Eng Hee confirmed that the above trees are a kind of fruit crops that people grow themselves, not under the forest law. The competent authority advises the buyer to apply for a transport permit from the specialized authority according to the procedure.
Based on the report of the Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes, please note that the above case is not a violation of the forest law.
