Royal Government: The salaries of all types of civil servants and members of the armed forces will be increased and continue to increase in 2024 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The hardships of civil servants, teachers, doctors and all types of armed forces, including retirement People are the concern of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In particular, to facilitate the spending of civil servants, teachers, doctors and the armed forces of all kinds, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to pay salaries every two weeks (twice a month). In addition, in addition to the salary increase, there is also an additional support of 50,000 Riels twice a year, the occasion of Pchum Ben and the traditional New Year. Each time the government pays more than 7 million dollars for this support.
In 2021 and 2022, the crisis of the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has to save money to help the poor and fight against Kovid 19 by failing to increase the salaries of civil servants, teachers, doctors and Armed forces of all kinds for two consecutive years.
For 2023, the Royal Government has started to increase the salaries of civil servants, teachers, doctors and the armed forces of all kinds, with the lowest salary of 1.3 million riels.
By 2023, the Royal Government plans to budget more than 9,555 billion riels or about 2,295 million US dollars to pay for civil servants in 2023 to increase the salaries of civil servants, doctors, teachers, armed forces officers. Minimum more than 1.1 million riels to more than 1.3 million riels, while contracted officials up to 710,000 riels to support the livelihood of civil servants.
From January 2023, the minimum salary of civil servants has been increased:
Meanwhile, the Royal Government has allocated 50 billion Riels for the health care fund for all civil servants, the Armed Forces and retirees and has continued to budget 6 billion Riels to support the social security system for occupational risk for public officials in In the budget of the Ministry of Health.
Separately, allowances for sub-national administration officials also increased as follows:
As for the cash transfer program for poor women, pregnant women and young children, the state has set a budget of 40,000 riels for four antenatal check-ups, 200,000 riels for each delivery at a health center or hospital. At the same time, the state also supports 10 more times when going to get vaccinated up to 2 years old children, with 40,000 riels per time. But this program will be doubled from August 2023 onwards.
From August 1, 2023 onwards, the Royal Government will increase the new allowance for female workers to receive 80,000 Riels at a time for 4 prenatal and 4 postnatal check-ups. 10 times for 2-year-old children and 800,000 Riel for one birth and an additional 400,000 Riel for the second and third twins and so on.
Urge to increase the salaries of civil servants, teachers, doctors and all kinds of armed forces in 2024, the Royal Government will continue to increase salaries.
