This statement was made by Mr. Desi Renia Rohirira during a working meeting between him and Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC on Tuesday morning, July 18, 2023 at the Office of the National Election Committee on the occasion of his leadership. The delegation came to observe the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 to pay a courtesy call and discuss the election work.
Desire Renia Rohirira said the OIF delegation's current mission is to meet with election officials, political parties and NGOs. At the end of the mission, the OIF delegation will issue a report on the election, including recommendations and shortcomings for the Cambodian side to supplement. Now the OIF delegation wants to know about the election process.
The NEC has held 16 regular, universal and non-universal self-elections, including general elections, parliamentary elections, commune council elections, and non-general elections. Senators and Elections Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council.
Mr. Prach Chan further informed that in 2015, the organization of the election has been deeply reformed, the election institution is stated in the Constitution, there is a law on the organization and functioning of the NEC, the law on Election of MPs, amendment of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election, etc. The NEC has prepared the rules and procedures for the election, the master plan and the election calendar for all parties to follow.
Regarding voter registration, Mr. Prach Chan informed that before the voter registration was done manually, now the NEC examines the voter list and voter registration using a computer system and many other programs are Made by computer system, such as registration of political parties, candidates and the list of candidates and management of election results, etc.
Mr. Prach Chan answered the questions of the delegation and added that so far, the NEC is ready for the election to be held on Sunday, July 23, 2023, both material and defense forces. Security, safety, public order for the election to be successful.
Once again, the OIF delegation also thanked the Chairman of the NEC for providing detailed information to the delegation, while the OIF delegation can assist in the training of election officials if requested. .
