(Siem Reap): A senior official of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation confirmed that Siem Reap Angkor International Airport will be opened on October 16, 2023 to receive passengers to this cultural province.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for Civil Aviation, said that the opening of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport coincided with the continuous increase in air passengers.
The confirmation of this senior official was made on the occasion of leading the Cambodian Tourism Association to visit Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) on July 17, 2023.
At the beginning of July 2023, the average national and international passenger and cargo flights operated 850 flights a week, departing and entering the three international airports, and there were 26 national and international airlines connecting flights. Re-flights with nine ASEAN countries, China, South Korea, Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, Taiwan and Qatar.
According to the senior civil aviation official, the construction process of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) has achieved good results as planned, which has so far completed more than 98%.
