Senior Minister Ly Thuch made this statement at a press conference on the morning of July 18, 2023. The demining team found millions of ammunition, including more than 1,175,000 anti-personnel mines, more than 26,222 anti-tank mines and 3,070 unexploded ordnance. 526 goals. It is this mine that has killed and maimed more than 65,000 people.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that for more than 30 years, Cambodia has been very successful in clearing landmines on more than 2,794 square kilometers, which is the largest land in the world compared to more than 30 countries. There are the same mines.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that a total of more than 4 million landmines and other explosives had been found and had been completely destroyed on Cambodian soil, and that it could no longer cause problems for the people. The cleared land has been handed over to farmers for more than 2,794 meters of land, which is safe for a long time.
The senior minister confirmed that the results of demining from 1992 to June 2023 under the assistance of Australia, Japan, the United States, Britain, Germany, Switzerland, Norway, China, Ireland, New Zealand, the Republic of Korea, Hungary, India, Canada, the United Nations, the EU, Spain, Sweden, Austria, Belgium. France, the Netherlands, Hungary and Denmark, as well as civil society organizations, the private sector and philanthropists.
However, Mr. Ly Thuch also said that the plan to clear mines in 2024-2025, covering an area of 358 square kilometers, requires a budget of $ 78 million. The mine-affected area does not include new minefields that national and international operators continue to discover, sending them to the Mine Authority for inspection and evaluation.
It should be noted that in terms of demining work, according to the report of the Mines Authority, deminers were involved in demining operations, including the loss of life, disability and a total of 155 people, including 31 lives.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has previously announced that in 2025, Cambodia will be landmine-free, provide land safely and with a smile, Samdech appealed to philanthropists to continue to support as much as possible in demining work.
